(1, 'logic', 'Which season comes right before autumn?', '["Winter", "Spring", "Summer", "Autumn"]', 2, 'The order is spring, summer, autumn, winter. Summer is just before autumn.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which month of the year has the fewest days?', '["April", "February", "June", "December"]', 1, 'February has 28 days most years, fewer than any other month.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these usually happens first in a day?', '["Lunch", "Dinner", "Bedtime", "Breakfast"]', 3, 'Breakfast is the first meal, then lunch, then dinner, then bedtime.'),
(1, 'logic', 'It is 3 o''clock. What time will it be in 2 hours?', '["5 o''clock", "4 o''clock", "6 o''clock", "1 o''clock"]', 0, '3 + 2 = 5, so it will be 5 o''clock.'),
(1, 'logic', 'School starts at 9 o''clock. Emi arrives 1 hour early. What time does she arrive?', '["10 o''clock", "8 o''clock", "7 o''clock", "9 o''clock"]', 1, 'One hour before 9 is 8, so she arrives at 8 o''clock.'),
(1, 'logic', 'A movie starts at 4 o''clock and lasts 2 hours. When does it end?', '["6 o''clock", "5 o''clock", "7 o''clock", "2 o''clock"]', 0, '4 + 2 = 6, so the movie ends at 6 o''clock.'),
(1, 'logic', 'An hour has 60 minutes. How many minutes are in half an hour?', '["15", "45", "20", "30"]', 3, 'Half of 60 is 30.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Nora''s bedtime is 8 o''clock. Tonight she goes to bed 1 hour early. What time does she go to bed?', '["9 o''clock", "6 o''clock", "7 o''clock", "8 o''clock"]', 2, 'One hour earlier than 8 is 7.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which comes first in a butterfly''s life?', '["Caterpillar", "Egg", "Chrysalis", "Butterfly"]', 1, 'A butterfly starts as an egg, then a caterpillar, then a chrysalis, then a butterfly.'),
(1, 'logic', 'When you get dressed, which must go on first?', '["Socks before shoes", "Shoes before socks", "Both at once", "Shoes on your hands"]', 0, 'Socks go on your feet first, and then shoes go over them.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which is the longest time?', '["1 day", "1 hour", "1 week", "1 minute"]', 2, 'A week is 7 days, which is longer than a day, an hour or a minute.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which is the shortest time?', '["1 hour", "1 day", "1 month", "1 minute"]', 3, 'A minute is 60 seconds, much shorter than an hour, a day or a month.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Two months after January is which month?', '["March", "February", "April", "December"]', 0, 'January, February, March. Two months later is March.'),
(1, 'logic', 'The 9th of the month is a Tuesday. What day is the 10th?', '["Monday", "Thursday", "Wednesday", "Tuesday"]', 2, 'The day after Tuesday is Wednesday.'),
(1, 'logic', 'If a light switch is off, the room is dark. The switch is off. What is the room like?', '["Bright", "Dark", "Warm", "Noisy"]', 1, 'The rule says off means dark, so the room is dark.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Whenever the school bell rings, class ends. The bell just rang. What happens?', '["Class starts", "Lunch is cancelled", "Nothing", "Class ends"]', 3, 'The rule says the bell means class ends.'),
(1, 'logic', 'If it is snowing, Yuki wears boots. Today Yuki is wearing sandals. Is it snowing?', '["Yes", "No", "Only at night", "Cannot tell"]', 1, 'If it were snowing she would wear boots. She wears sandals, so it is not snowing.'),
(1, 'logic', 'If the oven is hot, Dad wears mitts. Dad is wearing mitts. Is the oven definitely hot?', '["Cannot tell", "Yes, definitely", "No, definitely not", "Only on Sunday"]', 0, 'The rule only says a hot oven means mitts. Dad could wear mitts for other reasons.'),
