(1, 'logic', 'Zara says she has exactly 3 apples in her bag. She really has 2 apples. Is Zara''s statement true?', '["Yes, it is true", "Yes, because 2 is close", "No, it is false", "Only on Mondays"]', 2, 'She said 3 but has 2, so what she said is not true.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Two kids each say, "I am taller than you." Can both kids be right?', '["Yes", "Only if they are twins", "Only in the morning", "No"]', 3, 'If one kid is taller, the other cannot also be taller.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Leo says, "Today is Monday and tomorrow is Tuesday." Today really is Monday. Is what Leo said true?', '["Yes", "No", "Only in winter", "Cannot tell"]', 0, 'Today is Monday and the day after Monday is Tuesday, so both parts are true.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which statement is true about every triangle?', '["It has 4 corners", "It has no corners", "It has 3 sides", "It has 5 sides"]', 2, 'A triangle always has 3 sides and 3 corners.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which statement about time is true?', '["A day has 30 hours", "An hour has 100 minutes", "A week has 10 days", "A year has 12 months"]', 3, 'There are 12 months in a year.'),
