(1, 'logic', 'Rosa is 8 years old, Lee is 10 and Abe is 9. Who is the middle age of the three?', '["Abe", "Rosa", "Lee", "Cannot tell"]', 0, 'The ages in order are 8, 9, 10, so Abe at 9 is in the middle.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Tower A has 5 blocks, Tower B has 7 blocks and Tower C has 6 blocks. Which tower is the second tallest?', '["Tower A", "Tower C", "Tower B", "Cannot tell"]', 1, 'From tallest to shortest: B with 7, C with 6, A with 5. So C is second.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Team Red scored 7 goals and Team Blue scored 7 goals. Which team scored more?', '["Team Red", "Team Blue", "Neither, they tied", "Cannot tell"]', 2, '7 and 7 are the same amount, so it is a tie.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which number is closer to 10: 8 or 15?', '["15", "8", "They are the same", "Cannot tell"]', 1, '8 is 2 away from 10, while 15 is 5 away.'),
(1, 'logic', 'The ground outside is wet, there are puddles and the sky is gray. What most likely happened?', '["It rained", "It was very sunny", "There was a heat wave", "Nothing happened"]', 0, 'Puddles and wet ground with gray skies are signs of rain.'),
(1, 'logic', 'What happens to ice cream if you leave it in the hot sun?', '["It freezes harder", "It grows bigger", "It turns to stone", "It melts"]', 3, 'Heat makes ice cream soft and runny.'),
(1, 'logic', 'What will happen to a plant that gets no water for a very long time?', '["It will grow taller", "It will turn into a tree", "It will wilt and dry out", "Nothing at all"]', 2, 'Plants need water to stay healthy.'),
(1, 'logic', 'You give a ball a push on a flat floor. What does it do?', '["It rolls", "It sticks to the floor", "It disappears", "It melts"]', 0, 'A round ball rolls when pushed.'),
(1, 'logic', 'The sink plug is in and the tap is on. What will happen to the sink after a while?', '["It will stay empty", "It will fill with water", "It will freeze", "It will float away"]', 1, 'The water cannot drain, so it builds up.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Why do people wear warm coats in winter?', '["To feel hotter in summer", "To be louder", "To run faster", "To stay warm"]', 3, 'Coats keep body heat in when it is cold.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Why do people open umbrellas when it rains?', '["To stay dry", "To stay warm", "To see farther", "To be taller"]', 0, 'An umbrella blocks the raindrops.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Leo went to bed very late and got up early. How will he most likely feel?', '["Full of energy", "Tired", "Very tall", "Ready to fly"]', 1, 'Not getting enough sleep makes you feel tired.'),
(1, 'logic', 'You flip a light switch to ON. What happens to the light bulb?', '["It goes dark", "It melts", "It shrinks", "It lights up"]', 3, 'Turning the switch on lets electricity flow, so the bulb glows.'),
(1, 'logic', 'A puddle sits outside all day in hot sun. What happens to it?', '["It gets bigger", "It turns into ice", "It dries up", "It turns into milk"]', 2, 'The heat makes the water go into the air.'),
(1, 'logic', 'What should you do before you cross a road?', '["Close your eyes", "Look both ways", "Run as fast as you can", "Sing loudly"]', 1, 'Looking both ways lets you check for cars first.'),
(1, 'logic', 'You leave a cup of water in the freezer overnight. What is it in the morning?', '["Steam", "Milk", "Juice", "Ice"]', 3, 'Water freezes into ice when it gets very cold.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these birds cannot fly: Eagle, Penguin, Owl, Sparrow?', '["Eagle", "Owl", "Penguin", "Sparrow"]', 2, 'Penguins have wings that work like flippers for swimming, not flying.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these floats on water?', '["A wooden boat", "A stone", "A coin", "A key"]', 0, 'Wood is light for its size, so it floats. The other things sink.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these can you see through?', '["A brick wall", "Window glass", "A wooden door", "A metal box"]', 1, 'Glass is clear, so light passes through it.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these is alive?', '["A tree", "A rock", "A chair", "A cup"]', 0, 'A tree grows, drinks water and makes seeds, so it is alive.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these needs electricity to work?', '["A book", "A spoon", "A television", "A ball"]', 2, 'A television must be powered by electricity.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these would melt in the sun?', '["A stone", "A wooden log", "A steel spoon", "An ice cube"]', 3, 'Ice melts into water when it gets warm.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these will bounce the best?', '["A brick", "A pillow", "A stone", "A rubber ball"]', 3, 'Rubber springs back when it hits the ground.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these animals can live both in water and on land?', '["A frog", "A cow", "A goldfish", "An eagle"]', 0, 'Frogs start life in water and later live on land and in water.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these keeps you dry in the rain?', '["A net", "An umbrella", "A sponge", "A sieve"]', 1, 'An umbrella blocks the raindrops. The others let the water through.'),
(1, 'logic', 'You use your ___ to smell flowers.', '["Ears", "Elbow", "Nose", "Knee"]', 2, 'Your nose is the part of your body that smells.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these gives out light?', '["A rock", "A candle", "A sock", "A cup"]', 1, 'A lit candle glows and lights up the room.'),
(1, 'logic', 'Which of these can you drink?', '["Sand", "Paint", "Soap", "Milk"]', 3, 'Milk is a drink. The others are not for drinking.');
insert into questions (level, category, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanation) values
(1, 'riddle', 'I say moo, I eat grass, and I give you milk. What am I?', '["A pig", "A duck", "A horse", "A cow"]', 3, 'A cow says moo and gives us milk. Horses, pigs and ducks do not give milk for us to drink.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have eight legs and spin a sticky web to catch my food. What am I?', '["A beetle", "A spider", "A bee", "An ant"]', 1, 'A spider has eight legs and spins webs. Ants, beetles and bees only have six legs.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a long, green reptile with big teeth and a strong tail, and I live in rivers and swamps. What am I?', '["A crocodile", "A rabbit", "A penguin", "A frog"]', 0, 'A crocodile is a large reptile with big teeth and a strong tail that lives near water.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a reptile with a hard shell, and I can pull my head inside it when I feel scared. What am I?', '["A crocodile", "A lizard", "A turtle", "A snake"]', 2, 'A turtle can tuck its head into its hard shell to feel safe.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I look like a horse wearing black-and-white striped pajamas. What am I?', '["A zebra", "A panda", "A cow", "A tiger"]', 0, 'A zebra is shaped like a horse and has black and white stripes all over.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'My fluffy coat gets cut off in spring to make warm sweaters. What am I?', '["A cow", "A sheep", "A pig", "A horse"]', 1, 'A sheep grows thick wool, which people shear off and turn into sweaters.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I live in the ocean, I have eight arms, and I squirt dark ink to escape danger. What am I?', '["A crab", "A fish", "An octopus", "A dolphin"]', 2, 'An octopus has eight arms and can squirt ink to hide from enemies.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am round and flat, covered in sauce and cheese, and I am cut into triangle slices. What am I?', '["A pancake", "A cookie", "A sandwich", "Pizza"]', 3, 'Pizza is a round, flat food with sauce and cheese that is cut into slices.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am cold and sweet, and I come in scoops on a cone. What am I?', '["A sandwich", "Soup", "A pancake", "Ice cream"]', 3, 'Ice cream is a frozen, sweet treat that is often served in scoops on a cone.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am big and round with a green outside and red, juicy insides full of black seeds. What am I?', '["A pumpkin", "A watermelon", "An orange", "A tomato"]', 1, 'A watermelon has green skin and sweet red fruit inside with seeds.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a small red fruit with tiny seeds on my outside, and I am often eaten with cream. What am I?', '["A cherry", "A tomato", "A strawberry", "An apple"]', 2, 'A strawberry is red and has tiny seeds all over the outside of the fruit.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a hot, wet meal that you eat with a spoon, often made with chicken and noodles. What am I?', '["Soup", "A sandwich", "Pizza", "A cookie"]', 0, 'Soup is a warm liquid meal, and you eat it with a spoon.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a brown, oval vegetable that grows underground, and I can be mashed, baked or made into fries. What am I?', '["An apple", "A potato", "A pumpkin", "A carrot"]', 1, 'A potato grows underground and can be mashed, baked or fried.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have bristles and a handle, and you use me to untangle your hair. What am I?', '["A hairbrush", "A toothbrush", "A spoon", "A cup"]', 0, 'A hairbrush smooths and untangles your hair. A toothbrush is only for teeth.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a handle, and you sip your milk or hot chocolate from me. What am I?', '["A pillow", "A plate", "A cup", "A fork"]', 2, 'A cup holds a drink so you can sip it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I heat water for tea, and I whistle when the water boils. What am I?', '["A cup", "A bathtub", "A bucket", "A kettle"]', 3, 'A kettle heats water on the stove, and many of them whistle when it is hot.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I hang across a window, and you can pull me closed to keep the sunlight out. What am I?', '["A pillow", "A plate", "A curtain", "A carpet"]', 2, 'A curtain hangs at the window and slides shut to block light.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have four legs and a back, and you sit on me at the dinner table. What am I?', '["A shelf", "A chair", "A bed", "A lamp"]', 1, 'A chair has a back and legs and is made for sitting.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I come in a tube, I taste minty, and you squeeze me onto your toothbrush. What am I?', '["Toothpaste", "Ketchup", "Butter", "Glue"]', 0, 'Toothpaste is a minty paste that helps clean your teeth. You would not brush with glue, ketchup or butter.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I sit in the middle of your face and help you smell flowers and fresh cookies. What am I?', '["Your ear", "Your chin", "Your knee", "Your nose"]', 3, 'You smell things with your nose.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the joint in the middle of your leg that bends when you kneel, and I might get scraped when you fall. What am I?', '["Your wrist", "Your ear", "Your knee", "Your chin"]', 2, 'The knee is the joint in the middle of your leg, and it bends when you kneel.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I cover your whole body like a coat, and I keep your insides safely in. What am I?', '["Your bones", "Your skin", "Your heart", "Your hair"]', 1, 'Skin wraps around your whole body and protects it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'There are ten of us at the ends of your feet, and we wiggle inside your socks. What are we?', '["Your knees", "Your ears", "Your fingers", "Your toes"]', 3, 'Toes are the small parts at the front of your feet.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a little dent in the middle of your tummy, left over from when you were a baby. What am I?', '["Your belly button", "Your knee", "Your ear", "Your chin"]', 0, 'Everyone has a belly button in the middle of their tummy.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am huge, blue and salty, and I have waves, whales and fish. What am I?', '["A puddle", "The ocean", "A bathtub", "A lake"]', 1, 'The ocean is enormous, salty and full of sea creatures.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a hot, dry place with lots of sand and very little rain, and camels can live in me. What am I?', '["A desert", "A forest", "A lake", "The ocean"]', 0, 'A desert is very dry and sandy with hardly any rain.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a tiny, six-pointed piece of ice that floats down in winter, and no two of me look exactly alike. What am I?', '["A feather", "A pebble", "A snowflake", "A raindrop"]', 2, 'Snowflakes are tiny ice crystals that fall in winter, and each one has its own pattern.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a long, pointy spike of ice that hangs from a roof in winter. What am I?', '["A ladder", "A chimney", "A snowman", "An icicle"]', 3, 'An icicle forms when dripping water freezes into a pointy spike.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a small, smooth stone that you can skip across a pond. What am I?', '["A boulder", "A mountain", "A puddle", "A pebble"]', 3, 'A pebble is a little smooth stone, small enough to throw and skip across water.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a table in the classroom with a lid or drawer, and you sit at me to do your work. What am I?', '["A desk", "A slide", "A globe", "A bed"]', 0, 'A desk is where you sit and write or read in a classroom.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have buttons with numbers on them, and I can add and multiply very fast. What am I?', '["A mirror", "A piano", "A calculator", "A clock"]', 2, 'A calculator does math for you when you press its number buttons.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a cap and a felt tip, and I draw bold, bright lines that make a mess if I am left uncapped. What am I?', '["A backpack", "A marker", "A desk", "An eraser"]', 1, 'A marker has a felt tip and a cap that stops the ink from drying out.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have two wheels, two pedals and handlebars, and you ride me by pushing with your feet. What am I?', '["A bicycle", "A bus", "A train", "A tractor"]', 0, 'A bicycle has two wheels and pedals that you push to make it go.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have spinning blades on top, and I can hover in one spot in the air. What am I?', '["A bus", "A boat", "A helicopter", "An airplane"]', 2, 'A helicopter''s spinning blades lift it and let it hover, which an airplane cannot do.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have flashing lights and a loud siren, and I rush hurt or sick people to the hospital. What am I?', '["A bicycle", "A tractor", "A school bus", "An ambulance"]', 3, 'An ambulance hurries patients to the hospital with lights and a siren.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a narrow boat that you paddle while sitting low near the water. What am I?', '["A tractor", "A canoe", "A train", "A bicycle"]', 1, 'A canoe is a small, narrow boat moved along with a paddle.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I keep your hands warm in the snow, but I have no separate fingers, only a place for your thumb. What am I?', '["A hat", "A glove", "Mittens", "A sock"]', 2, 'Mittens keep all four fingers together in one pocket. Gloves have a separate spot for each finger.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have tiny teeth that lock together, and when you pull my tab, your jacket opens or closes. What am I?', '["A zipper", "A belt", "A button", "A comb"]', 0, 'A zipper''s little teeth lock together as the tab slides along.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I tie around your waist in the kitchen and keep your clothes clean from flour and sauce. What am I?', '["A helmet", "An apron", "A scarf", "A belt"]', 1, 'An apron protects your clothes when you cook.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am hard and go on your head to protect it when you ride a bike. What am I?', '["A sock", "A scarf", "A necklace", "A helmet"]', 3, 'A helmet is hard on the outside and protects your head in a fall.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am round, I bounce, and you can throw me, kick me or catch me. What am I?', '["A doll", "A ball", "A block", "A puzzle"]', 1, 'A ball is round and bouncy, so you can throw, kick or catch it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'Two kids sit at opposite ends of me and take turns going up and down. What am I?', '["A slide", "A sandbox", "A seesaw", "A swing"]', 2, 'A seesaw tips up and down like a balance, one child at each end.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big box of sand at the playground where you dig holes and build castles. What am I?', '["A sandbox", "A slide", "A swing", "A seesaw"]', 0, 'A sandbox is a box full of sand for digging and building.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'There are fifty-two of us in a set, with hearts, spades, clubs and diamonds. What are we?', '["A doll", "A drum", "A puzzle", "A deck of cards"]', 3, 'A deck has 52 cards in four suits: hearts, spades, clubs and diamonds.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I grow corn and wheat, and I take care of cows and sheep on my land. What am I?', '["A farmer", "A librarian", "A pilot", "A dentist"]', 0, 'A farmer grows crops and looks after farm animals.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I go from house to house dropping letters and packages into mailboxes. What am I?', '["A pilot", "A baker", "A mail carrier", "A dentist"]', 2, 'A mail carrier delivers letters and packages to your home.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I use a hammer and a saw to build things out of wood, like tables and houses. What am I?', '["A dentist", "A librarian", "A baker", "A carpenter"]', 3, 'A carpenter builds and fixes things made of wood.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I cut people''s hair with scissors and a comb. What am I?', '["A teacher", "A barber", "A baker", "A dentist"]', 1, 'A barber trims hair with scissors and a comb.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I work in a building full of books, and I help you find one and check it out. What am I?', '["A librarian", "A mechanic", "A pilot", "A gardener"]', 0, 'A librarian takes care of a library and helps people find books.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a loud rumbling noise that some people make while they sleep. What am I?', '["A sneeze", "A hiccup", "A snore", "A whistle"]', 2, 'Someone who is asleep can make a loud rumble called a snore.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'When you finish singing on stage, people make me with their hands to show they liked it. What am I?', '["A whisper", "Applause", "A snore", "A doorbell"]', 1, 'Applause is the sound of clapping hands to show people enjoyed a show.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am green and flat, I grow on branches, and in autumn I turn red and fall to the ground. What am I?', '["A feather", "A pebble", "A seed", "A leaf"]', 3, 'Leaves grow on branches, and many of them change color and fall in autumn.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am brown and scaly, I hang on evergreen trees, and I hold seeds inside my scales. What am I?', '["An apple", "A pebble", "An acorn", "A pine cone"]', 3, 'A pine cone grows on pine trees and holds seeds between its scales.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the rough brown covering on a tree trunk, and I protect the tree like skin. What am I?', '["A branch", "A leaf", "Bark", "A root"]', 2, 'Bark wraps around a tree trunk and keeps the tree safe.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a thin metal spike with a flat top, and I get hit with a hammer. What am I?', '["A spoon", "A nail", "A comb", "A pencil"]', 1, 'A nail is a metal spike hit into wood with a hammer to hold pieces together.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I roll out a long strip with numbers on it, and I snap back into my case when you let go. What am I?', '["A tape measure", "A shoelace", "A ruler", "A rope"]', 0, 'A tape measure rolls back into its case, and a stiff ruler cannot do that.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You stand on me, and I tell you how heavy you are. What am I?', '["A ruler", "A clock", "A scale", "A calculator"]', 2, 'A scale shows your weight when you stand on it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the season that comes right after winter, when flowers start to bloom and baby birds hatch. What am I?', '["Winter", "Spring", "Summer", "Autumn"]', 1, 'Spring follows winter, and plants begin to grow again.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the time when the sky is dark, the stars come out, and most people are asleep. What am I?', '["Night", "Noon", "Afternoon", "Morning"]', 0, 'Night is when it is dark, and most people sleep.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the exact middle of the night, when the clock hands both point to twelve and it is dark outside. What am I?', '["Breakfast time", "Recess", "Noon", "Midnight"]', 3, 'Midnight is twelve o''clock at night. Noon is twelve o''clock in the middle of the day.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What kind of dog never barks?', '["A puppy", "A hot dog", "A poodle", "A sheepdog"]', 1, 'A hot dog is something you eat, so it cannot bark. It is a silly joke about the name.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'Which letter of the alphabet sounds like a huge body of salty water?', '["The letter C", "The letter F", "The letter L", "The letter Q"]', 0, 'The letter C sounds like sea.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What is a witch''s favorite subject at school?', '["Music", "Math", "Spelling", "Art"]', 2, 'A witch loves casting spells, so her favorite subject is spelling. It is a pun!'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big building where doctors and nurses take care of people who are sick or hurt. What am I?', '["A castle", "A bakery", "A zoo", "A hospital"]', 3, 'A hospital is where sick or hurt people go to get better.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a tall tower by the sea, and my bright light guides ships safely past the rocks. What am I?', '["A bakery", "A barn", "A tent", "A lighthouse"]', 3, 'A lighthouse shines a bright light so ships can see where the rocks are.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a building where old things like dinosaur bones and paintings are shown for people to look at. What am I?', '["A hospital", "A museum", "A bakery", "A farm"]', 1, 'A museum keeps and shows interesting old things.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a building where children go on weekdays to learn, with classrooms and a playground. What am I?', '["A school", "A zoo", "A farm", "A bakery"]', 0, 'A school has classrooms where children learn.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I circle around the Earth high above, and I help with phones, TV and weather maps. What am I?', '["A balloon", "A kite", "A satellite", "An airplane"]', 2, 'A satellite orbits the Earth and sends information back down.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have three straight sides and three corners. What am I?', '["A circle", "A square", "A rectangle", "A triangle"]', 3, 'A triangle has three sides and three corners.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the word for a group of exactly twelve, like the eggs in a carton. What am I?', '["A dozen", "A pair", "A hundred", "A single"]', 0, 'A dozen means twelve of something, like 12 eggs.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I hop and swim, I croak, and I start life as a tadpole. What am I?', '["A frog", "A fish", "A duck", "A rabbit"]', 0, 'A baby frog is called a tadpole and lives in water. When it grows up, it hops and croaks.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the biggest animal that walks on land, and I have a long trunk and big floppy ears. What am I?', '["A horse", "A hippo", "An elephant", "A bear"]', 2, 'Only an elephant has a trunk and big floppy ears, and it is the largest land animal.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I hop on strong back legs and carry my baby in a pouch on my tummy. What am I?', '["A rabbit", "A frog", "A monkey", "A kangaroo"]', 3, 'A mother kangaroo keeps her baby safe in a pouch while she hops along.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the only mammal that can truly fly, and I sleep hanging upside down. What am I?', '["An eagle", "A bat", "An owl", "A butterfly"]', 1, 'Bats are mammals with wings. Owls, butterflies and eagles fly too, but they are not mammals.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I start as a caterpillar, rest inside a cocoon, and then come out with colorful wings. What am I?', '["A bee", "A butterfly", "A bat", "An ant"]', 1, 'A caterpillar changes inside its cocoon and comes out as a butterfly.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have no legs, but I slither on scaly skin and flick my tongue in and out. What am I?', '["A snake", "A frog", "A lizard", "A worm"]', 0, 'A snake is scaly and legless and flicks its tongue to sense things around it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a long, curved, yellow fruit, and you peel me before you eat me. What am I?', '["An apple", "A grape", "A pear", "A banana"]', 3, 'A banana has a yellow peel that you take off before eating the soft fruit inside.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am orange, I grow underground, and rabbits love to crunch me. What am I?', '["An orange", "A potato", "A carrot", "A pumpkin"]', 2, 'A carrot is an orange root vegetable that grows in the soil.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a round bun with a juicy meat patty inside, and I often come with fries. What am I?', '["A hamburger", "A cookie", "A pancake", "A pizza"]', 0, 'A hamburger is a bun with a patty tucked inside.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am round and baked, I often have chocolate chips in me, and I go well with milk. What am I?', '["A pancake", "A cookie", "A carrot", "A pizza"]', 1, 'A cookie is a small baked treat, and many have chocolate chips.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big orange vegetable that is carved into a face at Halloween. What am I?', '["An orange", "A carrot", "A melon", "A pumpkin"]', 3, 'Pumpkins are large and orange and are often carved into jack-o''-lanterns.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I grow underground inside a shell, and I am crushed to make a sticky spread for sandwiches. What am I?', '["A bean", "A pea", "A peanut", "A carrot"]', 2, 'Peanuts grow underground in shells and are ground up into peanut butter.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a round red fruit that many people call a vegetable, and I am squished to make ketchup and pizza sauce. What am I?', '["A banana", "A lemon", "A tomato", "A pumpkin"]', 2, 'A tomato is red and juicy, and it is used in salads and pizza sauce.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a round, bowl-shaped end and a handle, and you use me to eat soup or cereal. What am I?', '["A fork", "A plate", "A pillow", "A spoon"]', 3, 'A spoon''s round end holds liquid food like soup. A fork has prongs and the liquid runs through.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am big and warm, and you pull me over you at bedtime on a cold night. What am I?', '["A bucket", "A blanket", "A plate", "A lamp"]', 1, 'A blanket is a warm cover that keeps you cozy in bed.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have two blades and two loops for your fingers, and I snip paper into pieces. What am I?', '["Scissors", "A comb", "A glove", "A spoon"]', 0, 'Scissors have two blades that slide together to cut paper.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a soft covering that lies across the whole floor, and you can walk on me in your bare feet. What am I?', '["A curtain", "A pillow", "A shelf", "A carpet"]', 3, 'A carpet covers the floor and feels soft under your feet.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am big and cushy, and the whole family squeezes onto me to watch TV in the living room. What am I?', '["A sofa", "A table", "A bathtub", "A chair"]', 0, 'A sofa is a long, soft seat with room for several people, unlike a single chair.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a long handle and a stringy head, and you dip me in water to clean the floor. What am I?', '["A plate", "A mop", "A pillow", "A ladder"]', 1, 'A mop has a stringy head that soaks up water to wash the floor.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I live inside your mouth, help you taste ice cream, and help you talk. What am I?', '["Your ear", "Your knee", "Your tongue", "Your nose"]', 2, 'Your tongue lets you taste food and helps you make words.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I beat thump-thump inside your chest all day and all night, pumping blood around your body. What am I?', '["Your hair", "Your brain", "Your stomach", "Your heart"]', 3, 'Your heart pumps blood through your body and makes the thump-thump you can feel.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We are at the bottom of your legs, and you put socks and shoes on us. What are we?', '["Your feet", "Your knees", "Your ears", "Your hands"]', 0, 'Your feet are at the ends of your legs and go inside your shoes.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You have more than two hundred of us hidden inside you, and together we make up your skeleton. What are we?', '["Your skin", "Your bones", "Your nails", "Your hair"]', 1, 'Your bones are hard parts inside your body that hold you up as a skeleton.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I rumble and boom in the sky during a storm, and I can be very loud. What am I?', '["A rainbow", "Dew", "Thunder", "Snow"]', 2, 'Thunder is the loud booming sound you hear during a storm.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big body of still water with land all around me, and people paddle boats and fish on me. What am I?', '["A puddle", "A lake", "A hill", "A desert"]', 1, 'A lake is a large area of water surrounded by land.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a piece of land with water all around me, and a palm tree might grow on me. What am I?', '["A mountain", "A desert", "An island", "A lake"]', 2, 'An island is land with water on every side, unlike a lake, which is water with land around it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am hard and heavy, I lie on the ground, and if you kick me it hurts your toe. What am I?', '["A puddle", "A feather", "A leaf", "A rock"]', 3, 'A rock is a hard, heavy piece of stone.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I happen every morning when the sun peeks over the edge of the world and the sky turns pink and orange. What am I?', '["A sunrise", "A sunset", "A rainbow", "A storm"]', 0, 'A sunrise is when the sun first appears in the morning. A sunset happens at the end of the day.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am small and rubbery, and I make pencil mistakes disappear. What am I?', '["An eraser", "A backpack", "A crayon", "A ruler"]', 0, 'An eraser rubs out pencil marks so you can fix mistakes.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a cover and pages with lines, and you write your notes and stories in me. What am I?', '["A globe", "A notebook", "A crayon", "A lunchbox"]', 1, 'A notebook has lined pages ready for you to write on.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a small zip bag that holds your pencils, erasers and crayons. What am I?', '["A desk", "A stapler", "A lunchbox", "A pencil case"]', 3, 'A pencil case keeps your school supplies together in your backpack.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'Teachers give me to you to finish at home, and you bring me back the next day. What am I?', '["Lunch", "A holiday", "Homework", "Recess"]', 2, 'Homework is schoolwork that you do at home instead of in class.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big vehicle with lots of seats, and I stop at bus stops to pick up passengers. What am I?', '["A bus", "A canoe", "A rocket", "A sled"]', 0, 'A bus carries many passengers and stops along its route.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I blast off with a huge burst of fire and smoke and carry astronauts into outer space. What am I?', '["An airplane", "A rocket", "A helicopter", "A train"]', 1, 'A rocket is powerful enough to leave the Earth and travel into space.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big red truck with ladders and a long hose, and I race to put out fires. What am I?', '["A tractor", "A sled", "A bicycle", "A fire truck"]', 3, 'A fire truck carries ladders and hoses so firefighters can put out fires.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a little room that moves up and down inside a tall building when you press a button. What am I?', '["A bus", "A ladder", "An elevator", "A staircase"]', 2, 'An elevator lifts you between floors, and you do not have to climb.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We are strong shoes that go up over your ankles, and you wear us to stomp through mud. What are we?', '["Slippers", "A sock", "Boots", "Sandals"]', 2, 'Boots cover your ankles and keep your feet dry in mud.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a small pouch sewn into your pants, and you can keep a coin or a tissue in me. What am I?', '["A pocket", "A button", "A scarf", "A belt"]', 0, 'A pocket is a little pouch sewn into clothes for holding small things.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I sit on your nose and hook over your ears, and I help you see clearly. What am I?', '["A scarf", "A necklace", "A hat", "Glasses"]', 3, 'Glasses rest on your nose and ears and help you see better.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I hang around your neck, and I can be made of beads, pearls or a shiny chain. What am I?', '["A belt", "A necklace", "A glove", "A shoe"]', 1, 'A necklace is jewelry that hangs around your neck.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You roll dice, move your pieces around a flat board, and try to reach the finish first. What am I?', '["A doll", "A board game", "A drum", "A yo-yo"]', 1, 'A board game has a playing board, pieces and often dice, and players take turns.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You swing me over your head and under your feet, and you hop over me again and again. What am I?', '["A ball", "A yo-yo", "A kite", "A jump rope"]', 3, 'A jump rope swings around while you jump over it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a stretchy mat held by springs, and you jump on me to bounce high in the air. What am I?', '["A sandbox", "A swing", "A trampoline", "A slide"]', 2, 'A trampoline''s springy mat throws you up into the air.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I wear a white coat, I listen to your heartbeat, and I help you feel better when you are sick. What am I?', '["A doctor", "A pilot", "A baker", "A farmer"]', 0, 'A doctor checks patients and helps them get well.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I wake up very early to bake bread, cakes and cookies in the oven. What am I?', '["A farmer", "A pilot", "A baker", "A mechanic"]', 2, 'A baker makes bread and sweet treats and starts work early.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I wear a badge and a uniform, and my job is to keep the neighborhood safe. What am I?', '["A gardener", "A baker", "A teacher", "A police officer"]', 3, 'A police officer wears a badge and helps protect people.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I sit at a register in a store, scan your groceries and take your money. What am I?', '["A teacher", "A cashier", "A pilot", "A dentist"]', 1, 'A cashier rings up your items and takes payment at the store.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I wear coveralls and fix cars when their engines stop working. What am I?', '["A mechanic", "A teacher", "A baker", "A dentist"]', 0, 'A mechanic repairs cars and machines.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a high, shrill sound made by blowing through a tiny tube, and a referee uses me to stop the game. What am I?', '["A sneeze", "A whistle", "A snore", "A whisper"]', 1, 'A whistle makes a sharp, high sound when you blow into it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a very quiet way to talk, so only the person right next to you can hear. What am I?', '["A doorbell", "A siren", "A whisper", "A shout"]', 2, 'A whisper is soft and quiet so that only someone close by hears it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a tiny green baby plant that has just poked up out of the soil. What am I?', '["A button", "A pebble", "A feather", "A sprout"]', 3, 'A sprout is a new little plant that has just started to grow from a seed.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a tall yellow flower with a big round face that follows the sun, and my seeds can be eaten. What am I?', '["A sunflower", "A carrot", "A rose", "A cactus"]', 0, 'A sunflower is tall and yellow and turns to face the sun.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a yellow flower that turns into a white puffball, and you can blow on me to make a wish. What am I?', '["A rose", "A sunflower", "A cactus", "A dandelion"]', 3, 'A dandelion''s puffball has seeds that float away when you blow on it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a heavy metal head and a handle, and I pound nails into wood. What am I?', '["A sponge", "A hammer", "A feather", "A spoon"]', 1, 'A hammer is heavy and hits nails to push them into wood.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a wide scoop on the end of a long handle, and I dig holes in the ground. What am I?', '["A broom", "A hammer", "A shovel", "A rake"]', 2, 'A shovel''s wide scoop lifts soil and digs holes.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I pull nails and paper clips toward me without even touching them. What am I?', '["A magnet", "A feather", "A pillow", "A sponge"]', 0, 'A magnet pulls metal things like nails toward itself.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have two tubes joined together, and you hold me up to both eyes to see faraway birds. What am I?', '["A flashlight", "A bucket", "A ruler", "Binoculars"]', 3, 'Binoculars have two tubes, one for each eye, that make faraway things look closer.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the season, also called fall, when leaves turn red and orange and drop from the trees. What am I?', '["Autumn", "Winter", "Spring", "Summer"]', 0, 'Autumn is also called fall because the leaves fall from the trees.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the two days each week, Saturday and Sunday, when many kids do not go to school. What am I?', '["A year", "The weekend", "Monday", "A month"]', 1, 'The weekend is made of Saturday and Sunday.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I ring or beep at wake-up time to get you out of bed. What am I?', '["A blanket", "A pillow", "An alarm clock", "A lamp"]', 2, 'An alarm clock makes a noise at the time you set, so you wake up.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What do you call a bull that is taking a nap?', '["A cowboy", "A pillow", "A haystack", "A bulldozer"]', 3, 'A bull who is asleep is a bull-dozer, which sounds like bulldozer. It is a pun!'),
(1, 'riddle', 'Which letter of the alphabet sounds the same as a hot drink made from leaves?', '["The letter T", "The letter P", "The letter W", "The letter H"]', 0, 'The letter T sounds like tea.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What kind of music do balloons hate the most?', '["Rock music", "Jazz music", "Pop music", "Classical music"]', 2, 'Balloons do not like to pop, so pop music is their enemy. It is a joke!'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a huge stone building with towers, and long ago kings and queens lived in me. What am I?', '["A lighthouse", "A castle", "A barn", "A tent"]', 1, 'A castle has thick walls and towers, and royal families lived in them.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am made of cloth, held up with poles and ropes, and you sleep in me when you go camping. What am I?', '["A hospital", "A tent", "A castle", "A barn"]', 1, 'A tent is a cloth shelter that you can carry and put up for camping.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a busy place with long runways where airplanes take off and land. What am I?', '["A bakery", "A zoo", "A library", "An airport"]', 3, 'An airport has runways for airplanes and buildings for travelers.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the planet you live on, mostly covered with water, and I have one moon. What am I?', '["Saturn", "Jupiter", "Earth", "Mars"]', 2, 'Earth is our home planet. It has oceans and one moon.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the red planet, named for the rusty color of my dusty ground. What am I?', '["Mars", "The Moon", "Earth", "Saturn"]', 0, 'Mars is called the red planet because its ground is rusty red.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have four straight sides that are all exactly the same length, and four corners. What am I?', '["A triangle", "A square", "A circle", "A star"]', 1, 'A square has four equal sides and four corners.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'If you mix blue paint and yellow paint together, you make this color. What color is it?', '["Purple", "Pink", "Green", "Gray"]', 2, 'Blue and yellow mixed together make green.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I hoot at night, I have big round eyes, and I can turn my head almost all the way around. What am I?', '["A crow", "A parrot", "An eagle", "An owl"]', 3, 'Owls hoot at night and can turn their heads far around to look behind them.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have the longest neck of any animal, and I eat leaves from tall trees. What am I?', '["A horse", "A giraffe", "A zebra", "A camel"]', 1, 'A giraffe has a very long neck that helps it reach leaves high up in the trees.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have one or two big humps on my back and can walk in the hot desert for days without a drink. What am I?', '["An elephant", "A cow", "A camel", "A horse"]', 2, 'A camel stores fat in its humps and can go a long time without water.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a smart sea animal who jumps out of the waves, but I breathe air through a blowhole. What am I?', '["A dolphin", "An octopus", "A crab", "A shark"]', 0, 'Dolphins are mammals that come up to breathe air. Sharks, octopuses and crabs breathe underwater.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have fins and gills, I live in water, and I never need to come up for a bath. What am I?', '["A whale", "A frog", "A fish", "A duck"]', 2, 'Fish breathe underwater with gills and swim using their fins.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have long ears, a fluffy little tail, and love to munch on carrots. What am I?', '["A dog", "A cat", "A mouse", "A rabbit"]', 3, 'Rabbits have long ears and puffy tails and like eating carrots.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am baked in an oven, I am sliced for toast, and you can make a sandwich with me. What am I?', '["Bread", "Rice", "Soup", "Cheese"]', 0, 'Bread is baked from dough. You can toast it or use two slices for a sandwich.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am white, I come from cows, and you pour me over your cereal. What am I?', '["Juice", "Milk", "Water", "Honey"]', 1, 'Milk is a white drink that comes from cows, and it goes well with cereal.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am flat and round, and I am flipped in a pan and served with syrup for breakfast. What am I?', '["A pancake", "A pizza", "A cookie", "A sandwich"]', 0, 'A pancake is cooked in a pan and flipped over, then covered with syrup.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am long, thin pasta that turns soft when boiled, and you twirl me around a fork. What am I?', '["Rice", "Spaghetti", "Bread", "Cheese"]', 1, 'Spaghetti is long, thin pasta that you twirl on a fork.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a fluffy baked dessert with candles on top when it is someone''s birthday. What am I?', '["A pancake", "A pizza", "A cake", "A cookie"]', 2, 'A birthday cake is a sweet, fluffy dessert that has candles for making a wish.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I come in a bowl with milk, crunchy flakes or rings, and I am a popular breakfast. What am I?', '["Rice", "Pizza", "Soup", "Cereal"]', 3, 'Cereal is a breakfast food that you eat with milk from a bowl.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a soft mattress, and you climb under my covers to sleep at night. What am I?', '["A chair", "A shelf", "A sink", "A bed"]', 3, 'You sleep in a bed. Chairs, shelves and sinks are not made for sleeping.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a handle and sharp little prongs, and you use me to twirl noodles or poke your peas. What am I?', '["A spoon", "A fork", "A cup", "A plate"]', 1, 'A fork has prongs for spearing and twirling food.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I sit on a table by your bed, and I have a shade and a switch that turns on my light. What am I?', '["A curtain", "A pillow", "A lamp", "A cup"]', 2, 'A lamp gives light when you switch it on, and the shade covers the bulb.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a basin with a faucet where you wash your hands and the dishes. What am I?', '["A sink", "A lamp", "A shelf", "A blanket"]', 0, 'A sink is a basin with a tap, so you can wash things in it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I roar and suck up dust and crumbs from the floor through a long tube. What am I?', '["A lamp", "A vacuum cleaner", "A mop", "A fan"]', 1, 'A vacuum cleaner pulls dust into itself. A mop and a fan cannot suck things up.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a flat board fixed to a wall, and books and toys sit on top of me. What am I?', '["A curtain", "A bucket", "A shelf", "A carpet"]', 2, 'A shelf is a board fixed to a wall to hold things.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We come in pairs, we are round, and we open in the morning to let you see. What are we?', '["Your eyes", "Your knees", "Your ears", "Your toes"]', 0, 'Your eyes let you see the world around you.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We are white, we live in your mouth, and we help you chew your food. What are we?', '["Your nose", "Your tongue", "Your lips", "Your teeth"]', 3, 'You bite and chew food with your teeth.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I sit inside your head, and I help you think, remember and learn. What am I?', '["Your hair", "Your brain", "Your heart", "Your stomach"]', 1, 'Your brain is in your head and controls your thinking and your body.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I rumble when you are hungry, and I mix up your food after you swallow it. What am I?', '["Your knee", "Your lungs", "Your stomach", "Your ear"]', 2, 'Your stomach mixes your food and can rumble when it is empty.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We are hard and thin, we grow at the tips of your fingers, and you clip us when we get too long. What are we?', '["Your lips", "Your knees", "Your tongue", "Your fingernails"]', 3, 'Fingernails grow on your fingertips, and you trim them with clippers.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a bright, zigzag flash of light across the dark sky during a storm. What am I?', '["Lightning", "Snow", "Dew", "A rainbow"]', 0, 'Lightning is a bright flash of electricity in a stormy sky.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a small, rounded bump of land, lower than a mountain, and you can roll down my grassy side. What am I?', '["A puddle", "A lake", "A hill", "A cave"]', 2, 'A hill is a small, round rise in the land, much smaller than a mountain.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a river that tumbles straight down over a cliff with a big splash. What am I?', '["A waterfall", "A puddle", "A lake", "A hill"]', 0, 'A waterfall is where a river drops over the edge of a cliff.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am made of tiny grains, I cover beaches, and I get inside your shoes. What am I?', '["Water", "Snow", "Grass", "Sand"]', 3, 'Sand is made of tiny grains and is found on beaches.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I bring dark clouds, strong wind, heavy rain and thunder all at once. What am I?', '["A breeze", "A storm", "A puddle", "A rainbow"]', 1, 'A storm has strong wind, rain and thunder together, much more than a gentle breeze.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am made of colored wax, and you use me to color pictures. What am I?', '["A crayon", "A globe", "An eraser", "A stapler"]', 0, 'A crayon is a stick of colored wax used for coloring.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am sticky and squeezed from a bottle, and I stick paper to paper. What am I?', '["Milk", "Sand", "Glue", "Water"]', 2, 'Glue is sticky and holds pieces of paper together.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a small box with a handle, and your sandwich and juice ride to school inside me. What am I?', '["A ruler", "A globe", "A stapler", "A lunchbox"]', 3, 'A lunchbox keeps your lunch safe until it is time to eat.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I press down with a click and push a tiny metal piece through papers to hold them together. What am I?', '["A crayon", "A stapler", "An eraser", "A pencil"]', 1, 'A stapler fastens pages together with tiny metal staples.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I run along metal tracks, I have many cars linked together, and I say choo-choo. What am I?', '["A bus", "A train", "A boat", "A helicopter"]', 1, 'A train travels on tracks and pulls a long line of connected cars.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a ship that can dive deep under the sea and travel beneath the waves. What am I?', '["A bus", "A canoe", "A submarine", "An airplane"]', 2, 'A submarine can go underwater. A canoe stays on top of the water.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a short board with four small wheels, and you stand on me and push off with one foot. What am I?', '["A bicycle", "A sled", "A canoe", "A skateboard"]', 3, 'A skateboard has four wheels, and you stand on it and roll.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have one wheel in front and two handles at the back, and gardeners push me to carry dirt and plants. What am I?', '["A wheelbarrow", "A bicycle", "A skateboard", "A sled"]', 0, 'A wheelbarrow has one wheel and two handles, and it carries heavy loads in the garden.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I go around your waist through the loops of your pants, and I have a buckle. What am I?', '["A belt", "A glove", "A scarf", "A hat"]', 0, 'A belt holds up your pants and fastens with a buckle.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a waterproof coat that you wear on wet days so raindrops slide right off. What am I?', '["A scarf", "A pair of socks", "A raincoat", "A sweater"]', 2, 'A raincoat is waterproof, so the rain runs off it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I go around your wrist and tell you the time. What am I?', '["A belt", "A wristwatch", "A scarf", "A necklace"]', 1, 'A wristwatch is worn on your wrist so you can check the time.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a soft, stuffed animal with fuzzy fur and button eyes, and you cuddle me at bedtime. What am I?', '["A pillow", "A ball", "A puzzle", "A teddy bear"]', 3, 'A teddy bear is a cuddly stuffed toy shaped like a bear.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I hang from chains, and you sit on me and go back and forth in the air. What am I?', '["A sandbox", "A slide", "A seesaw", "A swing"]', 3, 'A swing hangs on chains and moves back and forth when you push.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I roll down on a string and then zip back up to your hand, over and over. What am I?', '["A doll", "A yo-yo", "A puzzle", "A kite"]', 1, 'A yo-yo spins down its string and comes back to your hand.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We are small cubes with dots on every side, and you roll us in board games. What are we?', '["Dice", "Marbles", "Buttons", "Coins"]', 0, 'Dice are little cubes with dots that you roll to get a number.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I stand at the front of the class, teach you to read and count, and give out gold stars. What am I?', '["A mechanic", "A pilot", "A teacher", "A dentist"]', 2, 'A teacher helps children learn at school.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I sit in a cockpit and steer airplanes high above the clouds. What am I?', '["A pilot", "A dentist", "A farmer", "A baker"]', 0, 'A pilot flies an airplane and takes passengers across the sky.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I paint pictures, draw sketches and make sculptures for people to enjoy. What am I?', '["A dentist", "A mechanic", "An artist", "A farmer"]', 2, 'An artist creates paintings, drawings and other works of art.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I put on a space suit, ride a rocket, and float around in space. What am I?', '["A baker", "A teacher", "A farmer", "An astronaut"]', 3, 'An astronaut travels to outer space, where everything floats.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I bring menus and carry food to your table at a restaurant. What am I?', '["A pilot", "A waiter", "A teacher", "A dentist"]', 1, 'A waiter takes orders and brings food to tables.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'Ah-ah-ah-CHOO! I burst out of your nose when it tickles or when you have a cold. What am I?', '["A whistle", "A hiccup", "A sneeze", "A snore"]', 2, 'A sneeze is the big ''achoo!'' that comes out when your nose tickles.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a loud wailing noise on police cars and fire trucks that tells everyone to move out of the way. What am I?', '["A whisper", "A snore", "A hiccup", "A siren"]', 3, 'A siren is a loud, wailing noise used by emergency vehicles.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a desert plant that stores water inside me, and I am covered with sharp spines. What am I?', '["A cactus", "A rose", "A carrot", "A leaf"]', 0, 'A cactus lives in dry places and keeps water inside, and its spines are sharp.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a flower with soft petals and a sweet smell, and I have thorns on my stem. What am I?', '["A carrot", "A rose", "A cactus", "A leaf"]', 1, 'A rose has soft, sweet-smelling petals and prickly thorns on its stem.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am one soft, colorful piece of a flower, and there are many of me around the middle. What am I?', '["A seed", "A petal", "A thorn", "A root"]', 1, 'A petal is one of the bright, soft parts that make up a flower.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a long blade with sharp teeth, and I cut through wood. What am I?', '["A saw", "A hammer", "A comb", "A spoon"]', 0, 'A saw''s sharp teeth cut wood. A comb''s teeth cannot cut anything.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a long handle and a row of pointy teeth, and I gather fallen leaves into a pile. What am I?', '["A spoon", "A hammer", "A shovel", "A rake"]', 3, 'A rake''s teeth pull leaves together so you can pile them up.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a round piece of glass on a handle, and I make tiny things look much bigger. What am I?', '["A mirror", "A window", "A magnifying glass", "A bottle"]', 2, 'A magnifying glass makes small things look bigger so you can see the details.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the coldest season, when snow falls and you need a warm coat. What am I?', '["Summer", "Autumn", "Spring", "Winter"]', 3, 'Winter is the coldest season of the year, with snow in many places.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I last about thirty days, and there are twelve of me in a year. January is one of me. What am I?', '["A week", "A month", "A day", "A minute"]', 1, 'A month is about thirty days long, and a year has twelve of them.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I come once a year on the day you were born, and there is cake, candles and presents. What am I?', '["A rainy day", "A bedtime", "A birthday", "A Monday"]', 2, 'Your birthday happens once a year on the day you were born.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You press my button to start me and press it again to stop me, and I count seconds in a race. What am I?', '["A stopwatch", "A ruler", "A globe", "A calendar"]', 0, 'A stopwatch counts the seconds from when you start it until you stop it.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What kind of ball do you throw in winter that melts in your warm hand?', '["A tennis ball", "A snowball", "A basketball", "A football"]', 1, 'A snowball is made of snow, so it melts when it gets warm.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What has ears but cannot hear?', '["A rabbit", "A cat", "Corn", "A mouse"]', 2, 'An ear of corn is the part of the plant with the kernels. Rabbits, cats and mice have ears that can really hear.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What does a bee use to brush its hair?', '["A honeycomb", "A toothbrush", "A mop", "A sponge"]', 0, 'A bee makes honey in a honeycomb, and a comb is used for brushing hair. It is a pun!'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a place with fields, barns and animals like cows and pigs, where food is grown. What am I?', '["A museum", "A hospital", "A bakery", "A farm"]', 3, 'A farm is where farmers grow crops and raise animals.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big red building on a farm where the hay is stored and the cows sleep. What am I?', '["A castle", "A barn", "A museum", "A hospital"]', 1, 'A barn is a large farm building that holds hay and shelters animals.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big tent show with clowns, acrobats and people who swing on trapezes. What am I?', '["A circus", "A library", "A hospital", "A bakery"]', 0, 'A circus is a show with clowns, acrobats and other exciting acts.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a planet famous for the big, bright rings that circle around me. What am I?', '["Earth", "Mars", "The Moon", "Saturn"]', 3, 'Saturn is known for its beautiful rings.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a giant swirl of billions of stars that includes our Sun and Earth, and my name sounds like a candy bar. What am I?', '["A comet", "The Moon", "The Milky Way", "A rocket"]', 2, 'The Milky Way is our galaxy, made of billions of stars including our Sun.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have six flat faces that are all squares, like a block or a dice. What am I?', '["A cube", "A pyramid", "A ball", "A cone"]', 0, 'A cube has six square faces. A ball has none, and a pyramid has triangle faces.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'A painter stirs a blob of red and a blob of blue into one puddle. Which color does the puddle turn?', '["Green", "Orange", "Brown", "Purple"]', 3, 'Red and blue mixed together make purple.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I buzz from flower to flower and make sweet honey. What am I?', '["An ant", "A ladybug", "A butterfly", "A bee"]', 3, 'Bees collect nectar from flowers and turn it into honey in their hive.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a black-and-white bird that cannot fly, but I swim very well and live where it is icy. What am I?', '["A penguin", "A duck", "An owl", "A seagull"]', 0, 'Penguins cannot fly, but they are excellent swimmers and live in cold places.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have webbed feet and a flat beak, and I say quack. What am I?', '["An owl", "A hen", "A duck", "A frog"]', 2, 'Ducks have webbed feet for swimming and a flat beak, and they quack.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I swing from tree to tree, and I love to eat bananas. What am I?', '["A rabbit", "A monkey", "A turtle", "A giraffe"]', 1, 'Monkeys are good climbers and swingers, and bananas are one of their favorite foods.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I purr when I am happy, chase mice, and sleep a lot during the day. What am I?', '["A cow", "A cat", "A horse", "A dog"]', 1, 'Cats purr when they are content and are famous for chasing mice and napping.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a bird, and the male of me has a giant tail that fans out with shiny blue and green circles. What am I?', '["A peacock", "A penguin", "An owl", "A duck"]', 0, 'A peacock shows off its beautiful, colorful tail feathers by fanning them out.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am yellow, I can have holes, and mice love to nibble on me in cartoons. What am I?', '["An egg", "Butter", "Bread", "Cheese"]', 3, 'Some cheese has holes in it, and cartoon mice are always sneaking a bite.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am golden and sweet and sticky, and bees make me. What am I?', '["Syrup", "Jam", "Honey", "Butter"]', 2, 'Bees make honey from flower nectar and store it in their hive.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have two slices of bread with tasty things like cheese or ham tucked in the middle. What am I?', '["A pancake", "A sandwich", "A soup", "A pizza"]', 1, 'A sandwich is made by putting a filling between two slices of bread.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a sour yellow fruit, and you can squeeze me to make lemonade. What am I?', '["A grape", "A pear", "A lemon", "A banana"]', 2, 'Lemons taste very sour, and their juice is used to make lemonade.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a red-skinned fruit that is crunchy and sweet, and a teacher might get one as a gift. What am I?', '["A carrot", "A banana", "A lemon", "An apple"]', 3, 'An apple is a crunchy fruit that is often red, and people give one to a teacher.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am small, round and juicy, I grow in bunches on a vine, and I can turn into raisins when dried. What am I?', '["A grape", "A pear", "An orange", "A lemon"]', 0, 'Grapes grow in bunches, and dried grapes are called raisins.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am soft and fluffy, and you rest your head on me when you lie down in bed. What am I?', '["A pillow", "A kettle", "A brick", "A spoon"]', 0, 'A pillow is soft and cushions your head so you can sleep comfortably.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am flat and round, and I hold your dinner on the table. What am I?', '["A blanket", "A plate", "A cup", "A kettle"]', 1, 'A plate is a flat dish that holds food at mealtime.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a hot box in the kitchen where mom bakes bread and cookies. What am I?', '["A closet", "A sink", "A bathtub", "An oven"]', 3, 'An oven gets very hot inside so it can bake food.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You fill me with warm water and bubbles and lie down in me to get clean. What am I?', '["A sink", "A closet", "A bathtub", "A bed"]', 2, 'A bathtub is big enough to lie in and holds water for bathing.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'Turn my handle and water pours out of my spout, so you can fill a glass. What am I?', '["A lamp", "A plate", "A faucet", "A curtain"]', 2, 'A faucet lets water flow out when you turn its handle.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a bent piece of wood or plastic, and you hang your shirt on me inside the closet. What am I?', '["A kettle", "A spoon", "A plate", "A hanger"]', 3, 'A hanger holds clothes up so they do not get wrinkled in the closet.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We stick out on the sides of your head and help you hear music and voices. What are we?', '["Your eyes", "Your ears", "Your nose", "Your chin"]', 1, 'Your ears catch sounds so you can hear.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'There are ten of us on your hands, and we help you hold a pencil. What are we?', '["Your fingers", "Your knees", "Your ears", "Your toes"]', 0, 'You have ten fingers on your hands that help you hold and grab things.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I grow on top of your head, I can be curly or straight, and you brush me every day. What am I?', '["Your nose", "Your hair", "Your chin", "Your knee"]', 1, 'Hair grows from your head, and you brush it to keep it neat.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We are two spongy bags in your chest that fill up with air every time you breathe. What are we?', '["Your brain", "Your heart", "Your lungs", "Your stomach"]', 2, 'Your lungs take in air when you breathe in.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We are two curved lines of little hairs that sit above your eyes. What are we?', '["Your eyebrows", "Your nose", "Your chin", "Your ears"]', 0, 'Eyebrows are the strips of hair above your eyes.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a thin, white, icy coating that sparkles on windows and grass on a freezing morning. What am I?', '["Sand", "Mud", "Thunder", "Frost"]', 3, 'Frost is a layer of tiny ice crystals that forms when it gets very cold.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big hollow place inside a mountain or hill, and bats like to sleep in me. What am I?', '["A hill", "A lake", "A cave", "A beach"]', 2, 'A cave is a large hollow space in rock, and bats hang there to rest.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am tiny drops of water on the grass early in the morning, and I disappear when the sun gets hot. What am I?', '["Dew", "Ice", "Snow", "Fog"]', 0, 'Dew forms on cool nights and dries up when the sun warms the grass.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I rise and fall on the sea and roll onto the shore, and you can also do me with your hand to say hello. What am I?', '["A puddle", "A bubble", "A cloud", "A wave"]', 3, 'A wave rolls across the sea, and a wave of your hand says hi.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am wet, brown and squishy ground made of dirt and water, and pigs love to roll in me. What am I?', '["Sand", "Mud", "Snow", "Grass"]', 1, 'Mud is soft, wet dirt that gets squishy and messy.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have two straps that go over your shoulders, and I carry your books to school. What am I?', '["A desk", "A bucket", "A hat", "A backpack"]', 3, 'A backpack rides on your back and carries your school things.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a wooden handle and soft hairs at the tip, and I spread paint on paper. What am I?', '["A broom", "A comb", "A paintbrush", "A spoon"]', 2, 'A paintbrush holds paint on its soft hairs so you can spread color.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You twist a pencil into me, and I shave its tip to a sharp point. What am I?', '["A pencil sharpener", "A glue stick", "An eraser", "A crayon"]', 0, 'A pencil sharpener cuts away a little wood and makes the pencil tip pointy.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a big white board on the classroom wall, and teachers write on me with markers that wipe away. What am I?', '["A blackboard", "A whiteboard", "A window", "A map"]', 1, 'A whiteboard is used with markers. A blackboard needs chalk instead.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have two big wings, I zoom down a runway, and I fly high in the sky carrying passengers. What am I?', '["A boat", "A helicopter", "An airplane", "A train"]', 2, 'An airplane speeds down a runway to take off, and its wings help it fly.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have huge back wheels, and a farmer drives me across the field to pull a plow. What am I?', '["A bus", "A tractor", "A sled", "A bicycle"]', 1, 'A tractor is a strong farm vehicle that pulls heavy machines through fields.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I slide over snow on smooth runners, and you can ride me down a snowy hill. What am I?', '["A sled", "A bicycle", "A train", "A rocket"]', 0, 'A sled slides on snow with no wheels at all.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a long strip of soft cloth that wraps around your neck to keep you warm in winter. What am I?', '["A sock", "A helmet", "A belt", "A scarf"]', 3, 'A scarf wraps around your neck and keeps out the cold.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am small and round with tiny holes, and I slip through a slit to close your shirt. What am I?', '["A coin", "A button", "A key", "A bell"]', 1, 'A button has holes for thread and fastens a shirt when you slide it through a slit.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You wear me to bed at night, and I am soft and comfy with a top and bottoms. What am I?', '["Pajamas", "A helmet", "An apron", "A raincoat"]', 0, 'Pajamas are soft clothes made for sleeping.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'A king or queen wears me on their head, and I am often golden with shiny jewels. What am I?', '["A belt", "A helmet", "A crown", "A scarf"]', 2, 'A crown is a royal headpiece, often gold with jewels.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I look like a tiny person with hair and clothes, and you can dress me up. What am I?', '["A puzzle", "A drum", "A ball", "A doll"]', 3, 'A doll is a toy shaped like a small person.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You climb my ladder to the top, then whoosh down my smooth ramp. What am I?', '["A sandbox", "A swing", "A slide", "A seesaw"]', 2, 'A slide has steps to climb and a smooth ramp to slide down.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'You stack us into towers and castles, and we come in lots of shapes and colors. What are we?', '["A ball", "Building blocks", "A drum", "A doll"]', 1, 'Building blocks are toys that you stack up to build things.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'We are little glass balls that you flick across the ground to hit other ones. What are we?', '["Buttons", "Dice", "Coins", "Marbles"]', 3, 'Marbles are small glass balls used in a game of flicking and hitting.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I wear a helmet and boots, ride a big red truck, and rescue people from fires. What am I?', '["A firefighter", "A librarian", "A farmer", "A barber"]', 0, 'A firefighter puts out fires and helps keep people safe.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I look at your teeth with a tiny mirror and help keep them healthy. What am I?', '["A dentist", "A farmer", "A barber", "A teacher"]', 0, 'A dentist takes care of your teeth. A barber only cuts hair.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I take care of pets like cats and dogs when they are sick or need a checkup. What am I?', '["A baker", "A teacher", "A veterinarian", "A mail carrier"]', 2, 'A veterinarian is a doctor for animals.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I plant flowers, pull weeds, and water the plants so they grow. What am I?', '["A pilot", "A gardener", "A baker", "A dentist"]', 1, 'A gardener looks after plants and flowers.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I sit on a tall chair by the pool or the beach, watch the swimmers and rescue anyone who needs help. What am I?', '["A baker", "A mechanic", "A librarian", "A lifeguard"]', 3, 'A lifeguard watches swimmers and helps keep them safe in the water.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I make you go ''hic!'' again and again, and sipping water slowly can help make me stop. What am I?', '["A snore", "A whistle", "A sneeze", "A hiccup"]', 3, 'A hiccup is a little ''hic!'' sound that jumps out of your throat.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'Ding-dong! You press my button, and I tell the people inside that someone is at the door. What am I?', '["A siren", "A whistle", "A doorbell", "A snore"]', 2, 'A doorbell rings ding-dong to say that a visitor has arrived.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am green, I grow in lawns, and you cut me with a mower. What am I?', '["Grass", "Snow", "Sand", "A rock"]', 0, 'Grass is the green plant that covers lawns and gets mowed.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a small nut that falls from an oak tree, and squirrels love to bury me. What am I?', '["A pine cone", "An acorn", "A peanut", "A pebble"]', 1, 'An acorn is the nut of an oak tree, and squirrels store them for winter.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a sharp point on a rose''s stem, and I can prick your finger. What am I?', '["A seed", "A petal", "A leaf", "A thorn"]', 3, 'A thorn is a sharp point on some plants that protects them.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a handle and a flat or cross-shaped tip, and I turn screws. What am I?', '["A screwdriver", "A saw", "A paintbrush", "A hammer"]', 0, 'A screwdriver turns screws to fasten things together.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I grip and turn bolts and nuts, and plumbers use me on pipes. What am I?', '["A shovel", "A wrench", "A hammer", "A saw"]', 1, 'A wrench grips nuts and bolts so you can turn them.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I have a long spout, and you tip me to sprinkle water on the plants. What am I?', '["A rake", "A bucket", "A watering can", "A shovel"]', 2, 'A watering can pours water gently through its spout onto plants.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the season with the longest, sunniest days, when ice cream melts fast. What am I?', '["Summer", "Autumn", "Spring", "Winter"]', 0, 'Summer is the warmest season with long, sunny days.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the part of the day when the sun comes up and you eat breakfast. What am I?', '["Bedtime", "Night", "Morning", "Evening"]', 2, 'Morning is the early part of the day when the sun rises.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am the day before today, and I have already gone by. What am I?', '["Today", "Next week", "Tomorrow", "Yesterday"]', 3, 'Yesterday is the day that came right before today.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What do you call a bear that has no teeth?', '["A polar bear", "A gummy bear", "A panda bear", "A brown bear"]', 1, 'A bear with no teeth is a gummy bear. It is a joke, because gums are where teeth would be.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'Which letter of the alphabet sounds like a buzzing insect that makes honey?', '["The letter Z", "The letter K", "The letter M", "The letter B"]', 3, 'The letter B sounds just like bee.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What kind of bed is found outside in the garden and has no mattress?', '["A bunk bed", "A sofa bed", "A flower bed", "A hospital bed"]', 2, 'A flower bed is a patch of soil in a garden where flowers grow.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'What can you hold in your left hand but never in your right hand?', '["A pencil", "Your right elbow", "A ball", "A book"]', 1, 'You can hold a pencil, ball or book in either hand, but your right elbow is out of reach for your right hand.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a park where you can visit lions, elephants and monkeys in their special homes. What am I?', '["A zoo", "A library", "A hospital", "A farm"]', 0, 'A zoo is a park where people can see many kinds of animals.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a very tall building with so many floors that I seem to touch the clouds. What am I?', '["A tent", "A skyscraper", "A bakery", "A barn"]', 1, 'A skyscraper is an extremely tall building with many floors.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a shop that smells of fresh bread and cakes because everything in me is baked. What am I?', '["A bakery", "A hospital", "A museum", "A zoo"]', 0, 'A bakery is a shop that bakes and sells bread and cakes.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a ball of ice and dust that grows a glowing tail when I get close to the sun. What am I?', '["A rocket", "A cloud", "A comet", "A planet"]', 2, 'A comet is icy and grows a bright tail near the sun.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am perfectly round, with no corners and no straight sides. What am I?', '["A triangle", "A rectangle", "A square", "A circle"]', 3, 'A circle is completely round with no corners.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'I am a number that means nothing at all, and I look like the letter O. What am I?', '["Ten", "Hundred", "Zero", "One"]', 2, 'Zero means none, and it looks like a round O.'),
(1, 'riddle', 'Which color, also the name of a juicy fruit, appears when red and yellow paint are mixed?', '["Pink", "Green", "Purple", "Orange"]', 3, 'Red and yellow mixed together make orange, the same name as the fruit.');
insert into questions (level, category, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanation) values
(1, 'spatial', 'Mia''s flat shape has 4 square corners, 2 long sides and 2 short sides. What shape is it?', '["Triangle", "Rectangle", "Circle", "Pentagon"]', 1, 'A rectangle has 4 square corners, with two long sides and two short sides. A triangle has only 3 corners and a circle has none.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which shape has two more sides than a square?', '["Triangle", "Pentagon", "Octagon", "Hexagon"]', 3, 'A square has 4 sides, and 4 + 2 = 6. The shape with 6 sides is a hexagon.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A flat shape with straight sides has 8 corners. How many sides does it have?', '["8", "4", "6", "10"]', 0, 'On a shape with straight sides, the number of corners is the same as the number of sides. So 8 corners means 8 sides.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Tomas draws 3 triangles on a page. How many corners did he draw altogether?', '["6", "12", "9", "3"]', 2, 'Each triangle has 3 corners. Three triangles have 3 + 3 + 3 = 9 corners.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which 3D shape can roll on its side and also stand up on its flat end?', '["Sphere", "Cube", "Pyramid", "Cylinder"]', 3, 'A cylinder has a curved side that rolls and flat circles at each end to stand on. A sphere cannot stand still on a flat spot and a cube cannot roll.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which 3D shape has one round flat face and one pointed tip?', '["Cone", "Cylinder", "Cube", "Sphere"]', 0, 'A cone has a round flat base and narrows to a single point at the top.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A tin can is a cylinder. How many flat round faces does it have?', '["1", "2", "3", "0"]', 1, 'A can has one flat circle on the top and one on the bottom. Its side is curved.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A square pyramid has a square bottom. What shape are its 4 sloping sides?', '["Squares", "Circles", "Triangles", "Rectangles"]', 2, 'The sloping sides all lean in to meet at the pointy top, so each one is a triangle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You are facing North and make a quarter turn clockwise (to the right). Which way are you facing now?', '["West", "South", "North", "East"]', 3, 'Clockwise is to the right. A quarter turn right from North points you East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The sun rises in the East. If you stand facing the sunrise, which direction is directly behind you?', '["West", "East", "North", "South"]', 0, 'Behind you is the opposite of the way you face. The opposite of East is West.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which direction lies exactly halfway between North and East?', '["North-West", "South-East", "North-East", "South-West"]', 2, 'North-East sits between North and East, so that is the halfway direction.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You face West and make a quarter turn to your left. Which way do you face now?', '["North", "South", "East", "West"]', 1, 'When you face West, your left hand points South. Turning left points you South.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'On a map with North at the top, the library is drawn directly above the school. Which direction is the library from the school?', '["North", "South", "East", "West"]', 0, 'Up on this map is North, so something drawn directly above is to the North.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Sara''s house is directly East of the park. Which direction is the park from Sara''s house?', '["East", "North", "West", "South"]', 2, 'If her house is East of the park, then the park is the opposite way from her house, which is West.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A boat sails 3 km North and then 3 km South. Where is it compared with where it began?', '["3 km North of the start", "3 km South of the start", "6 km North of the start", "Back at the start"]', 3, 'The 3 km North and the 3 km South cancel out, so it ends up back where it began.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Leo walks 4 steps West and then 2 steps East. Where is he compared with where he started?', '["2 steps East of the start", "2 steps West of the start", "6 steps West of the start", "Back at the start"]', 1, 'Going 2 steps East undoes 2 of the 4 steps West. That leaves him 2 steps West of the start.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You sit across the table from your friend. She holds up her right hand. Which side of YOU is her hand nearest to?', '["Your right side", "Straight in front", "Your back", "Your left side"]', 3, 'Facing each other, her right hand is on the same side as your left hand.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Your classroom door is on your left as you face the front of the room. Which way do you turn to face the door?', '["Right", "Around the other way", "Left", "Up"]', 2, 'The door is on your left side, so you turn left to face it.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Ali is facing North and his dog stands on his right side. Which direction is the dog?', '["East", "West", "South", "North"]', 0, 'When you face North, your right side is East. The dog is to the East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Zoe walks North along a path. A pond is on her left. Which direction is the pond?', '["East", "West", "South", "North"]', 1, 'Facing North, your left side is West. So the pond is to the West.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'On a bookshelf, the red book is on the top shelf and the blue book is on the bottom shelf. Which book is higher up?', '["The red book", "The blue book", "They are at the same height", "Neither"]', 0, 'The top shelf is higher than the bottom shelf, so the red book is higher.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A bird sits on a branch. A squirrel sits on the ground below the tree. Which animal is lower down?', '["The bird", "They are level", "The squirrel", "Neither"]', 2, 'The ground is lower than a branch, so the squirrel is lower than the bird.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A building has a shop on the ground floor, a gym one floor above it, and a cafe one floor above the gym. Which one is on the top floor?', '["The shop", "The gym", "The parking lot", "The cafe"]', 3, 'The floors go shop, gym, cafe from the bottom to the top. The cafe is the highest.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Three houses stand in a row: red, blue and green. Blue is between the red and green houses. If green is at the left end, where is red?', '["At the left end", "At the right end", "In the middle", "Behind the blue house"]', 1, 'The order is green, blue, red from left to right, so red is at the right end.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Priya is 3rd in the queue for the water fountain. How many people are in front of her?', '["2", "3", "4", "1"]', 0, 'Two people are ahead of her in the 1st and 2nd places. She is third.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'There are 6 children in a line. Sam is at the very back. What place in the line is he?', '["5th", "1st", "6th", "7th"]', 2, 'With 6 children, the last one in the line is number 6.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'In a line of children, Ben is 5th from the front and 3rd from the back. How many children are in the line?', '["8", "7", "6", "9"]', 1, 'There are 4 children ahead of Ben and 2 behind him. Add Ben himself: 4 + 2 + 1 = 7.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Five ducks waddle in a line. The 2nd duck is yellow. How many ducks are behind the yellow duck?', '["2", "4", "1", "3"]', 3, 'Duck 1 is in front, duck 2 is yellow, and ducks 3, 4 and 5 are behind. That is 3 ducks.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A counter starts on the square marked S. It moves 3 squares right and then 2 squares left. How far from S is it now?', '["1 square to the left", "5 squares to the right", "1 square to the right", "It is back on S"]', 2, '3 right and 2 left leaves it 3 - 2 = 1 square to the right of S.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A snail starts on a grid square. It moves 2 squares up, then 2 squares right, then 2 squares down. Where is it compared with its start?', '["2 squares up", "2 squares to the right", "2 squares to the left", "Back on the start"]', 1, 'The up and down moves cancel out, leaving only the 2 squares it moved to the right.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A frog hops 2 squares up, 3 squares right, and then 2 squares down. Where does it land compared with its start?', '["2 squares right, 1 up", "3 squares right, 2 down", "5 squares right, same row", "3 squares right, same row"]', 3, 'Up 2 and down 2 cancel out, so it is in the same row. It has gone 3 squares to the right.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Mina''s counter is on the top-left square of a board. She moves it 1 square right, 1 square down, and 1 square left. Where is it now?', '["Directly below where it started", "Back on the start", "Directly right of where it started", "Diagonally below and right"]', 0, 'Right then left cancel out. The one move down leaves it directly below its starting square.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A robot stands in the centre of a grid. It moves up, up, down, down, left, right. Where does it end up?', '["One square left", "Two squares up", "One square right", "Back in the centre"]', 3, 'Up-up-down-down cancels out, and left-right cancels out too. The robot is back in the centre.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A letter is flipped left to right, like its reflection in a mirror. Which capital letter would look exactly the same?', '["F", "A", "G", "R"]', 1, 'The two halves of the letter A are matching, so flipping it left to right gives A again. F, G and R all change.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You step closer to a mirror. What does your reflection appear to do?', '["Comes closer too", "Moves farther away", "Disappears", "Stays where it was"]', 0, 'A reflection acts like you. When you step toward the mirror, it appears to come toward the mirror too.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A mirror stands on a page right next to the letter b, on its right-hand side. What letter appears in the mirror?', '["p", "q", "d", "b"]', 2, 'A mirror flips left and right. A b, with its round part on the right, becomes a d.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'An arrow points up. You turn it a quarter turn clockwise. Which way does it point now?', '["Right", "Left", "Down", "Up"]', 0, 'Clockwise is the way clock hands move. A quarter turn takes up to right.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'An arrow points left. You give it a half turn. Which way does it point now?', '["Left", "Right", "Up", "Down"]', 1, 'A half turn points it the opposite way. The opposite of left is right.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The letter T is standing upright with its flat bar on top. Turn the page a half turn. Where is the flat bar now?', '["At the top", "On the left", "At the bottom", "On the right"]', 2, 'A half turn flips things upside down. The bar that was on top ends up at the bottom.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A rectangle stands tall, taller than it is wide. After a quarter turn, how does it look?', '["Still taller than wide", "Like a circle", "Like a triangle", "Wider than it is tall"]', 3, 'A quarter turn swaps the up-down and left-right directions, so the long sides now run side to side.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which capital letter can be folded down the middle from top to bottom so that both halves match exactly?', '["F", "R", "P", "M"]', 3, 'The left and right halves of M are mirror images of each other. The others are not.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A butterfly''s wings match on both sides. If you could fold it down the middle, what would happen?', '["One wing would be bigger", "Only the bodies would match", "The wings would fit exactly on top of each other", "The wings would not touch"]', 2, 'The two halves are mirror images, so folding along the middle lines them up perfectly.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A square paper is folded corner to corner. How do the two halves compare?', '["One is bigger", "They match exactly", "They are different shapes", "One half is a circle"]', 1, 'Folding a square along a diagonal makes two equal triangles that fit on top of each other.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which capital letter has a top half that matches its bottom half if you fold it straight across the middle?', '["E", "F", "G", "L"]', 0, 'The top half of E is a mirror image of the bottom half. F, G and L do not match that way.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You fold a square piece of paper in half once, then open it out again. How many fold lines (creases) do you see?', '["1", "2", "3", "4"]', 0, 'One fold makes one crease, which stays on the paper when you open it.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A paper is folded in half. A hole is punched through both layers in the middle of the folded paper, away from the fold. How many holes are there after unfolding?', '["1", "3", "4", "2"]', 3, 'The punch goes through two layers, so there is one hole in each half.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You fold a sheet of paper in half, and then in half again. How many layers of paper are stacked up?', '["2", "4", "3", "8"]', 1, 'Each fold doubles the layers. 1 layer becomes 2, and then 2 becomes 4.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A tower is made of 5 blocks stacked one on top of another. How many blocks sit above the bottom block?', '["5", "3", "4", "6"]', 2, 'The tower has 5 blocks. Take away the bottom one and 4 are above it.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Two rows of 3 blocks each sit side by side on the floor. How many blocks are there?', '["5", "8", "6", "9"]', 2, 'Two rows of 3 is 3 + 3 = 6 blocks.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A block staircase has 1 block on the first step, 2 blocks on the second step and 3 blocks on the third step. How many blocks are used?', '["6", "5", "7", "9"]', 0, 'Add the steps together: 1 + 2 + 3 = 6 blocks.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Lena builds 3 layers, and each layer has 4 blocks. How many blocks does she use?', '["7", "9", "16", "12"]', 3, 'Three layers of 4 blocks is 4 + 4 + 4 = 12.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A block tower is 2 blocks wide, 2 blocks long and 2 blocks tall. How many blocks make it?', '["6", "8", "4", "12"]', 1, 'Each layer is 2 x 2 = 4 blocks and there are 2 layers. So 4 + 4 = 8.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which 3D shape is a shoebox closest to?', '["A sphere", "A cone", "A rectangular box (cuboid)", "A cylinder"]', 2, 'A shoebox has flat rectangular sides, so it is a rectangular box, or cuboid.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A door is usually which flat shape?', '["Circle", "Rectangle", "Triangle", "Oval"]', 1, 'Most doors are tall with four square corners and two long and two short sides. That is a rectangle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these everyday objects is shaped like a cylinder?', '["A paper towel roll", "A dice", "A party hat", "A basketball"]', 0, 'A paper towel roll has two round ends and a curved side, just like a cylinder.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'It is exactly 3 o''clock. Which number is the minute hand pointing at?', '["3", "6", "9", "12"]', 3, 'On the hour, the minute hand always points straight up at the 12.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'At half past 4, which number does the minute hand point at?', '["4", "5", "6", "12"]', 2, 'Half past means the minute hand is halfway around the clock, pointing straight down at the 6.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'On a clock the minute hand points at the 3 and the hour hand is just past the 8. What time is it?', '["3:40", "8:15", "8:03", "3:08"]', 1, 'The minute hand at 3 means 15 minutes past. The hour hand just past 8 means it is 8:15.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'At 9 o''clock, the hour hand points at the 9. Is the 9 on the left or the right side of a clock face?', '["Left side", "Right side", "At the top", "At the bottom"]', 0, 'The 3 is on the right and the 9 is on the left of a normal clock.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A tennis ball is about 6 cm wide. Which box can hold it: one that is 3 cm wide or one that is 10 cm wide?', '["The 3 cm box", "Both boxes", "Neither box", "The 10 cm box"]', 3, 'The ball is wider than 3 cm, so it will not fit there. It will fit in the 10 cm box.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Sara has three sticks that are 12 cm, 7 cm and 20 cm long. Which one is the middle length?', '["7 cm", "12 cm", "20 cm", "None of them"]', 1, 'Line them up from shortest to longest: 7, 12, 20. The stick in the middle is 12 cm.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A toy car is 10 cm long. A toy garage is only 8 cm long inside. Does the car fit lengthways inside the garage?', '["Yes, it fits easily", "Yes, but only just", "No, the car is longer", "Only if the car is turned around"]', 2, 'The car is 10 cm and the garage is 8 cm. The car is 2 cm too long.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The cat is under the table. Where is the table compared with the cat?', '["Above the cat", "Below the cat", "Beside the cat", "Inside the cat"]', 0, 'If the cat is under the table, the table is over it, so the table is above the cat.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'In a photo, Lily stands in front of Omar. Who is closer to the camera?', '["Omar", "They are the same distance", "Neither", "Lily"]', 3, 'In front of means nearer to the camera, so Lily is closer.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A cup sits on a plate, and the plate sits on a tray. Which one is at the very bottom?', '["The tray", "The cup", "The plate", "They are all level"]', 0, 'The cup is on the plate and the plate is on the tray. That puts the tray at the bottom.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A pattern goes: triangle, triangle, circle, triangle, triangle, circle, triangle, triangle. What comes next?', '["Triangle", "Circle", "Square", "Star"]', 1, 'The pattern repeats two triangles then a circle. After two triangles, a circle comes next.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'An arrow turns a quarter turn each time: up, right, down, left, up, right. Which way does it point next?', '["Up", "Left", "Right", "Down"]', 3, 'The arrow keeps turning clockwise: up, right, down, left. After right comes down.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Blocks are lined up: red, blue, blue, red, blue, blue, red. What are the next two blocks?', '["Red, blue", "Blue, red", "Blue, blue", "Red, red"]', 2, 'The pattern is red then two blues. After the red, two blue blocks come next.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Two identical squares are placed side by side with their edges touching. What shape do they make together?', '["A rectangle", "A bigger square", "A triangle", "A circle"]', 0, 'Two squares side by side make a shape that is twice as long as it is tall, which is a rectangle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A square is cut in half along a line from one corner to the opposite corner. What shape is each piece?', '["A square", "A triangle", "A circle", "A rectangle"]', 1, 'A diagonal cut splits the square into two triangles.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Kofi taps each corner of a flat shape with his pencil. He taps 5 times. Which shape is it?', '["Square", "Hexagon", "Pentagon", "Triangle"]', 2, 'One tap for each corner means 5 corners. A shape with 5 corners and 5 sides is a pentagon.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'How many straight sides do a circle and a triangle have together?', '["0", "3", "4", "6"]', 1, 'A circle has no straight sides and a triangle has 3. So 0 + 3 = 3.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Pia''s shape has 6 sides. Chan''s shape has 3 fewer sides than Pia''s. What is Chan''s shape?', '["A square", "A pentagon", "A circle", "A triangle"]', 3, '6 - 3 = 3 sides. A shape with 3 sides is a triangle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'How many more sides does an octagon have than a square?', '["4", "2", "3", "8"]', 0, 'An octagon has 8 sides and a square has 4. The difference is 8 - 4 = 4.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Two cubes are glued together, face to face. What shape do they make?', '["A bigger cube", "A cylinder", "A rectangular box (cuboid)", "A sphere"]', 2, 'Two cubes in a row make a shape that is twice as long as it is wide, which is a rectangular box.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which 3D shape is best for building a tall, steady tower by stacking?', '["Sphere", "Cube", "Cone", "Cylinder lying on its side"]', 1, 'Cubes have flat faces that fit together and stay put, so they stack well. Spheres roll away.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which 3D shape has 6 faces, and every face is a rectangle or a square?', '["Cuboid", "Cone", "Sphere", "Cylinder"]', 0, 'A rectangular box (cuboid) has 6 flat faces with straight edges. A cone, sphere or cylinder has curved surfaces.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'How many pointed tips does a cone have?', '["0", "2", "3", "1"]', 3, 'A cone has one pointed tip at the top and a round base at the bottom.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A compass needle points North. You turn to face where it points, and then turn right. Which way do you face?', '["West", "South", "North", "East"]', 3, 'You face North, and a turn to the right takes you to East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'After school you walk straight toward the setting sun. Which direction are you walking?', '["East", "North", "West", "South"]', 2, 'The sun sets in the West, so walking toward it means walking West.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these is NOT a compass direction?', '["Up", "North", "South", "West"]', 0, 'North, South, East and West are compass directions. Up is not one of them.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You are facing North. How many quarter turns do you need to make to face South?', '["1", "2", "3", "4"]', 1, 'A quarter turn takes you from North to East or West. Two quarter turns in the same direction take you to South.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A bird flies South from the top of a tree. Where is the tree compared with the bird?', '["South of the bird", "East of the bird", "West of the bird", "North of the bird"]', 3, 'The bird went South, so the tree is back the other way, to the North.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'On a map, a lake is East of the forest, and a farm is East of the lake. Which place is farthest West?', '["The lake", "The forest", "The farm", "They are all the same"]', 1, 'Going East, the order is forest, lake, farm. So the forest is farthest West.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A postman walks 2 blocks East and then 2 blocks North. Which direction is he from where he began?', '["North-East", "South-West", "North-West", "South-East"]', 0, 'He moved East and North by the same amount, so he is North-East of his start.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A town map has North at the top. The bakery is left of the bank, and the bank is left of the school. Which building is farthest East?', '["The bakery", "The bank", "The school", "They are the same"]', 2, 'On this map, left is West and right is East. The order from West to East is bakery, bank, school.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You face the school building. The main gate is on your right and the bike shed is on your left. You turn around to face away from the school. Where is the gate now?', '["On your right", "In front of you", "Behind you", "On your left"]', 3, 'Turning around swaps your sides. The gate that was on your right is now on your left.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Three children stand side by side facing the front of the room. Dana is on the left, Eli is in the middle and Fay is on the right. Who is on Eli''s right side?', '["Dana", "Fay", "Nobody", "Eli himself"]', 1, 'They all face the same way, so Fay, on the right end, is beside Eli''s right side.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You write with your right hand. Which hand is best to use to hold the paper still?', '["Your right hand", "Either hand", "Your left hand", "Neither hand"]', 2, 'Your right hand is busy with the pencil. So the left hand holds the paper.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Nadia is facing East and her friend stands on her left side. Which direction is the friend?', '["North", "South", "East", "West"]', 0, 'When you face East, your left hand points North. So the friend is to the North.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A shelf has 3 rows. Apples are in the top row, pears are in the middle row and plums are in the bottom row. Which fruit is directly above the plums?', '["Apples", "Plums", "None", "Pears"]', 3, 'The rows from the top are apples, pears, plums. The row right above the plums is the pears.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Amir lives on the 4th floor of a building. Chen lives 2 floors below Amir. Which floor does Chen live on?', '["2nd floor", "3rd floor", "6th floor", "1st floor"]', 0, 'Two floors below the 4th floor is 4 - 2 = the 2nd floor.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Four toy cars are in a row: red, green, yellow and blue. Which car is between the green and the blue car?', '["The red car", "The green car", "The yellow car", "The blue car"]', 2, 'In the row, yellow comes right after green and right before blue.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A picture hangs above a sofa, and a rug lies below the sofa on the floor. Which of the three things is the lowest?', '["The sofa", "The rug", "The picture", "They are all level"]', 1, 'The rug is on the floor below the sofa. The picture is higher still.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'In a race, Kim finished before Lee, and Lee finished before Mo. Who finished last of these three?', '["Kim", "Mo", "Lee", "They tied"]', 1, 'The order is Kim, then Lee, then Mo. So Mo came last.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Eight kids stand in a line. Ana is 3rd from the front. How many kids stand behind Ana?', '["3", "4", "5", "6"]', 2, 'Ana is 3rd, so 2 kids are ahead of her and the other 8 - 3 = 5 kids are behind her.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Ten children sit on a bench. Yuki is 4th from the left end. How many children are on Yuki''s left?', '["4", "5", "6", "3"]', 3, 'Yuki is 4th, so 3 children are before her on the left.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Seven people stand in a line. Which place is the person in the exact middle?', '["4th", "3rd", "5th", "7th"]', 0, 'There are 3 people before and 3 people after the middle person. That makes them 4th.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A robot starts in the bottom-left square of a 3 by 3 grid. It moves up 2 squares and then right 2 squares. Which square is it on?', '["The top-left corner", "The bottom-right corner", "The centre", "The top-right corner"]', 3, 'Up 2 takes it to the top row and right 2 takes it to the far right column. That is the top-right corner.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You start facing North. You take one step forward, turn right, take one step forward, turn right again, and take one more step forward. Which way are you facing now?', '["North", "East", "South", "West"]', 2, 'The first right turn points you East and the second right turn points you South.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A ladybug walks 2 squares right, 2 squares down, 2 squares left and 2 squares up on a grid. What shape does its path draw?', '["A triangle", "A square", "A straight line", "A circle"]', 1, 'Four sides of the same length with turns of a quarter turn each make a square.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A frog moves 3 squares up, then 1 square right, and then 3 squares down. How many squares did it hop in total?', '["7", "1", "4", "6"]', 0, 'Count every square hopped: 3 + 1 + 3 = 7.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Mia moves a game piece: 1 square down, 1 square right, 1 square down, 1 square right. In which general direction is she moving?', '["Up and to the left", "Straight down", "Down and to the right", "Straight right"]', 2, 'Every step is either down or to the right, so she moves down and to the right, like a staircase.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which word looks the same when you see it reflected in a mirror placed beside it?', '["DAD", "MOM", "BAG", "PIG"]', 1, 'M and O look the same in a mirror, so the word MOM reads the same. D, B, G and P change.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'An arrow points to the right (→) and a mirror stands just to its right side. Which way does the arrow in the mirror point?', '["Right", "Up", "Down", "Left"]', 3, 'A mirror to the side flips left and right. The reflected arrow points back toward the real arrow, to the left.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which digit looks the same when reflected in a mirror placed beside it?', '["8", "2", "3", "6"]', 0, 'The two halves of an 8 are matching. 2, 3 and 6 change when flipped.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The letter L stands upright with its foot pointing to the right. You turn it a quarter turn clockwise. Where does the foot point?', '["Down", "Up", "Left", "Right"]', 0, 'A quarter turn clockwise takes right to down.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A triangle sits on the table with its point up. You give it a half turn. Where is the point now?', '["Up", "Down", "Left", "Right"]', 1, 'A half turn flips the shape upside down, so the point faces down.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'An arrow points right. You turn it a quarter turn anticlockwise. Which way does it point now?', '["Down", "Left", "Right", "Up"]', 3, 'Anticlockwise is the opposite way to clock hands. A quarter turn takes right to up.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A square is turned a quarter turn four times in a row in the same direction. How does it end up compared with the start?', '["Upside down", "Turned to the left", "It looks just like the start", "Turned to the right"]', 2, 'Four quarter turns make one full turn, which brings the square back to where it began.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which capital letter can be folded both top to bottom and left to right so that the halves always match?', '["F", "A", "H", "E"]', 2, 'H is matching in both directions. A matches only one way, E matches only across the middle, and F matches neither.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A heart shape is folded along the line from the dip at the top down to the point at the bottom. Do the two halves match?', '["No, one half is bigger", "Yes, they match exactly", "Only the top matches", "Only the bottom matches"]', 1, 'A heart is the same on its left and right, so folding down the middle lines the halves up.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Ann draws a butterfly with matching wings. She puts 3 spots on the left wing. How many spots should the whole butterfly have so both wings match?', '["3", "4", "9", "6"]', 3, 'The right wing needs the same 3 spots as the left wing. 3 + 3 = 6.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these capital letters does NOT have a line of symmetry?', '["F", "A", "O", "T"]', 0, 'A, O and T can each be folded to match. F has no fold that makes matching halves.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You fold a sheet of paper in half and cut along the crease with scissors. How many pieces do you have?', '["2", "1", "3", "4"]', 0, 'Cutting along the fold splits the paper into two halves.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A round paper circle is folded in half. What shape do you get?', '["A triangle", "A square", "A half circle", "A full circle"]', 2, 'Folding a circle across its middle gives half of it, a half circle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A square sandwich is cut into 4 equal squares with straight cuts across the whole sandwich. How many cuts are needed?', '["1", "2", "3", "4"]', 1, 'One cut across the middle makes 2 pieces. A second cut across the other way makes 4 squares.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A wall of blocks is 5 blocks long and 2 blocks high. How many blocks does it have?', '["7", "12", "25", "10"]', 3, 'Two rows of 5 blocks is 5 + 5 = 10.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A block pyramid has 1 block on the top layer, 4 blocks in the middle layer and 9 blocks in the bottom layer. How many blocks in total?', '["13", "15", "14", "16"]', 2, 'Add the layers: 1 + 4 + 9 = 14.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A tower has 7 blocks. Jo takes 3 blocks off the top. How many blocks are left in the tower?', '["3", "5", "10", "4"]', 3, '7 - 3 = 4 blocks are left.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A box shape is built with 2 layers, and each layer is 2 rows of 3 blocks. How many blocks touch the floor?', '["3", "6", "12", "2"]', 1, 'Only the bottom layer touches the floor. It has 2 rows of 3 = 6 blocks.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Elias has 10 blocks. He builds two towers that are each 4 blocks tall. How many blocks are left over?', '["2", "4", "6", "8"]', 0, 'Two towers of 4 use 8 blocks. 10 - 8 = 2 left over.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A yield sign on the road has 3 equal sides. Which flat shape is it?', '["Square", "Triangle", "Circle", "Rectangle"]', 1, 'A shape with 3 sides is a triangle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these objects is closest to a sphere?', '["A marble", "A book", "A ruler", "A cardboard box"]', 0, 'A marble is round in every direction, like a sphere.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these is closest to a rectangular box (cuboid)?', '["A football", "A drinks can", "A brick", "A funnel"]', 2, 'A brick has flat rectangular faces and straight edges, like a cuboid.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Both hands of a clock point straight up at the 12. What time is it?', '["6 o''clock", "3 o''clock", "9 o''clock", "12 o''clock"]', 3, 'When both hands point at 12, it is exactly 12 o''clock.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The minute hand points straight up at 12 and the hour hand points straight down at 6. What time is it?', '["12 o''clock", "6 o''clock", "3 o''clock", "9 o''clock"]', 1, 'On the hour the minute hand is at 12. The hour hand at 6 means it is 6 o''clock.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The minute hand of a clock points at the 9. How many minutes past the hour is it?', '["9", "15", "45", "30"]', 2, 'Each number is 5 minutes. 9 x 5 = 45 minutes past.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The minute hand points at the 6, and the hour hand is halfway between the 2 and the 3. What time is it?', '["3:30", "2:06", "6:02", "2:30"]', 3, 'The minute hand at 6 means half past. The hour hand halfway between 2 and 3 means 2:30.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A doorway is 2 metres tall. Which can walk through without ducking: a 1 metre tall child or a 3 metre tall giraffe?', '["The child", "The giraffe", "Both can", "Neither can"]', 0, 'The child is shorter than the doorway. The giraffe is taller than it.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A small cup fits inside a medium cup, and the medium cup fits inside a large cup. Does the small cup fit inside the large cup?', '["No", "Only if it is upside down", "Only if the cups are empty", "Yes"]', 3, 'If the small cup fits in the medium one, and that one fits in the large one, the small cup fits in the large cup too.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which is the widest: a 2 cm coin, a 5 cm cookie, a 9 cm plate or a 4 cm button?', '["The coin", "The plate", "The cookie", "The button"]', 1, '9 cm is the biggest number, so the plate is widest.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Ravi stands behind Meg in the queue for the bus. Who gets on the bus first?', '["Ravi", "They get on together", "Meg", "Nobody"]', 2, 'Meg is in front, so she reaches the bus first.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A bird perches on top of a chimney, and the chimney is on a roof. Which is highest?', '["The bird", "The chimney", "The roof", "They are all level"]', 0, 'The bird sits on top of the chimney, which stands on the roof. So the bird is highest.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Tom stands on the floor wearing a hat and shoes. Which of the two is nearest the ceiling?', '["The shoes", "They are the same distance", "The hat", "Neither"]', 2, 'The hat is on his head, which is high up. The shoes are on his feet at the bottom.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Shapes are in a row: square, circle, triangle, square, circle, triangle, square. What comes next?', '["Triangle", "Square", "Star", "Circle"]', 3, 'The pattern repeats square, circle, triangle. After a square comes a circle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A pattern of dots grows: 1 dot, then 3 dots, then 5 dots. How many dots come next?', '["6", "7", "8", "9"]', 1, 'Each picture has 2 more dots than the one before. 5 + 2 = 7.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A path goes: right, right, up, right, right, up, right, right. What is the next step?', '["Up", "Right", "Down", "Left"]', 0, 'The pattern is two rights then an up. After two rights comes up.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Four identical squares are put together in a 2 by 2 block. What shape do they make?', '["A triangle", "A long thin rectangle", "A bigger square", "A circle"]', 2, 'Two rows of two squares make a shape with equal width and height, so a bigger square.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A rectangle is twice as long as it is wide. You cut it in half across the middle. What shape is each piece?', '["A triangle", "A circle", "A longer rectangle", "A square"]', 3, 'Halving the long side gives pieces whose length equals their width, so squares.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A shape has more sides than a pentagon, fewer sides than an octagon, and it is not a hexagon. How many sides does it have?', '["6", "7", "8", "5"]', 1, 'More than 5 and fewer than 8 leaves 6 or 7. It is not a hexagon (6), so it has 7 sides.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Hana counts 12 corners on three identical shapes. How many corners does each shape have?', '["3", "6", "4", "12"]', 2, 'Share 12 corners among 3 shapes: 12 divided by 3 is 4 corners each.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which shape has more sides than a triangle but fewer corners than a pentagon?', '["Square", "Triangle", "Pentagon", "Hexagon"]', 0, 'A square has 4 sides, which is more than 3, and 4 corners, which is fewer than 5.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these is true for both a square and a rectangle?', '["Both have 3 corners", "Both have all sides equal", "Both have 6 sides", "Both have 4 square corners"]', 3, 'Squares and rectangles both have 4 sides and 4 square corners. Only the square has every side equal.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these 3D shapes has only flat faces and no curved surface?', '["Cone", "Cylinder", "Sphere", "Cube"]', 3, 'A cube has 6 flat square faces. The cone, cylinder and sphere all have a curved surface.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The flat face on the bottom of a cone is what shape?', '["A square", "A triangle", "A circle", "A rectangle"]', 2, 'A cone stands on a round flat base, so its flat face is a circle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'How many flat faces does a sphere have?', '["1", "0", "2", "6"]', 1, 'A sphere is round all over, so it has no flat faces at all.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these has 6 faces that are all exactly the same size and shape?', '["A cube", "A long thin box", "A cylinder", "A cone"]', 0, 'A cube has 6 identical squares. A long thin box has faces of different sizes.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You face North and make three quarter turns to the right, one after another. Which way do you face at the end?', '["West", "East", "South", "North"]', 0, 'Right from North is East, then South, then West.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which direction is exactly opposite to North-East?', '["South-East", "South-West", "North-West", "North-East"]', 1, 'Opposite directions point in exactly the other way, so the opposite of North-East is South-West.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The wind is blowing from the North. Which way is the air moving toward?', '["North", "East", "West", "South"]', 3, 'Wind that comes from the North blows toward the South.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A weather vane arrow points East. It turns a quarter turn clockwise. Where does it point now?', '["North", "West", "South", "East"]', 2, 'Clockwise from East is South.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Priya''s map shows the beach South of the cafe, and the cafe South of the hill. Which place is farthest North?', '["The cafe", "The hill", "The beach", "They are all level"]', 1, 'The order from North to South is hill, cafe, beach. So the hill is farthest North.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A hiker walks 3 km North, then 4 km East, then 3 km South. Where is she compared with her start?', '["3 km North of the start", "10 km from the start, going North", "4 km East of the start", "Back at the start"]', 2, 'The North and South parts cancel out. That leaves only the 4 km she walked East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Ben''s map has North at the top. He puts a red pin at the top-right corner. Which direction is the pin from the middle of the map?', '["North-East", "South-West", "North-West", "South-East"]', 0, 'Up is North and right is East, so the top-right corner is North-East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'From the school, the park is 2 blocks North and the pool is 2 blocks South. Which direction is the pool from the park?', '["North", "East", "West", "South"]', 3, 'The park is North of the school and the pool is South of it. So from the park you go South to reach the pool.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Hakim walks home and his house is on the right side of the street. On the way back the other way, which side of the street is the house on?', '["On his right", "On his left", "Straight ahead", "Behind him"]', 1, 'Turning around swaps sides. What was on his right is now on his left.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Three friends sit in a row on a sofa, all facing the TV: Hugo, Zoe and Ali. Ali sits on Hugo''s right, and Zoe sits on Ali''s right. Who is in the middle?', '["Ali", "Hugo", "Zoe", "Nobody"]', 0, 'The order from left to right is Hugo, Ali, Zoe, so Ali is in the middle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'When you read English words on a line, which way do your eyes move across the page?', '["From right to left", "From top to bottom only", "From bottom to top", "From left to right"]', 3, 'English is read from the left side of the page toward the right side.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A car''s blinking light on the left side means the driver is about to turn which way?', '["Right", "Around in a circle", "Left", "Up"]', 2, 'The blinking light is on the side the car is planning to turn toward.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Three books are stacked: the maths book is on top of the art book, and the art book is on top of the story book. Which book is at the bottom?', '["The maths book", "The art book", "They are side by side", "The story book"]', 3, 'The order from the top is maths, art, story. The story book is at the bottom.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Lockers are numbered from left to right. Locker 5 is between locker 4 and locker 6. Which locker is just to the right of locker 6?', '["Locker 5", "Locker 4", "Locker 7", "Locker 3"]', 2, 'Numbers grow going to the right, so the next locker after 6 is locker 7.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The moon is above a hill, and the hill is above a river in a picture. Which one is lowest?', '["The moon", "The river", "The hill", "They are all level"]', 1, 'From the top: moon, hill, river. The river is at the bottom.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A lift starts on floor 2 and goes up 2 floors. Which floor is it on now?', '["Floor 4", "Floor 3", "Floor 2", "Floor 0"]', 0, 'Going up 2 floors from floor 2 gives floor 4.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Fatima is 3rd from the front and 3rd from the back of a line. How many people are in the line?', '["6", "5", "3", "7"]', 1, 'There are 2 people ahead of her and 2 behind her, plus Fatima. 2 + 2 + 1 = 5.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Four monkeys sit in a line on a branch. Max is 2nd from the left. Which place is he counting from the right?', '["3rd", "2nd", "4th", "1st"]', 0, 'There are 4 monkeys. The one that is 2nd from the left has 2 monkeys on his right side. That makes him 3rd from the right.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The bus seats are numbered from the front, 1 to 10. You sit in seat 6. How many seats are in front of you?', '["6", "4", "10", "5"]', 3, 'Seats 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 are in front of seat 6. That is 5 seats.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Four ducks walk in a line. The first duck is at the front and the fourth duck is at the back. How many ducks are between the first and the fourth duck?', '["1", "2", "3", "4"]', 1, 'Only the 2nd and 3rd ducks are between the first and the fourth, so there are 2 ducks.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A counter starts on a square. It moves 2 squares right, 1 square up and then 2 squares left. Where is it now compared with its start?', '["1 square below the start", "1 square above the start", "2 squares right of the start", "Back on the start"]', 1, 'Right and left cancel out. The one move up leaves it 1 square above the start.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A mouse starts in the top-right corner of a 4 by 4 grid. It runs 3 squares left and then 3 squares down. Which corner is it in?', '["Bottom-left", "Bottom-right", "Top-left", "Top-right"]', 0, 'Left 3 takes it to the left edge and down 3 takes it to the bottom edge. That is the bottom-left corner.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You start facing North. You walk 2 steps forward, turn right and walk 1 step, turn right again and walk 2 steps. Where are you compared with your start?', '["1 step West of the start", "2 steps South of the start", "Back at the start", "1 step East of the start"]', 3, 'Two steps North, one East, then two steps South (after turning right twice). You are level with the start but 1 step East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A dot is in column 3, row 2 of a grid (rows are counted up from the bottom). It moves 2 columns right and 1 row up. Where is it now?', '["Column 4, row 3", "Column 5, row 1", "Column 5, row 3", "Column 1, row 3"]', 2, '3 + 2 = column 5 and 2 + 1 = row 3.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A robot faces East. It is told: turn left, then walk 2 steps. Which direction does it walk?', '["South", "East", "West", "North"]', 3, 'Facing East, a left turn points you North. So it walks 2 steps North.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You hold a page with the word CAT up to a mirror. How does the word look in the mirror?', '["The same as on the page", "Upside down", "Backwards, flipped left to right", "Some letters are missing"]', 2, 'A mirror flips left and right, so the letters come out backwards.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A duck floats on calm water. Where does its reflection appear?', '["Above the duck", "Below the duck, upside down", "Beside the duck", "Inside the duck"]', 1, 'The water acts like a mirror lying down, so the reflection is below the duck and upside down.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which two letters are mirror images of each other, one flipped left to right from the other?', '["p and q", "n and u", "m and w", "O and Q"]', 0, 'Flip a p from left to right and you get a q. The others are not left-right mirror images.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You face North, turn a half turn, and then a quarter turn to the right. Which way do you face at the end?', '["West", "East", "South", "North"]', 0, 'A half turn from North points South. A quarter turn right from South is West.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A toy compass needle points West. You turn it a quarter turn anticlockwise, the opposite way to clock hands. Where does it point now?', '["North", "East", "South", "West"]', 2, 'Anticlockwise goes North, West, South, East. So after West comes South.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The small letter b is turned a half turn (upside down). Which letter does it look like now?', '["d", "p", "b", "q"]', 3, 'Turned upside down, the b has its round part on the left and its long stem on the right reaching down. That is a q.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A card shows the number 6. You turn the card a half turn. Which number does it look like now?', '["6", "9", "8", "0"]', 1, 'Upside down, the round part of the 6 ends up at the top and the tail at the bottom, so it looks like a 9.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A shape is drawn on one side of a fold line. To make a symmetrical picture, where does the matching half go?', '["On the same side", "On the other side, as a mirror image", "On top of the first half", "Anywhere on the page"]', 1, 'In a symmetrical picture, the second half is the mirror image on the other side of the line.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these capital letters has a line of symmetry down the middle?', '["G", "J", "W", "S"]', 2, 'The left and right halves of W match. G, J and S do not.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these has no line of symmetry: a circle, a square, a rectangle, or a lopsided blob whose two sides look different?', '["The lopsided blob", "The circle", "The square", "The rectangle"]', 0, 'A circle, square and rectangle can all be folded so the halves match. A lopsided blob cannot.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The capital letter V is folded down the middle from top to bottom. What happens?', '["One side sticks out more", "It turns into a Y", "It turns into an A", "The two sides match"]', 3, 'The two arms of a V are the same, so folding it in half makes matching sides.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You fold a piece of paper in half 3 times. How many layers are stacked up?', '["8", "6", "3", "4"]', 0, 'Each fold doubles the layers: 2, then 4, then 8.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A paper is folded in half, and a hole is punched close to the fold through both layers. When you unfold it, where are the two holes?', '["Both on the same side", "Both on the crease", "On each side of the crease, the same distance from it", "One hole only"]', 2, 'Each layer gets a hole. The two holes match up across the crease like a mirror.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Ali wants to cut a paper strip into 3 equal pieces with straight cuts. How many cuts does he need?', '["3", "2", "1", "4"]', 1, 'One cut makes 2 pieces and a second cut makes 3 pieces.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Three towers of blocks stand side by side. They are 2 blocks, 3 blocks and 4 blocks tall. How many blocks are there in all?', '["8", "10", "24", "9"]', 3, 'Add them up: 2 + 3 + 4 = 9.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A floor is covered by 3 rows of 3 blocks. Two more blocks are stacked on top of the middle block. How many blocks are there?', '["9", "11", "12", "10"]', 1, 'The floor has 3 x 3 = 9 blocks. Add 2 more on top: 9 + 2 = 11.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A big cube is built from blocks and is 3 blocks wide, 3 blocks long and 3 blocks tall. How many blocks are in its top layer?', '["3", "6", "9", "27"]', 2, 'Each layer is 3 rows of 3 blocks, which is 9 blocks.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Nina has 15 blocks. She builds a staircase with steps of 1, 2, 3 and 4 blocks. How many blocks are left over?', '["5", "10", "4", "6"]', 0, 'The staircase uses 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10 blocks. 15 - 10 = 5 are left.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A tower has 8 blocks stacked up, and each block is 2 cm tall. How tall is the tower?', '["10 cm", "8 cm", "20 cm", "16 cm"]', 3, '8 blocks of 2 cm each is 8 x 2 = 16 cm.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which everyday object has the shape of a cone?', '["An ice-cream cone", "A brick", "A marble", "A juice can"]', 0, 'An ice-cream cone has a round opening and narrows to a point, just like a cone.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which everyday object is shaped like a cube?', '["A pencil", "A football", "A sugar cube", "A funnel"]', 2, 'A sugar cube has 6 equal square faces.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A sheet of writing paper is closest to which flat shape?', '["A circle", "A rectangle", "A triangle", "A hexagon"]', 1, 'Writing paper has 4 square corners with long and short sides, so it is a rectangle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The minute hand moves from the 12 to the 3. How much of a full turn around the clock is that?', '["A half", "Three quarters", "A full turn", "A quarter"]', 3, 'From 12 to 3 is one quarter of the way around the clock face.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The minute hand starts at the 12, goes all the way around and comes back to the 12. How many minutes have passed?', '["30", "12", "24", "60"]', 3, 'One full trip around by the minute hand takes 60 minutes, or 1 hour.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'At 12:30, which way does the minute hand point?', '["Straight down", "Straight up", "To the right", "To the left"]', 0, 'Half past means the minute hand is at the 6, which is straight down.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which number is directly opposite the 12 on a clock face?', '["3", "6", "9", "1"]', 1, 'The 12 is at the top and the 6 is at the bottom, straight across from it.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which ribbon is the shortest: 30 cm, 3 m, 25 cm or 2 m?', '["30 cm", "2 m", "25 cm", "3 m"]', 2, 'A metre is 100 cm. 25 cm is shorter than 30 cm and much shorter than 2 m or 3 m.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A parking spot is 3 metres wide. Each car is 2 metres wide. Can two cars fit side by side in one spot?', '["No, they are too wide together", "Yes, with room to spare", "Yes, exactly", "Only if the cars are small"]', 0, 'Two cars would be 2 + 2 = 4 metres wide, which is wider than 3 metres.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these can hold the most water: a teaspoon, a mug, a bathtub or a thimble?', '["A mug", "A teaspoon", "A thimble", "A bathtub"]', 3, 'A bathtub is much bigger than the others, so it holds the most.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A cat hides in the gap between a sofa and the wall. Where is the cat compared with the sofa?', '["On top of the sofa", "In front of the sofa", "Behind the sofa", "Inside the sofa"]', 2, 'The gap between the sofa and the wall is at the back of the sofa.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Mira slides her toy car under the bed. Which of these is above the toy car?', '["The floor", "The bed", "The wall", "Nothing"]', 1, 'Under the bed means the bed is over the car, directly above it.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Three animals sit in a straight row in this order: cat, dog, mouse. Is the cat next to the mouse?', '["Yes, they touch", "Yes, the cat is beside the mouse", "No, the dog is between them", "It cannot be known"]', 2, 'The dog is in the middle, so the cat and mouse are at the two ends with the dog between.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A pattern of stars: row 1 has 2 stars, row 2 has 4 stars, row 3 has 6 stars. How many stars are in row 4?', '["8", "7", "9", "10"]', 0, 'Each row has 2 more stars than the one before. 6 + 2 = 8.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Floor tiles go black, white, black, white and so on. What colour is the 7th tile?', '["White", "Grey", "It cannot be told", "Black"]', 3, 'Odd-numbered tiles (1st, 3rd, 5th, 7th) are black.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A pattern goes: circle, circle, square, circle, circle, square, and so on. What is the 9th shape?', '["Circle", "Square", "Triangle", "Star"]', 1, 'Every third shape is a square: the 3rd, 6th and 9th.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A rectangle is cut from one corner straight to the opposite corner. What do you get?', '["2 triangles", "2 squares", "2 circles", "3 rectangles"]', 0, 'A cut from corner to corner splits the rectangle into two triangles.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You cut off one corner of a square with a single straight cut. How many sides does the new shape have?', '["3", "5", "4", "6"]', 1, 'The cut adds a new side and the other 4 sides stay (two of them get shorter). That makes 5 sides.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Tia joins 3 dots that are not in a straight line using straight lines. Which shape does she draw?', '["Triangle", "Square", "Circle", "Rectangle"]', 0, 'Three dots joined by three straight lines make a shape with 3 sides and 3 corners, a triangle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A triangle and one other flat shape have 7 corners in total. Which is the other shape?', '["Pentagon", "Hexagon", "Square", "Circle"]', 2, 'A triangle has 3 corners. 7 - 3 = 4, and a square has 4 corners.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Anna draws a hexagon and Ben draws a pentagon. Whose shape has more corners, and by how many?', '["Ben''s, by 1", "Anna''s, by 2", "They have the same number", "Anna''s, by 1"]', 3, 'A hexagon has 6 corners and a pentagon has 5. So Anna''s shape has 1 more.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'One long side of a rectangle is 6 cm. How long is the opposite long side?', '["3 cm", "6 cm", "12 cm", "It cannot be told"]', 1, 'The two long sides of a rectangle are always equal, so the opposite side is also 6 cm.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which 3D shape looks like a circle when seen from above and like a rectangle when seen from the side?', '["A cone", "A cube", "A cylinder standing upright", "A pyramid"]', 2, 'Standing up, a can shows a round top and a rectangle from the side. A cone shows a triangle from the side.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Whichever side you look at a ball from, what flat shape does it look like?', '["A circle", "A square", "A triangle", "A rectangle"]', 0, 'A ball is round in every direction, so it always looks like a circle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Where do all four sloping sides of a square pyramid come together?', '["In the middle of the base", "At the four bottom corners", "They never meet", "At the top point"]', 3, 'Every sloping triangle leans in toward the top, and they all meet at the pointed tip.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A cardboard tube is cut straight across, in a line at a right angle to its length. What shape is the cut end?', '["A square", "A circle", "A triangle", "A rectangle"]', 1, 'The tube is a cylinder, and a straight cut across a cylinder makes a circle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You face North. Which side of you is East on?', '["Your left side", "Behind you", "In front of you", "Your right side"]', 3, 'When you face North, East is on your right hand side.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You are facing South. Which direction is on your left?', '["West", "North", "East", "South"]', 2, 'Facing South, your left hand points East and your right hand points West.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A ship is heading West. Which direction is the back of the ship pointing?', '["West", "East", "North", "South"]', 1, 'The back of the ship points the opposite way to where it is heading, which is East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You are facing East and you turn to face North. Was that a quarter turn to the left or to the right?', '["A quarter turn to the left", "A quarter turn to the right", "A half turn", "A full turn"]', 0, 'Turning left from East takes you to North.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'On a map, a fox is North of a rabbit, and the rabbit is North of a mouse. Which direction is the mouse from the fox?', '["North", "East", "West", "South"]', 3, 'The mouse is farther South than both of them, so it is South of the fox.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A park map has North at the top. The pond is in the middle, the swings are on the East side and the slide is on the West side. Which is on the right of the pond?', '["The slide", "Both", "The swings", "Neither"]', 2, 'On a map with North at the top, East is on the right, so the swings are on the right.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Zara walks 5 steps West and then 2 steps North. Which direction is her starting point from where she stands now?', '["South-East", "North-West", "South-West", "North-East"]', 0, 'She went West and then North, so to go back she must go East and South. That is South-East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A museum is directly West of the library, and the zoo is directly East of the library. Walking from the museum to the zoo, which direction do you go?', '["West", "East", "North", "South"]', 1, 'The order from West to East is museum, library, zoo, so you walk East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Sunil faces East. He turns left, then left again, and then right. Which way does he face now?', '["South", "East", "West", "North"]', 3, 'Left from East is North, left again is West, and then right from West is North.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Three flags stand in a line in front of you: red on your left, blue in the middle, green on your right. You walk around to the other side and face them again. Which flag is on your right now?', '["Blue", "Red", "Green", "None of them"]', 1, 'Seen from the opposite side, left and right swap, so the red flag is now on your right.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Two kids stand back to back. One is facing North. Which way is the other facing?', '["North", "East", "South", "West"]', 2, 'Standing back to back means they face opposite ways. The opposite of North is South.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Lola is walking East and the sea is on her right side. In which direction is the sea?', '["South", "North", "East", "West"]', 0, 'When you walk East, your right side is South. The sea is to the South.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A cupboard has 4 shelves counted from the bottom (1) to the top (4). A jar sits on shelf 2. Where is it compared with a box on shelf 3?', '["Above the box", "Level with the box", "Beside the box", "Below the box"]', 3, 'Shelf 2 is under shelf 3, so the jar is below the box.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A ship floats on the sea, a submarine is deep under it, and a fish swims between them. Which one is in the middle in height?', '["The ship", "The fish", "The submarine", "They are all level"]', 1, 'The ship is highest and the submarine is lowest. The fish is between them.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You are on step 4 of a staircase and you walk down 3 steps. Which step are you on now?', '["Step 1", "Step 2", "Step 3", "Step 7"]', 0, '4 - 3 = 1, so you are on step 1.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'In Ana''s bedroom the bed is against the North wall and the desk is against the opposite wall. Which wall is the desk against?', '["The East wall", "The West wall", "The South wall", "The North wall"]', 2, 'The wall opposite the North wall is the South wall.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Tom is 1st in a line of 9 children and Uma is at the very end. How many children stand between them?', '["8", "6", "9", "7"]', 3, 'Take away Tom and Uma from the 9 children. 9 - 2 = 7 stand between them.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'In a race, gold is for 1st, silver is for 2nd and bronze is for 3rd. Which medal goes to the runner who finished second?', '["Gold", "Silver", "Bronze", "None"]', 1, 'Second place gets the silver medal.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A cinema row has 6 seats. Kai sits in the 2nd seat from the left and Lin sits in the 2nd seat from the right. How many seats are between them?', '["1", "3", "2", "4"]', 2, 'Kai is in seat 2 and Lin is in seat 5. Seats 3 and 4 are between them.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Four children finish a race. Jo is 1st, and Mia finishes 2 places behind Jo. What place is Mia?', '["3rd", "2nd", "4th", "1st"]', 0, 'Two places behind 1st is 3rd.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A bug starts in the middle square of a 3 by 3 grid. It moves up 1 square and then right 1 square. Which square is it on?', '["The top-right corner", "The top-left corner", "The bottom-right corner", "The middle"]', 0, 'Up 1 puts it on the top edge, and right 1 puts it in the far right. That is the top-right corner.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You start facing North. You turn left, walk 3 steps, turn left again and walk 3 more steps. Which way are you facing at the end?', '["North", "East", "West", "South"]', 3, 'The first left turn points you West and the second left turn points you South.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A robot walks forward 2 steps, turns around completely to face the other way, and then walks forward 2 steps. Where does it end up?', '["2 steps from the start", "Back at the start", "4 steps from the start", "It cannot be told"]', 1, 'The second walk goes the opposite way, so it exactly cancels the first walk.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Leo''s goal star is 3 squares to the right and 2 squares up from him on a grid. Which moves will get him there?', '["Right 2, up 3", "Left 3, up 2", "Right 3, up 2", "Right 3, down 2"]', 2, 'The star is 3 squares right and 2 squares up, so he moves right 3 and up 2.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A frog jumps 2 squares to the right every time. How many jumps does it take to move 8 squares to the right?', '["4", "2", "6", "8"]', 0, 'Each jump is 2 squares, and 4 jumps of 2 make 8.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Ali holds up 3 fingers to a mirror. How many fingers does his reflection show?', '["2", "6", "0", "3"]', 3, 'A mirror only flips left and right. It does not change how many fingers there are.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these looks exactly the same when reflected in a mirror placed to its side?', '["An arrow pointing right", "An arrow pointing up", "Both of them", "Neither of them"]', 1, 'A mirror at the side flips left and right. An arrow pointing right would turn to point left, but an up arrow stays the same.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A flag has a red stripe on its left half and a blue stripe on its right half. You see it reflected in a mirror beside it. What does the reflection show?', '["Red on the left, blue on the right", "Both halves red", "Blue on the left, red on the right", "Both halves blue"]', 2, 'A mirror flips left and right, so the two colours swap sides.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A plus sign (+) is given a quarter turn. What does it look like now?', '["A minus sign", "Still a plus sign", "A cross like an X", "A circle"]', 1, 'A plus sign has 4 matching arms, so a quarter turn puts each arm where another one was.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The capital letter N is turned a quarter turn. Which letter does it look like?', '["M", "W", "H", "Z"]', 3, 'Lying on its side, the N has a slanted stroke between two parallel lines, just like a Z.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which capital letter looks exactly the same after a half turn (turning it upside down)?', '["O", "L", "F", "P"]', 0, 'The O is round all over, so upside down it is still an O. L, F and P change.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You face East and turn all the way around in a full turn. Which way do you face at the end?', '["West", "North", "East", "South"]', 2, 'A full turn brings you back to exactly where you started, facing East.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A house is drawn from the front with a door in the middle and identical windows on each side. Does it have a line of symmetry down the middle?', '["No", "Yes", "Only the roof does", "Only the door does"]', 1, 'The left half and right half are the same, so folding down the middle makes them match.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You fold a paper in half, draw half a heart with its middle on the fold, cut it out and unfold it. What do you get?', '["Half a heart", "A circle", "A whole heart", "Two hearts"]', 2, 'The fold is the line of symmetry, so the cut-out opens up into a full heart shape.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these has exactly one line of symmetry?', '["A circle", "A square", "A plus sign", "A butterfly"]', 3, 'A butterfly has one fold down the middle. A square and a plus sign have 4 and a circle has many.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which digit has a left half that matches its right half when folded down the middle from top to bottom?', '["8", "2", "4", "7"]', 0, 'The two sides of an 8 are the same. 2, 4 and 7 do not match that way.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You fold a paper in half so that the two halves match exactly. What do we call the crease line?', '["A corner", "A circle", "A curve", "A line of symmetry"]', 3, 'A fold that makes two matching halves is called a line of symmetry.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'You fold a letter into thirds so it fits in an envelope. How many equal sections does the paper have?', '["3", "2", "4", "6"]', 0, 'Folding into thirds gives 3 equal sections.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A sheet of paper is folded in half. Compared with the unfolded sheet, how big is the folded paper?', '["The same size", "Half the size", "Twice the size", "A quarter of the size"]', 1, 'Folding in half puts one half over the other, so it covers half the space.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A 2 by 2 by 2 cube is built from blocks and sits on a table. How many blocks can you see when you look straight down on it?', '["2", "8", "4", "6"]', 2, 'From above you see only the top layer, which is 2 x 2 = 4 blocks.'),
(1, 'spatial', '12 blocks are shared into 3 towers of the same height. How many blocks are in each tower?', '["4", "3", "6", "9"]', 0, '12 shared equally between 3 towers is 4 blocks each.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A block pyramid has a bottom row of 4 blocks, then rows of 3, 2 and 1 blocks above. How many blocks are there in all?', '["9", "10", "8", "12"]', 1, 'Add up the rows: 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 10.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Sofia builds a wall with 3 rows of 5 blocks. She takes away 2 blocks. How many blocks are left?', '["15", "12", "10", "13"]', 3, 'The wall has 3 x 5 = 15 blocks. After taking 2 away, 13 are left.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A tower has a red block at the bottom, then a blue block, then a green block, then a yellow block on top. Which colour is second from the bottom?', '["Red", "Green", "Blue", "Yellow"]', 2, 'From the bottom the order is red, blue, green, yellow. Blue is second.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Looking at a bicycle from the side, each wheel looks like which flat shape?', '["A square", "A triangle", "A circle", "A rectangle"]', 2, 'A wheel is round, so from the side it looks like a circle.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Which of these is NOT round like a sphere?', '["A brick", "An orange", "A marble", "A beach ball"]', 0, 'An orange, a marble and a beach ball are all ball-shaped. A brick is a box shape.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A pizza is round. Seen from above, its box is usually which flat shape?', '["A circle", "A square", "A triangle", "An oval"]', 1, 'Pizza boxes are made of flat cardboard folded into a square shape.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'It is 15 minutes to 6. Which number does the minute hand point at?', '["3", "6", "12", "9"]', 3, '15 minutes to the hour means 45 minutes past, and 45 minutes is the number 9.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The minute hand points at the 2. How many minutes past the hour is it?', '["2", "12", "20", "10"]', 3, 'Each number on the clock is 5 minutes. 2 x 5 = 10 minutes.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'On a clock face, which number is on the far right side?', '["3", "9", "6", "12"]', 0, 'The 12 is at the top, the 6 at the bottom, the 9 on the left and the 3 on the right.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'On most clocks, which hand is longer?', '["The hour hand", "The minute hand", "They are the same length", "It depends on the time"]', 1, 'The minute hand travels farther around the face, so it is the longer hand.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A shelf is 30 cm wide. Three stuffed animals, each 12 cm wide, are put on it side by side. Will they all fit?', '["Yes, they take up 24 cm", "Yes, exactly", "No, they take up 36 cm", "Only if they are squashed"]', 2, '3 x 12 = 36 cm, which is wider than the 30 cm shelf.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A suitcase is 60 cm long. The car trunk is 1 metre long. Does the suitcase fit lengthways?', '["No, the suitcase is longer", "They are the same length", "It cannot be told", "Yes, the trunk is longer"]', 3, '1 metre is 100 cm, and 60 cm is less than 100 cm, so it fits.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Box A fits inside box B, and box B fits inside box C. Which box is the smallest?', '["Box A", "Box B", "Box C", "They are all the same"]', 0, 'The box that fits inside the others is the smallest, which is box A.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Sam puts a coin in a jar, then puts the jar in a box, and then puts the box in a bag. Which of these holds all the others?', '["The box", "The jar", "The bag", "The coin"]', 2, 'The coin is inside the jar, the jar is inside the box, and the box is inside the bag. So the bag holds everything.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'The cat sits on a mat, and the mat lies on the floor. What is between the cat and the floor?', '["The wall", "The mat", "The table", "Nothing"]', 1, 'The cat is on the mat and the mat is on the floor, so the mat is in between.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'In a classroom, Nora sits at the back and Ivo sits at the front next to the whiteboard. Who is farther from the whiteboard?', '["Ivo", "They are the same distance", "Nora", "It cannot be told"]', 2, 'Ivo is right beside the whiteboard, and Nora is at the other end of the room.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Beads are threaded in a repeating pattern: red, blue, green, red, blue, green, and so on. What colour is the 10th bead?', '["Blue", "Red", "Green", "Yellow"]', 1, 'The reds are the 1st, 4th, 7th and 10th beads.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A path goes: right 1, up 1, right 2, up 2, right 3, up 3. What is the next move?', '["Up 4", "Right 3", "Left 4", "Right 4"]', 3, 'The moves grow by one each time, going right then up, so right 4 is next.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'Shapes are drawn with one more side each time: triangle, square, pentagon, and then? What comes next?', '["Hexagon", "Octagon", "Circle", "Triangle"]', 0, 'The sides go 3, 4, 5, so the next shape has 6 sides, a hexagon.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A square sheet of paper is folded exactly in half, and then it is cut along the fold. How many pieces of paper are there?', '["1", "2", "3", "4"]', 1, 'Cutting along the fold splits the paper into 2 equal pieces.'),
(1, 'spatial', 'A round pizza is cut into equal slices by straight cuts that all pass through the middle. How many cuts are needed to make 6 equal slices?', '["2", "4", "6", "3"]', 3, 'Each cut through the middle makes 2 slices. 3 cuts make 6 slices.');
insert into questions (level, category, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanation) values
(2, 'logic', 'Five kids ran a race with no ties. Ana beat Ben but lost to Chen. Dia beat Chen. Eli lost to Ben. Who finished 2nd?', '["Ana", "Dia", "Chen", "Ben"]', 2, 'The finishing order was Dia, Chen, Ana, Ben, Eli. Chen came 2nd.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Four blocks are stacked in a tower. Green is above red. Blue is below red. Yellow is above green. Which block is second from the bottom?', '["Green", "Red", "Blue", "Yellow"]', 1, 'From top to bottom the tower is yellow, green, red, blue. The second one up from the bottom is red.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Tom has more stickers than Uma. Vik has fewer stickers than Uma. Wes has more stickers than Tom. Who has the fewest stickers?', '["Uma", "Tom", "Wes", "Vik"]', 3, 'Ordering from most to fewest gives Wes, Tom, Uma, Vik. Vik is at the end.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Red is heavier than Blue. Green is lighter than Blue. Yellow is heavier than Red. If the lightest backpack is taken away, which of the rest is now the lightest?', '["Blue", "Red", "Yellow", "Green"]', 0, 'Heaviest to lightest is Yellow, Red, Blue, Green. Green is taken away, so Blue becomes the lightest.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Five kids compare heights. Mia is the 3rd tallest. Leo is taller than Mia but shorter than exactly one other kid. Where does Leo rank, counting from the tallest?', '["1st", "2nd", "4th", "5th"]', 1, 'Leo is taller than Mia, so he is 1st or 2nd. Being shorter than exactly one kid means only one kid is above him, so he is 2nd.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Peak A is higher than Peak C. Peak B is lower than Peak C. Peak D is higher than Peak A. Which list goes from highest to lowest?', '["D, A, C, B", "A, D, C, B", "D, A, B, C", "D, C, A, B"]', 0, 'D is above A, A is above C, and C is above B. So the order is D, A, C, B.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 3, 4, 6, 9, 13, ___?', '["17", "19", "20", "18"]', 3, 'The gaps grow by 1 each time (1, 2, 3, 4), so the next gap is 5. 13 + 5 = 18.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 2, 3, 5, 9, 17, ___?', '["25", "31", "33", "34"]', 2, 'Each number is double the one before, minus 1. So 17 x 2 - 1 = 33.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 81, 27, 9, 3, ___?', '["1", "0", "2", "6"]', 0, 'Each number is divided by 3 to get the next. 3 divided by 3 is 1.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 5, 10, 7, 14, 11, 22, ___?', '["25", "44", "19", "18"]', 2, 'The rule alternates: double, then subtract 3. After 22 comes 22 - 3 = 19.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 1, 10, 2, 20, 3, 30, ___?', '["40", "5", "31", "4"]', 3, 'Two patterns are woven together: 1, 2, 3 and 10, 20, 30. After 30 it is the turn of the first pattern, giving 4.'),
(2, 'logic', 'One of three kids broke a vase. Ana says, "Ben did it." Ben says, "I did not do it." Cy says, "Ana is lying." Only ONE statement is true. Who broke the vase?', '["Ana", "Ben", "Cy", "It cannot be worked out"]', 1, 'If Ben did it, only Ana''s statement is true. If Ana or Cy did it, both Ben''s and Cy''s statements would be true, which is too many.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every statement Dara makes is false. Dara says, "I have a cat and a dog." Which must be true?', '["Dara has neither a cat nor a dog", "Dara has a cat but no dog", "Dara does not have both a cat and a dog", "Dara has a dog but no cat"]', 2, 'For "cat and dog" to be false, at least one animal is missing. We cannot tell which, so only "not both" is certain.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A prize is in one of three boxes. Box 1 says, "The prize is here." Box 2 says, "The prize is not here." Box 3 says, "The prize is not in Box 1." Only one label is true. Where is the prize?', '["Box 1", "Box 2", "Box 3", "It cannot be worked out"]', 1, 'If it were in Box 1, two labels would be true; in Box 3, two would be true. In Box 2, only Box 3''s label is true, which fits.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Yara always tells the truth and Zed always lies. One of them says, "We are both liars." Who said it?', '["Zed", "Yara", "Either of them", "Neither of them"]', 0, 'Yara can never say something false, and that sentence is false for her. Zed can say it, because it is untrue since Yara is honest.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Kids are either honest (always true) or fibbers (always lie). Beth says, "Ravi is a fibber." Ravi says, "Beth and I are the same type." What is Ravi?', '["Honest", "Could be either", "Not enough information", "A fibber"]', 3, 'If Beth were a fibber, Ravi would be honest, but then his statement would be false. That cannot happen, so Beth is honest and Ravi is a fibber.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Eight kids sit at a round table in seats numbered 1 to 8 in order around the table. Zoe is in seat 3. Kim sits directly across from Zoe. Which seat is Kim in?', '["Seat 5", "Seat 6", "Seat 7", "Seat 8"]', 2, 'Directly across is halfway around, which is 4 seats away. 3 + 4 = 7.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ivy is in a line. She has 4 kids in front of her and 6 kids behind her. How many kids are in the line?', '["10", "11", "12", "9"]', 1, 'Count the 4 in front, the 6 behind, and Ivy herself: 4 + 6 + 1 = 11.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A line has 12 kids. Lola is 3rd from the front and Max is 4th from the back. How many kids stand between them?', '["5", "4", "6", "7"]', 0, 'Max is 12 - 4 + 1 = 9th from the front. The kids between 3rd and 9th are in places 4 to 8, which is 5 kids.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Al, Bea, Cy and Di sit on a bench. Cy is at the left end. Di sits right next to Cy. Bea does not sit next to Di. Who sits at the right end?', '["Al", "Cy", "Di", "Bea"]', 3, 'Cy is 1st and Di is 2nd. Bea cannot be 3rd (next to Di), so Bea is 4th, at the right end, and Al is 3rd.'),
(2, 'logic', 'No bird in the zoo is a mammal. All the penguins in the zoo are birds. Which statement must be true?', '["No penguin in the zoo is a mammal", "Some penguins in the zoo are mammals", "All birds in the zoo are penguins", "All mammals in the zoo are birds"]', 0, 'Penguins are birds, and no bird in the zoo is a mammal. So no penguin there can be a mammal.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every spider has 8 legs. Zia finds a creature with 8 legs. Is it definitely a spider?', '["Yes, every 8-legged creature is a spider", "Yes, but only if it is small", "No, other creatures can have 8 legs too", "No, because spiders have 6 legs"]', 2, 'The rule says spiders have 8 legs, not that only spiders do. Other animals, such as scorpions, also have 8 legs.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every member of the chess club is in Grade 5. Mina is in Grade 4. Can Mina be in the chess club?', '["Yes", "Only on Fridays", "It cannot be told", "No"]', 3, 'Chess club members must all be in Grade 5. Mina is in Grade 4, so she cannot be a member.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every student who passed the test got a sticker. Lucas did not get a sticker. What can we be sure of?', '["Lucas was absent", "Lucas did not pass the test", "Lucas passed the test", "Lucas did not take the test"]', 1, 'If Lucas had passed, he would have got a sticker. He got none, so he did not pass. We cannot tell why.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What letter comes next: A, C, F, J, O, ___?', '["U", "T", "V", "S"]', 0, 'The jumps are 2, 3, 4, 5 letters, so the next jump is 6. O is the 15th letter, and 15 + 6 = 21, which is U.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: AZ, BY, CX, DW, ___?', '["EU", "FV", "DV", "EV"]', 3, 'The first letter moves forward (A, B, C, D, E) and the second moves backward (Z, Y, X, W, V). So the next pair is EV.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which letter is missing: C, F, ___, L, O?', '["H", "J", "I", "K"]', 2, 'The letters skip 2 each time: C, (D, E), F, (G, H), I, (J, K), L, (M, N), O. The missing letter is I.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What letter comes next: O, T, T, F, F, S, S, ___?', '["N", "E", "T", "O"]', 1, 'These are the first letters of the counting words: One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven. Next is Eight, so E.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which word can NOT be made using only the letters of SANDWICH (each letter used once)?', '["WIND", "CHAIN", "DISH", "WHICH"]', 3, 'SANDWICH has only one H, but WHICH needs two H''s. The other three words can all be spelled from its letters.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Lia, Max and Nell each own a different pet: a dog, a rabbit or a parrot. Nell''s pet has feathers. Lia does not own the rabbit. Who owns the dog?', '["Lia", "Max", "Nell", "It cannot be told"]', 0, 'Nell has the parrot. Lia does not have the rabbit, so she has the dog, and Max has the rabbit.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ava, Bo, Cy and Di wear four different colors: red, blue, green, yellow. Bo wears red. Cy wears neither green nor yellow. Di does not wear green. Ava does not wear blue. What does Ava wear?', '["Red", "Green", "Blue", "Yellow"]', 1, 'Cy must wear blue (red is Bo''s). Di is not green, red or blue, so Di wears yellow. That leaves green for Ava.'),
(2, 'logic', 'I am thinking of a number between 10 and 40. It is a multiple of both 3 and 4, and its digits add up to 6. What is it?', '["12", "36", "24", "16"]', 2, 'Multiples of both 3 and 4 in that range are 12, 24 and 36. Only 24 has digits adding to 6 (2 + 4).'),
(2, 'logic', 'A prize is under one of five cups numbered 1 to 5. It is not under the first or last cup, not under a cup next to the last cup, and not under an even-numbered cup. Which cup hides it?', '["Cup 3", "Cup 2", "Cup 4", "Cup 5"]', 0, 'Not first or last leaves 2, 3, 4. Next to the last removes 4, and even-numbered removes 2. Cup 3 is left.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a class of 25 kids, 14 have a dog, 9 have a cat, and 3 have both. How many kids have a dog or a cat (or both)?', '["23", "17", "20", "22"]', 2, '14 + 9 = 23 counts the 3 kids with both twice, so subtract 3 to get 20.'),
(2, 'logic', '12 kids play soccer and 8 kids play tennis. Every tennis player also plays soccer. How many kids play at least one of the two sports?', '["20", "8", "4", "12"]', 3, 'All 8 tennis players are already among the 12 soccer players. So the total stays 12.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Each of 18 kids speaks Spanish, English, or both. 10 speak Spanish and 10 speak English. How many speak both?', '["0", "2", "4", "8"]', 1, '10 + 10 = 20, but there are only 18 kids. The 2 extra counts are kids counted twice, so 2 speak both.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A box holds 10 toys. 6 are red and 5 are cars. What is the smallest possible number of red cars?', '["0", "2", "1", "5"]', 2, '6 + 5 = 11 is more than 10 toys, so at least one toy must be counted as both red and a car.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Today is Thursday. What day of the week will it be 10 days from now?', '["Saturday", "Sunday", "Monday", "Friday"]', 1, '7 days later is Thursday again. 3 more days is Friday, Saturday, Sunday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'School ends at 3:20. Soccer practice starts 1 hour and 25 minutes later. When does practice start?', '["4:35", "4:55", "5:05", "4:45"]', 3, '3:20 plus 1 hour is 4:20, and 25 more minutes makes 4:45.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Nadia''s trip starts on March 25. Her cousin''s party is 12 days after that. What is the date of the party? (March has 31 days.)', '["April 6", "April 5", "April 7", "April 8"]', 0, '6 days after March 25 is March 31. Another 6 days gets to April 6.'),
(2, 'logic', 'The day before yesterday was Sunday. What day will tomorrow be?', '["Tuesday", "Thursday", "Monday", "Wednesday"]', 3, 'Yesterday was Monday, so today is Tuesday, and tomorrow is Wednesday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Bird is to nest as bee is to ___.', '["honey", "flower", "hive", "wing"]', 2, 'A nest is where a bird lives, and a hive is where bees live.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Doctor is to hospital as teacher is to ___.', '["school", "homework", "principal", "pencil"]', 0, 'A doctor works at a hospital. A teacher works at a school.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Second is to minute as minute is to ___.', '["day", "hour", "clock", "watch"]', 1, '60 seconds make a minute, and 60 minutes make an hour.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Sculptor is to statue as author is to ___.', '["book", "library", "pen", "paper"]', 0, 'A sculptor makes statues. An author makes books.'),
(2, 'logic', 'If A=1, B=2, C=3 and so on, what is the total of the letters in the word FED?', '["13", "14", "15", "16"]', 2, 'F is 6, E is 5 and D is 4. 6 + 5 + 4 = 15.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a secret code, each vowel is swapped for the next vowel in the list A, E, I, O, U (and U becomes A). How is MOUSE written?', '["MEASI", "MIASI", "MUESA", "MUASI"]', 3, 'O becomes U, U becomes A, and E becomes I. The consonants M and S stay the same, giving MUASI.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a game, the sign ★ means "add 3" and the sign ● means "double". You start at 4, apply ★ first and then ●. What do you finish with?', '["11", "14", "16", "7"]', 1, '4 + 3 = 7, then doubling 7 gives 14.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a code, CAT is 3, HORSE is 5 and ELEPHANT is 8. What is BUTTERFLY in this code?', '["8", "9", "7", "10"]', 1, 'The code counts the letters in each word. BUTTERFLY has 9 letters.'),
(2, 'logic', 'On a balance scale, 2 apples weigh the same as 1 orange, and 3 oranges weigh the same as 1 melon. How many apples weigh the same as 1 melon?', '["5", "8", "9", "6"]', 3, '1 orange is 2 apples, so 3 oranges are 3 x 2 = 6 apples.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A balance scale has a 5 kg bag and a 2 kg box on the left, and a 4 kg bag on the right. How much more weight must go on the right to balance?', '["2 kg", "4 kg", "3 kg", "7 kg"]', 2, 'The left side weighs 5 + 2 = 7 kg. The right has 4 kg, so it needs 7 - 4 = 3 kg more.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Box X is heavier than Box Y. Box Z is lighter than Box Y. Box W balances perfectly with Box X. Which box is definitely the lightest of the four?', '["Box Z", "Box X", "Box Y", "Box W"]', 0, 'W and X weigh the same, X is heavier than Y, and Y is heavier than Z. So Z is the lightest.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Lena''s mother has one brother. What is he to Lena?', '["Her uncle", "Her cousin", "Her grandfather", "Her nephew"]', 0, 'Your mother''s brother is your uncle.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Kofi is 4 years older than his sister Abena. Their mom is 30 years older than Kofi. Abena is 8. How old is their mom?', '["38", "34", "46", "42"]', 3, 'Kofi is 8 + 4 = 12. Mom is 12 + 30 = 42.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ravi, a boy, points to a boy in a photo and says, "He is my father''s only son''s son." Who is the boy in the photo to Ravi?', '["His brother", "His nephew", "His son", "His father"]', 2, 'Ravi''s father''s only son is Ravi himself. That boy is Ravi''s son.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In 6 years, Tia will be twice as old as she was 3 years ago. How old is Tia now?', '["9", "12", "10", "15"]', 1, 'At 12: in 6 years she will be 18, and 3 years ago she was 9. 18 is twice 9.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ali and his dad''s ages add up to 50. Dad is 30 years older than Ali. How old is Ali?', '["10", "15", "20", "25"]', 0, 'If Ali is 10, Dad is 40, and 10 + 40 = 50.'),
(2, 'logic', 'At the pool, every swimmer must wear a cap, except children under 4 years old. Sana is 3 and Diego is 6. Who must wear a cap?', '["Only Sana", "Both of them", "Neither of them", "Only Diego"]', 3, 'Diego is 4 or older, so the rule applies to him. Sana is under 4, so she is the exception.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A game starts you at 10 points. A red card adds 5 points. A card showing a 7 then subtracts 3 points. You draw a red 7. What is your score?', '["15", "12", "18", "7"]', 1, '10 + 5 = 15 for the red card, then 15 - 3 = 12 for the 7.'),
(2, 'logic', 'School rule: no phones in class unless the teacher gives permission. Priya uses a phone for a project after her teacher said yes. Did she break the rule?', '["Yes, phones are never allowed", "Yes, because it was a project", "No, she had permission", "Only if it rang"]', 2, 'The rule has an exception for permission. Priya had it, so she followed the rule.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A machine gives a prize only if you put in exactly 3 tokens that are NOT all the same color. Which set gets a prize?', '["Green, green, green", "Red, blue", "Red, red, blue, blue", "Red, blue, blue"]', 3, 'Red, blue, blue is 3 tokens and not all the same. The others are all one color, only 2 tokens, or 4 tokens.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A robot dog sits when it hears a bell and jumps when it hears a whistle. If it hears both at once, it spins instead. It hears a bell and a whistle together. What does it do?', '["Sits", "Spins", "Jumps", "Sits and jumps"]', 1, 'The rule says that hearing both together makes it spin instead of sitting or jumping.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A doctor gives you 3 pills and says to take one every 30 minutes, starting now. How long until you have taken all 3?', '["30 minutes", "90 minutes", "60 minutes", "120 minutes"]', 2, 'You take the 1st now, the 2nd at 30 minutes, and the 3rd at 60 minutes.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A bus has 12 passengers. At stop 1, 5 get off and 3 get on. At stop 2, 4 get off and 6 get on. How many passengers are on the bus now?', '["12", "10", "14", "16"]', 0, '12 - 5 + 3 = 10, then 10 - 4 + 6 = 12.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Some months have 31 days. How many months have at least 28 days?', '["1", "2", "7", "12"]', 3, 'Every month has 28 days or more, so all 12 months count.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A clock takes 6 seconds to strike 4 times at 4 o''clock. How long does it take to strike 7 times at 7 o''clock?', '["12 seconds", "10.5 seconds", "14 seconds", "9 seconds"]', 0, 'Four strikes have 3 gaps, so each gap is 2 seconds. Seven strikes have 6 gaps, and 6 x 2 = 12 seconds.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which number does not belong: 16, 25, 36, 48, 49?', '["16", "36", "48", "49"]', 2, '16, 25, 36 and 49 are square numbers (4x4, 5x5, 6x6, 7x7). 48 is not a square.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which one does not belong: violin, cello, harp, trumpet?', '["violin", "trumpet", "cello", "harp"]', 1, 'Violin, cello and harp all make sound with vibrating strings. A trumpet is played by blowing.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which animal does not belong with the others: whale, dolphin, bat, shark?', '["shark", "whale", "dolphin", "bat"]', 0, 'Whales, dolphins and bats are mammals. A shark is a fish.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Three of these words read the same forwards and backwards. Which one does not: LEVEL, RADAR, KAYAK, HOUSE?', '["LEVEL", "RADAR", "KAYAK", "HOUSE"]', 3, 'LEVEL, RADAR and KAYAK are palindromes. HOUSE backwards is ESUOH.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Four kids performed in a talent show one after another. Sara went before Tao but after Uri. Vera went after Tao. Who performed 3rd?', '["Sara", "Tao", "Uri", "Vera"]', 1, 'The order was Uri, Sara, Tao, Vera. So Tao was 3rd.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a game, Kian scored 5 more points than Lin. Mo scored 3 fewer points than Lin. Nia scored 2 more points than Kian. Who scored the most?', '["Kian", "Lin", "Nia", "Mo"]', 2, 'Call Lin''s score L. Kian has L + 5, Mo has L - 3, and Nia has L + 7. Nia''s is the biggest.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A rabbit is faster than a turtle. A cheetah is faster than a horse. A horse is faster than a rabbit. A snail is slower than a turtle. Which animal is 3rd fastest?', '["The horse", "The turtle", "The cheetah", "The rabbit"]', 3, 'Fastest to slowest: cheetah, horse, rabbit, turtle, snail. The rabbit is 3rd.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Monday was warmer than Tuesday. Wednesday was colder than Tuesday. Thursday was warmer than Monday. Which day was the second warmest?', '["Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Monday", "Thursday"]', 2, 'Warmest to coldest: Thursday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday. Monday is 2nd warmest.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Rita finished 3 places ahead of Sam. Sam finished 2 places ahead of Tao. Tao finished 6th. What place did Rita finish?', '["1st", "2nd", "3rd", "4th"]', 0, 'Sam was 2 places ahead of 6th, so 4th. Rita was 3 places ahead of 4th, so 1st.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 1, 8, 27, 64, ___?', '["100", "125", "121", "216"]', 1, 'These are cube numbers: 1x1x1, 2x2x2, 3x3x3, 4x4x4. Next is 5x5x5 = 125.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 2, 6, 7, 21, 22, 66, ___?', '["67", "68", "132", "198"]', 0, 'The rule alternates: multiply by 3, then add 1. After 66 comes 66 + 1 = 67.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What number is missing: 7, 14, 28, ___, 112?', '["42", "70", "84", "56"]', 3, 'Each number is double the one before. 28 x 2 = 56, and 56 x 2 = 112.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 100, 91, 83, 76, 70, ___?', '["64", "65", "66", "60"]', 1, 'The amounts taken away shrink by 1 each time: 9, 8, 7, 6, so the next is 5. 70 - 5 = 65.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 1, 3, 6, 10, 15, ___?', '["20", "22", "21", "25"]', 2, 'The gaps grow by 1 each time: 2, 3, 4, 5, so the next gap is 6. 15 + 6 = 21.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 1, 2, 6, 24, 120, ___?', '["720", "240", "600", "840"]', 0, 'Multiply by 2, then 3, then 4, then 5, so next multiply by 6. 120 x 6 = 720.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Pia and Quin are each either a truth-teller or a liar. Pia says, "At least one of us is a liar." What are they?', '["Pia lies and Quin tells the truth", "Both of them lie", "Both of them tell the truth", "Pia tells the truth and Quin lies"]', 3, 'If Pia were a liar, her sentence would be true, which is impossible. So Pia is honest, and her sentence means Quin is the liar.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Elm says, "Fay lies." Fay says, "Gus lies." Gus says, "Elm and Fay both lie." Each always tells the truth or always lies. Who is the only honest one?', '["Elm", "Gus", "Fay", "Nobody"]', 2, 'If Elm were honest, Fay lies, so Gus is honest, but then Gus''s words would call honest Elm a liar. So Elm lies, Fay is honest, and Gus lies.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ann says, "Ben is lying." Ben says, "Cara is lying." Cara says, "Ann and Ben are both lying." Each kid is either always honest or always lies. Who is telling the truth?', '["Only Ann", "Only Ben", "Only Cara", "Nobody"]', 1, 'If Cara were honest, Ann and Ben would both be lying - but then Ann''s claim that Ben lies would be true, a contradiction. So Cara lies, which makes Ben honest, and Ann (who says Ben lies) is lying.'),
(2, 'logic', 'The key is in the box, under the mat, or in the pot. Someone who always lies says, "It is in the box or under the mat." Where is the key?', '["In the box", "In the pot", "Under the mat", "It cannot be told"]', 1, 'The statement is false, so the key is neither in the box nor under the mat. Only the pot is left.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Five friends sit in seats 1 to 5. Pat is in seat 3 and Rob is in seat 1. Sue sits between Rob and Pat. Quin does not sit next to Pat. Tia is the fifth friend. Who is in seat 5?', '["Tia", "Sue", "Rob", "Quin"]', 3, 'Sue is in seat 2. Seats 4 and 5 are left for Quin and Tia. Quin cannot be next to Pat (seat 4), so Quin is in seat 5.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A cinema row has 9 seats. Nita sits in the exact middle seat. Oz sits 2 seats to the right of Nita. What seat number is Oz in, counting from the left?', '["Seat 6", "Seat 8", "Seat 7", "Seat 9"]', 2, 'The middle of 9 seats is seat 5. Two seats to the right is 5 + 2 = seat 7.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Kids stand in a circle, numbered 1, 2, 3 and so on in order. Kid 4 is directly across from kid 10. How many kids are in the circle?', '["12", "10", "14", "16"]', 0, 'Directly across is halfway around. From 4 to 10 is 6 steps, so the full circle is 6 x 2 = 12 kids.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a queue, Jae is 7th from the front. Kim stands 4 places behind Jae. There are 3 kids behind Kim. How many kids are in the queue?', '["14", "13", "15", "12"]', 0, 'Kim is 7 + 4 = 11th. With 3 kids behind her, the queue has 11 + 3 = 14 kids.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Four houses stand in a row. Ola lives at one end. Pia lives right next to Ola. Quin lives next to Pia but not next to Ola. Rae lives in the last house. Who lives at the other end from Ola?', '["Pia", "Quin", "It could be Quin or Rae", "Rae"]', 3, 'Ola, Pia and Quin take three houses in a line starting from Ola''s end, leaving Rae at the far end.'),
(2, 'logic', 'If it is a weekend day, the library opens at 10. Today the library opened at 9. What must be true?', '["Today is Saturday", "Today is Sunday", "Today is not a weekend day", "The library was closed"]', 2, 'On a weekend day the library opens at 10. It opened at 9, so today cannot be a weekend day.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Everyone who joins the choir must practice. Everyone who practices gets a snack. Rita joined the choir. What must be true?', '["Rita does not get a snack", "Rita gets a snack", "Rita skips practice", "Everyone in the school gets a snack"]', 1, 'Rita joined, so she practices. Anyone who practices gets a snack, so Rita gets one.'),
(2, 'logic', 'All the roses in the garden are red. Some of the flowers in the garden are roses. Which must be true?', '["All flowers in the garden are red", "Some flowers in the garden are red", "No flowers in the garden are red", "All red things are roses"]', 1, 'The flowers that are roses are red, so at least some garden flowers are red. We know nothing about the other flowers.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Nothing in the toy box is broken. The train is not in the toy box. Is the train broken?', '["Yes", "No", "It cannot be told", "Only if it is red"]', 2, 'The rule only covers things inside the toy box. The train is outside it, so we are told nothing about it.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Some kids at camp like hiking. Every kid who likes hiking owns boots. Which statement must be true?', '["All kids at camp own boots", "No kid at camp owns boots", "Every kid with boots likes hiking", "Some kids at camp own boots"]', 3, 'The kids who like hiking are at camp, and they all own boots. So at least some kids at camp own boots.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What letter comes next: B, D, G, K, ___?', '["P", "O", "Q", "N"]', 0, 'The jumps are 2, 3, 4 letters, so the next jump is 5. K is the 11th letter, and 11 + 5 = 16, which is P.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Start at the letter H. Move 6 letters forward, then 4 letters back. Which letter do you land on?', '["J", "I", "K", "L"]', 0, 'Six letters after H is N. Four letters back from N is M, L, K, J. You land on J.'),
(2, 'logic', 'How many letters are between C and J in the alphabet, not counting C and J themselves?', '["5", "6", "7", "8"]', 1, 'The letters between are D, E, F, G, H and I. That is 6 letters.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which number does not belong: 2, 3, 5, 9, 11?', '["2", "5", "9", "11"]', 2, '2, 3, 5 and 11 are prime numbers. 9 can be divided by 3, so it is not prime.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which does not belong: triangle, square, cube, hexagon?', '["triangle", "square", "hexagon", "cube"]', 3, 'Triangle, square and hexagon are flat shapes. A cube is a solid 3-D shape.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which does not belong with the others: Mercury, Venus, Moon, Mars?', '["Mercury", "Venus", "Mars", "Moon"]', 3, 'Mercury, Venus and Mars are planets. The Moon goes around a planet, so it is not a planet itself.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which does not belong: tiger, lion, leopard, wolf?', '["tiger", "lion", "wolf", "leopard"]', 2, 'Tigers, lions and leopards are big cats. A wolf belongs to the dog family.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which bird does not belong with the others: eagle, sparrow, ostrich, hawk?', '["eagle", "ostrich", "sparrow", "hawk"]', 1, 'Eagles, sparrows and hawks can all fly. An ostrich cannot fly.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Abe, Bea, Cai and Dot each have a piano lesson on a different day: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday. Cai''s is Monday. Abe''s is the day after Bea''s. Dot''s is not Thursday. What day is Abe''s lesson?', '["Thursday", "Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday"]', 0, 'Bea and Abe need two days in a row from Tue-Thu. Bea Tuesday would leave Dot on Thursday, which is not allowed. So Bea is Wednesday, Abe is Thursday, Dot is Tuesday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'I am a number between 50 and 100. I am a multiple of 5, and my digits add up to 10. What number am I?', '["55", "50", "65", "95"]', 0, 'A multiple of 5 ends in 0 or 5. If it ends in 5, the tens digit must be 5 to reach 10, giving 55. Ending in 0 would need a tens digit of 10.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A lock code uses the digits 1, 4 and 7 once each. The first digit is not 1, the last is not 7, and the middle is not 4. The first digit is smaller than the middle digit. What is the code?', '["714", "417", "471", "174"]', 2, 'Only 471 and 714 obey the first three clues. In 714 the first digit 7 is bigger than the middle 1, so the code is 471.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Mia visits her grandma on a weekday whose name starts with T. It is not the day right before Wednesday. Which day does she visit?', '["Tuesday", "Thursday", "Wednesday", "Friday"]', 1, 'The weekdays starting with T are Tuesday and Thursday. Tuesday is right before Wednesday, so it is Thursday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Xena, Yui and Zed each ride one of a bike, a scooter and a skateboard. Zed does not ride the bike. Yui does not ride the scooter. Xena rides neither the skateboard nor the scooter. Who rides the scooter?', '["Xena", "Yui", "It cannot be told", "Zed"]', 3, 'Xena rides the bike. Yui cannot have the scooter, so Yui has the skateboard. That leaves the scooter for Zed.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Out of 20 kids, 12 are in band, 10 are in drama, and 4 are in both. How many kids are in exactly one of the two?', '["14", "18", "22", "16"]', 0, '8 kids are in band only (12 - 4) and 6 in drama only (10 - 4). 8 + 6 = 14.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A bag has 20 candies. 12 have nuts, 9 are chocolate, and 5 are both nuts and chocolate. How many have neither?', '["3", "5", "8", "4"]', 3, 'Nuts or chocolate is 12 + 9 - 5 = 16 candies. So 20 - 16 = 4 have neither.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Of 15 kids, 9 wear red shoes and 8 wear a hat. What is the greatest possible number wearing both?', '["9", "8", "7", "17"]', 1, 'The group wearing both cannot be bigger than the smaller group. All 8 hat-wearers could wear red shoes, so 8.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Of 40 kids, 25 play a sport, 18 play an instrument, and 5 do neither. How many do both?', '["5", "7", "8", "13"]', 2, '35 kids do at least one thing (40 - 5). 25 + 18 = 43, which is 8 more than 35, so 8 kids do both.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A month with 30 days starts on a Monday. What day of the week is the 30th?', '["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Sunday"]', 1, 'The 1st, 8th, 15th, 22nd and 29th are Mondays. So the 30th is a Tuesday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Kara''s clock runs 10 minutes fast. It shows 4:05. What is the real time?', '["3:55", "4:15", "3:45", "4:00"]', 0, 'A fast clock shows too much, so subtract 10 minutes. 4:05 - 10 minutes = 3:55.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A night train leaves at 11:40 pm and travels for 2 hours 35 minutes. When does it arrive?', '["2:05 am", "2:35 am", "1:15 am", "2:15 am"]', 3, '11:40 pm plus 20 minutes is midnight. The remaining 2 hours 15 minutes makes 2:15 am.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Today is Friday. What day of the week was it 12 days ago?', '["Saturday", "Monday", "Sunday", "Tuesday"]', 2, '12 days is 7 days plus 5 days. 7 days ago was Friday, and 5 days back from Friday is Sunday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Painter is to brush as writer is to ___.', '["paint", "pen", "easel", "chisel"]', 1, 'A brush is a tool a painter uses. A pen is a tool a writer uses.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Foal is to horse as lamb is to ___.', '["sheep", "goat", "cow", "pig"]', 0, 'A foal is a baby horse, and a lamb is a baby sheep.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Wheel is to car as wing is to ___.', '["road", "sky", "airplane", "pilot"]', 2, 'A wheel is a part of a car, and a wing is a part of an airplane.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Pentagon is to 5 as octagon is to ___.', '["6", "7", "10", "8"]', 3, 'A pentagon has 5 sides, and an octagon has 8 sides.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a code, each letter is written as double its place in the alphabet (A is 1, so it becomes 2). How is ACE written?', '["1-3-5", "2-6-8", "2-4-10", "2-6-10"]', 3, 'A is 1, C is 3, and E is 5. Doubled, they become 2, 6 and 10.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a mirror code, A becomes Z, B becomes Y, and C becomes X. How is CAB written?', '["XZY", "XYZ", "ZYX", "YZX"]', 0, 'C becomes X, A becomes Z, and B becomes Y. That gives XZY.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a code, DOG is written 4-15-7 (A is 1, B is 2, and so on). Which word is written 3-1-20?', '["CUT", "CAT", "COT", "BAT"]', 1, '3 is C, 1 is A, and 20 is T. That spells CAT.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A number machine changes 2 into 7, 3 into 10, and 5 into 16. What does it change 6 into?', '["18", "20", "19", "21"]', 2, 'The rule is multiply by 3, then add 1. So 6 x 3 + 1 = 19.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Eight coins look the same, but one is heavier. What is the fewest number of weighings on a balance scale that is always enough to find the heavy coin?', '["1", "2", "3", "4"]', 1, 'Weigh 3 against 3. If they balance, the heavy coin is one of the other 2; if not, it is in the heavier 3. One more weighing settles it, so 2.'),
(2, 'logic', 'On a balance scale, 2 melons weigh the same as 3 pineapples. One pineapple weighs 4 kg. How much does one melon weigh?', '["6 kg", "8 kg", "12 kg", "4 kg"]', 0, '3 pineapples weigh 12 kg, so 2 melons weigh 12 kg. One melon weighs 6 kg.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A balance is perfectly level with a 3 kg weight and 2 identical blocks on the left pan, and 5 of the same blocks on the right pan. How heavy is one block?', '["3 kg", "2 kg", "0.5 kg", "1 kg"]', 3, 'The extra 3 blocks on the right must weigh the same as the 3 kg weight. So each block is 1 kg.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A melon on the left pan tips the scale against 3 apples on the right. Adding a 4th apple makes the pans balance exactly. The melon weighs 800 g. How much does one apple weigh?', '["100 g", "160 g", "200 g", "400 g"]', 2, '4 apples balance the 800 g melon, so one apple weighs 800 / 4 = 200 g.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Max is 3 times as old as his cousin Zed. In 4 years Max will be twice as old as Zed. How old is Zed now?', '["4", "3", "6", "8"]', 0, 'If Zed is 4, Max is 12. In 4 years they will be 8 and 16, and 16 is twice 8.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Nora''s brother Sam has a daughter named Tia. What is Nora to Tia?', '["Her mother", "Her cousin", "Her grandmother", "Her aunt"]', 3, 'Your father''s sister is your aunt.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A father is 3 times as old as his son. Together their ages add up to 48. How old is the father?', '["32", "24", "36", "40"]', 2, 'Father plus son is 4 equal parts, so each part is 12. The son is 12 and the father is 36.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ali has 3 brothers, and each of his brothers has exactly 2 sisters. How many children are in the family, counting Ali?', '["5", "6", "7", "9"]', 1, 'Ali and his 3 brothers make 4 boys. The 2 sisters make 4 + 2 = 6 children.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Lunch rules: kids who bring lunch eat in Room 5, kids who buy lunch eat in Room 6, but kids with an allergy always eat in Room 7. Ravi has an allergy and buys lunch. Where does he eat?', '["Room 5", "Room 6", "Room 5 or Room 6", "Room 7"]', 3, 'The allergy rule overrides the other rules, so Ravi eats in Room 7.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A park lets children under 5 in free and ages 5 to 12 pay half price. Everyone else pays the full $10. Ana is 4, Ben is 9 and Cal is 13. How much do they pay altogether?', '["$10", "$20", "$15", "$25"]', 2, 'Ana pays $0, Ben pays half of $10, which is $5, and Cal pays $10. That is $15.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a game, green means go, yellow means slow down and red means stop. But when the referee''s flag is up, everyone must stop, whatever the color. The light is green and the flag is up. What must you do?', '["Stop", "Go", "Slow down", "Go faster"]', 0, 'The flag rule beats the light colors, so with the flag up you must stop.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a card game a number card scores its number, a face card scores 10, but the joker always scores 0. You draw a 6, a king, the joker and a 3. What is your total score?', '["29", "19", "9", "13"]', 1, '6 + 10 (king) + 0 (joker) + 3 = 19.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A log is cut into 5 equal pieces with straight cuts. How many cuts are needed?', '["4", "5", "6", "3"]', 0, 'Each cut makes one more piece than before, starting from one piece. To get 5 pieces you need 4 cuts.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A pen and a notebook cost $1.10 together. The notebook costs $1.00 more than the pen. How much does the pen cost?', '["10 cents", "1 cent", "5 cents", "15 cents"]', 2, 'If the pen is 5 cents, the notebook is $1.05, and together they are $1.10. A 10-cent pen would make the total $1.20.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A water lily doubles in size every day. It covers the whole pond on day 10. On which day did it cover half of the pond?', '["Day 5", "Day 9", "Day 8", "Day 7"]', 1, 'It doubles each day, so the day before it covers everything, it covered exactly half. That is day 9.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which weighs more: one kilogram of feathers or one kilogram of stones?', '["The feathers", "The stones", "It depends on the day", "They weigh the same"]', 3, 'Both are exactly one kilogram, so they weigh the same. The feathers just take up more space.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Dr. Ito''s office is 2 floors above the bakery. The bakery is 1 floor above the gym. The gym is on floor 3. Which floor is Dr. Ito''s office on?', '["Floor 5", "Floor 7", "Floor 9", "Floor 6"]', 3, 'The bakery is on floor 3 + 1 = 4. The office is 2 floors above that, on floor 6.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Among six cousins, Pia is older than Quin. Rex is younger than Quin. Sol is older than Pia. Tam is younger than Rex but older than Uma. Which cousin is 5th oldest?', '["Rex", "Tam", "Uma", "Quin"]', 1, 'Oldest to youngest: Sol, Pia, Quin, Rex, Tam, Uma. Tam is 5th.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Mo finished a race in 2nd place. Lea finished right behind Mo. Nia finished 3 places behind Mo. Ken finished between Lea and Nia. What place did Ken get?', '["4th", "3rd", "5th", "6th"]', 0, 'Lea is 3rd and Nia is 2 + 3 = 5th. Ken is between them, so he is 4th.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ada is 5 cm taller than Bo. Bo is 8 cm taller than Cy. Cy is 130 cm tall. Dee is 2 cm shorter than Ada. How tall is Dee?', '["138 cm", "143 cm", "141 cm", "136 cm"]', 2, 'Bo is 138 cm and Ada is 143 cm. Dee is 2 cm shorter than Ada, so 141 cm.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ravi and Sia scored the same number of points. Tess scored more than Ravi. Uma scored fewer points than Sia. Who scored the most and who scored the least?', '["Ravi most, Uma least", "Tess most, Sia least", "Tess most, Uma least", "Sia most, Tess least"]', 2, 'Ravi and Sia are level, Tess is above them and Uma is below them. So Tess is highest and Uma is lowest.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 3, 5, 9, 15, 23, ___?', '["33", "31", "32", "35"]', 0, 'The gaps go 2, 4, 6, 8, so the next gap is 10. 23 + 10 = 33.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 1, 4, 10, 22, 46, ___?', '["92", "94", "90", "96"]', 1, 'Each number is double the one before, plus 2. So 46 x 2 + 2 = 94.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next in the pattern: 2, 5, 8, 11, 14, ___?', '["16", "17", "18", "19"]', 1, 'The numbers go up by 3 each time, so 14 + 3 = 17.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, ___?', '["15", "19", "17", "21"]', 2, 'These are the prime numbers in order. The next prime after 13 is 17, since 14, 15 and 16 can be divided evenly.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 5, 8, 6, 9, 7, 10, ___?', '["8", "7", "9", "11"]', 0, 'The rule alternates: add 3, then subtract 2. After 10 comes 10 - 2 = 8.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Kids in Club A always tell the truth and kids in Club B always lie. You ask a kid, "Are you in Club A?" What answer will you always hear?', '["No", "Yes", "Yes from Club A and no from Club B", "It depends on the day"]', 1, 'A truthful Club A kid says yes. A Club B kid lies about it and also says yes. Everyone answers yes.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Lia, Mei and Noor: one of them took the last slice. Lia says, "Mei took it." Mei says, "I did not take it." Noor says, "Lia took it." Exactly one of them is lying. Who took it?', '["Mei", "Noor", "It cannot be worked out", "Lia"]', 3, 'If Lia took it, only Lia''s statement is a lie. If Mei or Noor took it, two statements would be lies.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A door has two signs. Sign 1 says, "Both of these signs are false." What must be true?', '["Sign 1 is false and Sign 2 is true", "Sign 1 is true and Sign 2 is false", "Both signs are false", "Both signs are true"]', 0, 'If Sign 1 were true, it would be saying itself is false, which is impossible. So it is false, meaning not both are false. Sign 2 must be true.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Exactly one of Ana, Ben and Cy always lies; the other two always tell the truth. Ana says, "Ben is honest." Ben says, "Cy is a liar." Who is the liar?', '["Ana", "Cy", "Ben", "It cannot be told"]', 1, 'If Ben or Ana were the liar, the other''s statement would make a second liar. With Cy as the liar, both statements are true.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Six kids sit evenly around a round table. Ana sits directly across from Ben. Cy sits right next to Ana. Dev sits directly across from Cy. Do Ben and Dev sit next to each other?', '["No", "Only if Cy sits on Ana''s left", "They sit across from each other", "Yes"]', 3, 'Ben is 3 seats from Ana. Whichever side Cy takes, Dev lands right next to Ben on the same side.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Five kids stand in the order A, B, C, D, E. The first and last kids swap places. Then the 2nd and 4th kids swap places. What is the new order?', '["E, B, C, D, A", "A, D, C, B, E", "E, D, C, B, A", "D, E, C, A, B"]', 2, 'After the first swap: E, B, C, D, A. After swapping the 2nd and 4th: E, D, C, B, A.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A classroom has 3 rows of 4 desks, numbered row by row from the front-left desk (row 1 is desks 1 to 4, row 2 is 5 to 8, row 3 is 9 to 12). Where is desk 10?', '["Row 2, 2nd desk", "Row 3, 3rd desk", "Row 3, 2nd desk", "Row 2, 4th desk"]', 2, 'Row 3 starts at desk 9, so desk 10 is the second desk in that row.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Sal, Pim, Quo, Rui and Tam sit in a row of 5 chairs. Sal is in chair 1 and Pim is in chair 3. Quo sits next to Pim. Rui does not sit next to Pim. Who is in chair 5?', '["Quo", "Tam", "Sal", "Rui"]', 3, 'Chairs 2 and 4 are next to Pim, and Rui cannot take them. Chair 1 is Sal''s, so Rui must be in chair 5.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every cookie in the jar has chocolate. Nothing with chocolate is allowed in the lunch box. Can a cookie from the jar go in the lunch box?', '["Yes", "No", "Only one at a time", "It cannot be told"]', 1, 'Jar cookies have chocolate, and chocolate is not allowed in the lunch box. So they cannot go in.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Some dogs are brown. Some brown things are muddy. Must some dogs be muddy?', '["Not necessarily", "Yes, some dogs must be muddy", "Yes, all dogs are muddy", "No, no dog can be muddy"]', 0, 'The muddy brown things could be boots or logs. Nothing says the muddy ones are the dogs.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every drummer in the band is also a singer. Kara is not a singer. Can Kara be a drummer in the band?', '["Yes", "Only if she practices", "No", "It cannot be told"]', 2, 'Drummers in the band must all be singers. Kara is not a singer, so she cannot be a drummer.'),
(2, 'logic', 'If the light is on, someone is home. The light is off. Is the house definitely empty?', '["Yes, the house is empty", "Yes, but only at night", "No, someone is definitely home", "No, someone might still be home"]', 3, 'The rule only tells us what a lit light means. Someone could be home with the light off.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Everyone in Room 4 is in Grade 4 or Grade 5. Nell is in Room 4 and is not in Grade 5. Which grade is Nell in?', '["Grade 4", "Grade 5", "Grade 3", "It cannot be told"]', 0, 'Room 4 only holds Grade 4 and Grade 5 kids. Nell is not Grade 5, so she is Grade 4.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What letter comes next: Z, X, U, Q, ___?', '["M", "L", "K", "N"]', 1, 'The letters move backward by 2, 3 and 4 places, so the next move is 5 back. Q is the 17th letter, and 17 - 5 = 12, which is L.'),
(2, 'logic', 'The alphabet is a circle, so after Z comes A again. Start at X and move 5 letters forward. Where do you land?', '["B", "C", "D", "A"]', 1, 'From X the letters go Y, Z, A, B, C. The 5th one is C.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which of these words has its letters in alphabetical order from first to last: CHAIR, BEGIN, TRAIN, MOUSE?', '["BEGIN", "CHAIR", "TRAIN", "MOUSE"]', 0, 'In BEGIN, the letters B, E, G, I, N go up the alphabet in order. The other words break the order, like H then A in CHAIR.'),
(2, 'logic', 'How many of the letters in the word MATHEMATICS are vowels (A, E, I, O, U)?', '["3", "5", "4", "6"]', 2, 'The vowels are A, E, A and I. That makes 4.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which number does not belong: 8, 27, 64, 100, 125?', '["8", "27", "125", "100"]', 3, '8, 27, 64 and 125 are cube numbers (2x2x2, 3x3x3, 4x4x4, 5x5x5). 100 is not a cube.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which does not belong: minute, hour, meter, second?', '["meter", "minute", "hour", "second"]', 0, 'Minute, hour and second measure time. A meter measures length.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which does not belong: whale, seal, penguin, dolphin?', '["whale", "seal", "dolphin", "penguin"]', 3, 'Whales, seals and dolphins are mammals. A penguin is a bird.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which number does not belong: 24, 36, 48, 50, 60?', '["24", "36", "50", "60"]', 2, '24, 36, 48 and 60 are all multiples of 12. 50 is not.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Grace, Hiro, Isla and Jack finished a game in places 1st to 4th, with no ties. Hiro finished right ahead of Grace. Isla was not 1st or last. Jack finished ahead of Isla. Who was 1st?', '["Grace", "Jack", "Hiro", "Isla"]', 1, 'Isla is 2nd or 3rd. If Hiro and Grace were 1st and 2nd, Jack would be behind Isla. If they were 2nd and 3rd, Isla has no spot. So they are 3rd and 4th, Isla is 2nd, and Jack is 1st.'),
(2, 'logic', 'I am a two-digit number. My tens digit is 2 more than my units digit, and my digits add up to 8. What number am I?', '["62", "35", "44", "53"]', 3, 'The digits must be 5 and 3, because 5 is 2 more than 3 and 5 + 3 = 8. With 5 as the tens digit, the number is 53.'),
(2, 'logic', 'The cookie thief is taller than Ada (130 cm) and shorter than Cy (140 cm). The suspects are Ben (135 cm), Dee (145 cm), Eli (128 cm) and Cy. Who is the thief?', '["Dee", "Ben", "Eli", "Cy"]', 1, 'The thief must be between 130 cm and 140 cm tall. Only Ben, at 135 cm, fits.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Uma, Vic, Wes and Xia each play a different game: tag, hopscotch, marbles or jump rope. Uma plays neither tag, hopscotch nor jump rope. Vic plays neither tag, marbles nor jump rope. Wes does not play tag. Who plays tag?', '["Uma", "Vic", "Xia", "Wes"]', 2, 'Uma plays marbles and Vic plays hopscotch. Wes does not play tag, so Wes has jump rope. That leaves tag for Xia.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A two-digit code has an even first digit greater than 5 and an odd second digit. The digits add up to 9 and differ by 3. What is the code?', '["63", "81", "45", "36"]', 0, 'The first digit is 6 or 8. With 6 the second digit is 3 (sum 9, difference 3). With 8 it would be 1, a difference of 7.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every kid in Room 9 plays chess, checkers, or both. 14 play chess, 11 play checkers and 5 play both. How many kids are in Room 9?', '["20", "25", "19", "30"]', 0, '14 + 11 = 25 counts the 5 kids who play both twice. So 25 - 5 = 20 kids.'),
(2, 'logic', 'At a party, 10 kids like only apples, 8 kids like only pears, and 6 kids like both. How many kids like apples?', '["10", "14", "16", "24"]', 2, 'Kids who like apples are the 10 who like only apples plus the 6 who like both. That is 16.'),
(2, 'logic', 'How many whole numbers from 1 to 20 are multiples of 2 or multiples of 3 (or both)?', '["16", "14", "10", "13"]', 3, 'There are 10 multiples of 2 and 6 multiples of 3, but 6, 12 and 18 are in both lists. 10 + 6 - 3 = 13.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Of 30 kids, 20 like swimming. Of those swimmers, 8 also like running. Another 5 kids like running but not swimming. How many kids like running?', '["5", "13", "8", "20"]', 1, 'The kids who like running are the 8 swimmers who also run plus the 5 who do not swim. That is 13.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a year that is not a leap year, February 1 is a Wednesday. What day of the week is March 1?', '["Thursday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Friday"]', 2, 'February has 28 days, exactly 4 weeks. So March 1 falls on the same weekday as February 1.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A shop opens at 9:30 am and closes at 6:15 pm. How long is it open each day?', '["8 hours 45 minutes", "8 hours 15 minutes", "9 hours 15 minutes", "8 hours 55 minutes"]', 0, '9:30 am to 6:30 pm is 9 hours. The shop closes 15 minutes earlier, so 8 hours 45 minutes.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Kai''s flight leaves at 5:50 pm. He wants to arrive at the airport 90 minutes before. What time should he arrive?', '["4:10 pm", "4:20 pm", "4:30 pm", "3:50 pm"]', 1, '90 minutes is 1 hour 30 minutes. 5:50 pm minus 1 hour is 4:50, and minus 30 more minutes is 4:20 pm.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A party is 3 weeks and 2 days after Monday, May 5. What is the date of the party?', '["May 26", "May 30", "June 2", "May 28"]', 3, '3 weeks is 21 days, and 2 more days makes 23 days. May 5 + 23 days = May 28.'),
(2, 'logic', 'The 5th of a month is a Sunday. What day of the week is the 20th of that month?', '["Sunday", "Tuesday", "Monday", "Saturday"]', 2, 'The 5th to the 20th is 15 days, which is 2 weeks and 1 day. One day after Sunday is Monday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Seed is to plant as egg is to ___.', '["chick", "nest", "shell", "farm"]', 0, 'A plant grows from a seed, and a chick hatches from an egg.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Thermometer is to temperature as clock is to ___.', '["numbers", "wall", "tick", "time"]', 3, 'A thermometer measures temperature. A clock measures time.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Library is to books as museum is to ___.', '["tickets", "exhibits", "guards", "shelves"]', 1, 'A library is a place that keeps books for people to see and borrow. A museum keeps exhibits for people to see.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Egg is to omelet as flour is to ___.', '["oven", "wheat", "sugar", "bread"]', 3, 'An egg is an ingredient of an omelet. Flour is an ingredient of bread.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a code, every vowel (A, E, I, O, U) is replaced by a star. How is ELEPHANT written?', '["*L*PH*NT", "*L*PHANT", "EL*PH*NT", "*LEPH*NT"]', 0, 'E, E and A are the vowels, so they become stars. That gives *L*PH*NT.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a code, the first letter of a word moves to the end (LION becomes IONL). How is TIGER written?', '["RTIGE", "REGIT", "IGERT", "GERTI"]', 2, 'Move the first letter T to the end: I, G, E, R, T.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a code, red = 3, blue = 5 and green = 7. What is (red + blue) x green?', '["38", "56", "105", "46"]', 1, 'red + blue = 3 + 5 = 8. Then 8 x 7 = 56.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a made-up language, "pim tok" means red car, "pim sar" means red bike, and "lun tok" means blue car. What does "lun sar" mean?', '["Red car", "Red bike", "Blue car", "Blue bike"]', 3, '"pim" is red, "lun" is blue, "tok" is car and "sar" is bike. So "lun sar" is blue bike.'),
(2, 'logic', 'On a balance scale, 3 cubes and 1 ball on the left exactly balance 2 balls and 1 cube on the right. How many cubes weigh the same as 1 ball?', '["1", "3", "2", "4"]', 2, 'Take 1 cube and 1 ball off both sides. The left has 2 cubes and the right has 1 ball, so they weigh the same.'),
(2, 'logic', 'The left pan holds 1 kg of rice and 200 g of beans. The right pan holds 900 g of flour. How much more must go on the right pan to balance?', '["100 g", "300 g", "200 g", "400 g"]', 1, 'The left weighs 1000 + 200 = 1200 g. The right has 900 g, so it needs 300 g more.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Bag A balances Bag B. Bag C is heavier than Bag A. Bag D is lighter than Bag B. Which list goes from heaviest to lightest?', '["C, then A and B equal, then D", "D, then A and B equal, then C", "A, B, C, D", "C, D, then A and B equal"]', 0, 'A and B weigh the same. C is above them and D is below them.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A box holding 12 identical pencils weighs 150 g in total. Each pencil weighs 10 g. How much does the empty box weigh?', '["20 g", "40 g", "50 g", "30 g"]', 3, 'The pencils weigh 12 x 10 = 120 g. The box weighs 150 - 120 = 30 g.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Sunil''s mom was 24 when he was born. Sunil is 11 now. How old will his mom be in 5 years?', '["40", "35", "29", "45"]', 0, 'Mom is 24 + 11 = 35 now. In 5 years she will be 40.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Two sisters are 9 and 15 years old. How many years ago was the older sister exactly 3 times as old as the younger?', '["3", "4", "6", "5"]', 2, '6 years ago they were 3 and 9, and 9 is 3 times 3.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Grace''s mother''s sister''s son is Grace''s ___.', '["brother", "cousin", "uncle", "nephew"]', 1, 'Your aunt''s child is your cousin.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a family with 3 daughters, every daughter has exactly one brother. How many children are in the family?', '["3", "5", "6", "4"]', 3, 'All the sisters share the same one brother. That makes 3 girls and 1 boy, so 4 children.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A pool gate opens only when BOTH the sign is green and the lifeguard is on duty. The sign is green, but the lifeguard is not on duty. Does the gate open?', '["Yes, the green sign is enough", "Only for adults", "No", "Only for a minute"]', 2, 'Both things must be true. The lifeguard is missing, so the gate stays shut.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A shop takes $10 off any order over $40, but only for items not on sale. Mia buys a $30 hat and a $25 book, both at regular price. How much does she pay?', '["$55", "$45", "$35", "$65"]', 1, 'The order is $55, which is over $40, and nothing is on sale. So she pays $55 - $10 = $45.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Class 3 has music every Friday, but on a holiday Friday it has art instead. Next Friday is a holiday. What does Class 3 have?', '["Art", "Music", "Both music and art", "No class"]', 0, 'The holiday rule replaces music with art.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a board game, an even roll moves you forward that many spaces and an odd roll moves you back 1 space. You start on space 10 and roll 4, then 3, then 6. Which space do you end on?', '["23", "13", "17", "19"]', 3, 'Roll 4 (even): 14. Roll 3 (odd): back 1 to 13. Roll 6 (even): 19.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Mia has 5 sisters. Each of her sisters has exactly 1 brother. How many brothers does Mia have?', '["1", "0", "5", "6"]', 0, 'Mia and her sisters share the same brother, so Mia has 1 brother.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A straight fence is 20 m long, with a post every 5 m, including one at each end. How many posts are there?', '["4", "5", "6", "20"]', 1, 'Posts stand at 0, 5, 10, 15 and 20 m. That is 5 posts.'),
(2, 'logic', 'You are in a running race and you pass the runner who is in 2nd place. What place are you in now?', '["1st", "3rd", "2nd", "4th"]', 2, 'Passing the runner in 2nd place puts you in 2nd place. You did not pass the leader.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A lift takes 12 seconds to go from floor 1 to floor 4 at a steady speed. How long does it take to go from floor 1 to floor 7?', '["24 seconds", "21 seconds", "28 seconds", "36 seconds"]', 0, 'Floor 1 to 4 is 3 floors in 12 seconds, so 4 seconds per floor. Floor 1 to 7 is 6 floors, or 24 seconds.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A drawer holds 6 black socks and 6 white socks. In the dark, what is the fewest socks you must pull out to be SURE of a matching pair?', '["2", "4", "7", "3"]', 3, 'With two colors, two socks might be different. A third sock must match one of them.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Zoe is older than Yan. Xu is between Zoe and Yan in age. Wade is older than Zoe. Who is the second youngest of the four?', '["Zoe", "Xu", "Yan", "Wade"]', 1, 'Oldest to youngest: Wade, Zoe, Xu, Yan. Xu is second youngest.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ellie has swimming the day after chess. Chess is two days before dance. Dance is on Friday. On which day is swimming?', '["Wednesday", "Friday", "Thursday", "Tuesday"]', 2, 'Chess is two days before Friday, which is Wednesday. Swimming is the day after, Thursday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Gala earned 4 more badges than Hugo. Hugo earned twice as many badges as Ida. Ida earned 3 badges. How many badges did Gala earn?', '["7", "10", "9", "12"]', 1, 'Hugo has 2 x 3 = 6 badges. Gala has 6 + 4 = 10.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a race, Ola took 14 seconds, Pip took 12, Quy took 15 and Rob took 11. Who finished 3rd?', '["Pip", "Quy", "Ola", "Rob"]', 2, 'The smallest time wins. The order is Rob (11), Pip (12), Ola (14), Quy (15), so Ola is 3rd.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A cat is heavier than a rabbit. A dog is heavier than a cat. A mouse is lighter than a rabbit. A horse is heavier than a dog. Which animal is exactly in the middle of the five by weight?', '["The dog", "The rabbit", "The horse", "The cat"]', 3, 'Heaviest to lightest: horse, dog, cat, rabbit, mouse. The cat is 3rd of 5.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Five kids line up from tallest to shortest. Ira is taller than Gia, and Gia is 2nd. Han is right after Gia. Kim is the shortest. What place is Jay, the remaining kid?', '["4th", "1st", "3rd", "5th"]', 0, 'Ira is 1st, Gia 2nd, Han 3rd and Kim 5th. That leaves 4th place for Jay.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 30, 29, 27, 24, 20, ___?', '["16", "15", "14", "17"]', 1, 'The amounts taken away grow by 1 each time: 1, 2, 3, 4, so the next is 5. 20 - 5 = 15.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 0, 3, 8, 15, 24, ___?', '["33", "34", "36", "35"]', 3, 'Each number is a square minus 1: 1-1, 4-1, 9-1, 16-1, 25-1. The next is 36 - 1 = 35.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 2, 2, 4, 6, 10, 16, ___?', '["26", "22", "24", "32"]', 0, 'Each number is the sum of the two before it. 10 + 16 = 26.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 5, 15, 45, 135, ___?', '["270", "450", "405", "180"]', 2, 'Each number is multiplied by 3. 135 x 3 = 405.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 100, 50, 60, 30, 40, 20, ___?', '["10", "25", "30", "40"]', 2, 'The rule alternates: halve, then add 10. Adding 10 to 20 gives 30.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: 12, 15, 21, 30, 42, ___?', '["54", "57", "55", "60"]', 1, 'The gaps are 3, 6, 9, 12, growing by 3 each time. The next gap is 15, and 42 + 15 = 57.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Nima says, "I always lie." Which must be true?', '["Nima does not always lie, and this statement is a lie", "Nima always lies", "Nima always tells the truth", "Nima is telling the truth now"]', 0, 'If Nima always lied, his statement would be true, which is impossible. So he does not always lie, and this time he is not telling the truth.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Kai always tells the truth and Lou always lies. Someone asks Lou, "Is Kai honest?" What does Lou answer?', '["Yes", "He does not answer", "It depends", "No"]', 3, 'Kai really is honest, so the true answer is yes. Lou always lies, so he says no.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Sign A says, "Exactly one sign here is false." Sign B says, "Exactly two signs here are false." Sign C says, "Exactly three signs here are false." Which sign is true?', '["Sign A", "Sign C", "None of them", "Sign B"]', 3, 'If exactly one were false, B and C would both be false, which makes two. If all three were false, C would be true. Exactly two false works: A and C are false, B is true.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Twelve chairs are numbered 1 to 12 around a circle, and after chair 12 comes chair 1 again. Zed sits in chair 11 and moves 4 chairs ahead. Which chair does he end in?', '["Chair 2", "Chair 4", "Chair 3", "Chair 1"]', 2, 'Moving ahead from 11: 12, 1, 2, 3. He ends in chair 3.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A car park has two rows of 6 spaces, A1 to A6 and B1 to B6, with A1 directly across from B1, A2 across from B2, and so on. A red car is in A4. A blue car is directly across from it. A green car is right next to the blue car, on the side with higher numbers. Which space is the green car in?', '["B3", "B5", "A5", "B6"]', 1, 'The blue car is in B4, across from A4. Right next to it toward higher numbers is B5.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Nine kids sit on a bench, alternating boy, girl, boy, girl, and so on, with a boy at each end. How many girls are on the bench?', '["4", "5", "3", "9"]', 0, 'The seats go boy, girl, boy, girl, boy, girl, boy, girl, boy. That is 5 boys and 4 girls.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Kids numbered 1 to 10 stand in a circle in order. A ball starts with kid 1, and each pass goes 3 kids ahead (1 to 4, and so on, going back to 1 after 10). Which kid holds the ball after 4 passes?', '["Kid 2", "Kid 3", "Kid 4", "Kid 10"]', 1, 'The ball goes 1, 4, 7, 10, and then 3 kids past 10 is kid 3 (11 is 1, 12 is 2, 13 is 3).'),
(2, 'logic', 'Jin is ahead of Kai in a line, and Kai is ahead of Lea. Mo stands between Jin and Kai. Ned stands right behind Lea. Who is 4th in line?', '["Kai", "Mo", "Lea", "Ned"]', 2, 'The line is Jin, Mo, Kai, Lea, Ned. Lea is 4th.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every pilot at the airport wears a cap. Some people who wear caps are tall. Are any pilots definitely tall?', '["Yes, all pilots are tall", "Yes, some pilots must be tall", "No pilot is tall", "No, not for sure"]', 3, 'The tall cap-wearers might not be pilots at all. The facts do not tell us anything about the pilots'' height.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every fruit in a basket is an apple or a pear. None of the fruits in the basket is a pear. What must all the fruits be?', '["Apples", "Pears", "Some of each", "Oranges"]', 0, 'Each fruit is an apple or a pear. Pears are ruled out, so every fruit is an apple.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Some students in the class have a bike. Nobody with a bike is ever late. Ivan is late. Does Ivan have a bike?', '["Yes", "No", "Only sometimes", "It cannot be told"]', 1, 'Nobody with a bike is late. Ivan is late, so he cannot have a bike.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every kid in Team Red is in Grade 5. Every kid in Grade 5 has a badge. Teo is in Team Red, Uri is in Grade 4, and Val is not in Team Red. Who definitely has a badge?', '["Uri", "Val", "Teo", "All three of them"]', 2, 'Teo is in Team Red, so he is in Grade 5, so he has a badge. We know nothing that gives Uri or Val a badge.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What comes next: AC, EG, IK, MO, ___?', '["QS", "PR", "QR", "RT"]', 0, 'Each pair skips one letter (A, C). The first letters go A, E, I, M, so the next is Q, and its pair is QS.'),
(2, 'logic', 'What letter comes next: Z, A, Y, B, X, ___?', '["W", "D", "Y", "C"]', 3, 'Two patterns are mixed: Z, Y, X going backward and A, B, C going forward. The next in the forward pattern is C.'),
(2, 'logic', 'How many different letters are in the word MISSISSIPPI?', '["3", "5", "4", "11"]', 2, 'The letters used are M, I, S and P. That is 4 different letters, even though the word has 11 letters.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which of these number words has exactly as many letters as the number it names: ONE, TWO, FOUR, FIVE?', '["FOUR", "ONE", "TWO", "FIVE"]', 0, 'FOUR has 4 letters. ONE and TWO have 3 letters, and FIVE has 4 letters but means 5.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which number does not belong: 121, 131, 141, 152?', '["121", "131", "141", "152"]', 3, '121, 131 and 141 read the same forwards and backwards. 152 backwards is 251.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which month does not belong: February, April, June, September?', '["April", "February", "June", "September"]', 1, 'April, June and September each have 30 days. February has 28 or 29.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Which shape does not belong: triangle, pentagon, circle, hexagon?', '["triangle", "circle", "pentagon", "hexagon"]', 1, 'Triangles, pentagons and hexagons are made of straight sides. A circle has no straight sides.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A number between 40 and 50 is prime, and its digits add up to 11. What is it?', '["47", "43", "49", "45"]', 0, 'The primes between 40 and 50 are 41, 43 and 47. Only 47 has digits adding to 11 (4 + 7).'),
(2, 'logic', 'Three baskets hold 3, 5 and 8 apples, in some order. The blue basket holds neither the most nor the fewest. The red basket holds fewer apples than the green basket. How many apples are in the red basket?', '["5", "8", "It cannot be told", "3"]', 3, 'Blue is the middle amount, 5. Red has fewer than green, so red has 3 and green has 8.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Four kids have 0, 1, 2 and 3 pets, one number each. Cy has no pets. Al has more pets than Bea. Di has more pets than Al. How many pets does Bea have?', '["0", "2", "1", "3"]', 2, 'Cy has 0. For the others, Di > Al > Bea using 1, 2 and 3, so Bea has 1.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Pat, Quin and Ray are a teacher, a doctor and a pilot, in some order. Ray is not the doctor. Quin is not the pilot. The teacher is older than Ray, and Pat is the youngest of the three. Who is the pilot?', '["Pat", "Quin", "Ray", "It cannot be told"]', 2, 'Pat is the youngest, so Pat cannot be older than Ray, and Ray cannot be older than himself. So Quin is the teacher. Ray is not the doctor, so Ray is the pilot.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A box holds balls that are big or small and red or blue: 5 big red, 3 big blue, 4 small red and 6 small blue. How many balls are red or big (or both)?', '["8", "9", "18", "12"]', 3, 'Every ball except the small blue ones is red or big. 5 + 3 + 4 = 12.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Every kid who plays violin is also in the orchestra. 5 kids play violin. What is the smallest possible number of kids in the orchestra?', '["0", "5", "1", "10"]', 1, 'All 5 violin players must be in the orchestra, so there are at least 5.'),
(2, 'logic', 'How many numbers from 1 to 40 are multiples of both 4 and 6?', '["3", "2", "4", "6"]', 0, 'Numbers that are multiples of both 4 and 6 are multiples of 12. Up to 40 those are 12, 24 and 36.'),
(2, 'logic', 'How many numbers from 1 to 10 are neither prime nor odd?', '["3", "5", "6", "4"]', 3, 'The even numbers are 2, 4, 6, 8 and 10, but 2 is prime. That leaves 4, 6, 8 and 10.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Today is Wednesday. What day will it be in 3 weeks and 4 days?', '["Saturday", "Monday", "Sunday", "Thursday"]', 2, '3 weeks later is still Wednesday. Then 4 more days is Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A movie starts at 2:45 pm and ends at 4:20 pm. How long is the movie?', '["1 hour 35 minutes", "1 hour 25 minutes", "1 hour 45 minutes", "2 hours 35 minutes"]', 0, '2:45 to 3:45 is 1 hour, and 3:45 to 4:20 is 35 more minutes.'),
(2, 'logic', 'How many minutes are there from 9:48 to 11:05?', '["67", "77", "87", "73"]', 1, '9:48 to 10:00 is 12 minutes, and 10:00 to 11:05 is 65 minutes. 12 + 65 = 77.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a leap year, February has 29 days. What is the date 2 days after February 28?', '["March 2", "February 29", "March 1", "March 3"]', 2, 'One day after February 28 is February 29, and one more day is March 1.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Yesterday was Sunday the 15th. What day and date will it be 10 days from today?', '["Wednesday the 26th", "Thursday the 26th", "Thursday the 25th", "Friday the 27th"]', 1, 'Today is Monday the 16th. Ten days later is the 26th, and 10 days is 1 week plus 3 days, so Monday becomes Thursday.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Kilogram is to weight as liter is to ___.', '["volume", "length", "speed", "temperature"]', 0, 'Kilograms measure weight. Liters measure volume, the amount of space a liquid fills.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Petal is to flower as page is to ___.', '["pen", "story", "library", "book"]', 3, 'A petal is a part of a flower, and a page is a part of a book.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Whisper is to shout as walk is to ___.', '["run", "sit", "crawl", "stop"]', 0, 'A shout is a much stronger version of a whisper. Running is a much faster version of walking.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ten is to number as Tuesday is to ___.', '["week", "month", "day", "clock"]', 2, 'Ten is one example of a number. Tuesday is one example of a day.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a code, ▲ = 1, ■ = 2 and ● = 3. Multiplication is done before addition. What is ▲ + ■ x ●?', '["9", "6", "11", "7"]', 3, 'Multiply first: 2 x 3 = 6. Then add 1 to get 7.'),
(2, 'logic', 'If A=1, B=2, C=3 and so on, which word has letters that add up to 10?', '["ACE", "BAG", "BED", "CAB"]', 1, 'BAG is 2 + 1 + 7 = 10. ACE makes 9, BED makes 11 and CAB makes 6.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a code, each digit is replaced by 9 minus that digit (so 0 becomes 9 and 3 becomes 6). What does 2471 become?', '["7529", "6528", "7258", "7528"]', 3, '9 - 2 = 7, 9 - 4 = 5, 9 - 7 = 2, and 9 - 1 = 8. That gives 7528.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A robot starts facing north. F means step forward 1, and R means turn right. Where is the robot after F, F, R, F?', '["1 step north, 2 steps east", "2 steps north, 1 step east", "3 steps north", "2 steps north, 1 step west"]', 1, 'Two steps forward takes it 2 north. Turning right makes it face east, so the last step is 1 east.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Parcel A weighs 2 kg more than Parcel B, and B weighs 3 kg more than Parcel C. Together the three weigh 23 kg. How much does C weigh?', '["5 kg", "6 kg", "7 kg", "8 kg"]', 0, 'If C is 5 kg, B is 8 kg and A is 10 kg. 5 + 8 + 10 = 23.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A 6 kg bag on the left pan is balanced by 4 identical stones and a 2 kg weight on the right pan. How heavy is one stone?', '["2 kg", "1.5 kg", "1 kg", "4 kg"]', 2, 'The 4 stones must weigh 6 - 2 = 4 kg together. So one stone weighs 1 kg.'),
(2, 'logic', 'On a balance scale, 3 books weigh the same as 2 vases, and 1 vase weighs the same as 3 mugs. How many mugs weigh the same as 1 book?', '["1", "2", "3", "6"]', 1, '2 vases are 6 mugs, so 3 books weigh 6 mugs. One book weighs 2 mugs.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Tara is 5 years older than her brother Ben. Five years ago their ages added up to 17. How old is Ben now?', '["9", "10", "11", "12"]', 2, 'If Ben is 11 now, Tara is 16. Five years ago they were 6 and 11, and 6 + 11 = 17.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Mira''s mother is Nita. Nita''s brother is Omar. Omar''s daughter is Pia. What is Pia to Mira?', '["Her cousin", "Her sister", "Her aunt", "Her niece"]', 0, 'Omar is Mira''s uncle, and his daughter is Mira''s cousin.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Two years ago Ram was 10 years old. In how many years will he turn 20?', '["6", "10", "12", "8"]', 3, 'Ram is 12 now. To reach 20 he needs 20 - 12 = 8 more years.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Three sisters are each 2 years apart in age, and their ages add up to 30. How old is the youngest?', '["8", "6", "9", "10"]', 0, 'The ages are 8, 10 and 12, and they add up to 30.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Five years from now, Ann and her dad''s ages will add up to 70. Dad is 4 times as old as Ann is now. How old is Ann now?', '["10", "11", "14", "12"]', 3, 'If Ann is 12, Dad is 48. In 5 years they will be 17 and 53, and 17 + 53 = 70.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Recycling rules: paper goes in the blue bin and plastic in the green bin, but anything dirty goes in the black bin. Where does a dirty plastic cup go?', '["The blue bin", "The green bin", "The black bin", "Either the blue or green bin"]', 2, 'The dirty rule overrides the material rule, so it goes in the black bin.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ari''s bedtime is 8:30 pm if there is school the next day and 9:30 pm if not. On the night before a holiday it is always 10:00 pm. Tomorrow is a Saturday holiday. What is his bedtime tonight?', '["8:30 pm", "10:00 pm", "9:30 pm", "9:00 pm"]', 1, 'The holiday rule always applies the night before a holiday, whatever else is going on. So it is 10:00 pm.'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a dice game, you win if you roll a 6, or if you roll two even numbers in a row. Mia rolls 3 then 5, Nate rolls 2 then 4, and Ola rolls 1 then 3. Who wins?', '["Mia", "Ola", "Nate", "All three"]', 2, 'Nate rolled two even numbers in a row. Mia and Ola rolled no 6 and did not roll two evens.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A jar holds 21 candies. Ben eats 5. Cara then eats half of what is left. Dev then eats 2. How many candies are left?', '["6", "8", "4", "7"]', 0, '21 - 5 = 16. Cara eats half, 8, leaving 8. Dev eats 2, leaving 6.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Two ducks are in front of a duck, two ducks are behind a duck, and one duck is in the middle. What is the smallest number of ducks that can make this true?', '["2", "4", "5", "3"]', 3, 'Three ducks in a line work. The first has two behind, the last has two in front, and the middle one is in the middle.'),
(2, 'logic', 'How many times does the digit 1 appear when you write all the numbers from 1 to 20?', '["11", "12", "10", "13"]', 1, '1 and 10 use one 1 each, 11 uses two, and 12 to 19 use one each (8 more). 1 + 1 + 2 + 8 = 12.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A hen lays 6 eggs in 3 days. At the same rate, how many eggs do 2 hens lay in 6 days?', '["12", "18", "24", "36"]', 2, 'One hen lays 2 eggs a day. Two hens lay 4 a day, and over 6 days that is 24.'),
(2, 'logic', 'Ken has 12 pencils. He gives half of them to Lia. Lia then gives one third of her pencils back to Ken. How many pencils does Ken have now?', '["6", "8", "4", "10"]', 1, 'Ken keeps 6 and Lia has 6. Lia gives back 2, so Ken has 6 + 2 = 8.'),
(2, 'logic', 'A digital clock shows 12:21, which reads the same backwards (1221). What is the next time after it that reads the same backwards?', '["1:11", "12:22", "2:02", "1:01"]', 3, 'After 12:21 the clock goes on to 1:00, and the first time that reads the same backwards is 1:01 (101).'),
(2, 'logic', 'In a race of 100 runners, Ravi is in 40th place. He passes 5 runners, and then 2 runners pass him. What place is he in now?', '["37th", "33rd", "38th", "43rd"]', 0, 'Passing 5 runners takes him to 35th. Being passed by 2 moves him back to 37th.');
insert into questions (level, category, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanation) values
(2, 'riddle', 'I turn a blunt pencil into a sharp one, leaving little curly shavings. What am I?', '["An eraser", "A pencil sharpener", "A stapler", "A marker"]', 1, 'A pencil sharpener shaves the wood to expose a sharp point.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I sit on your back, and I zip open to hold your books and lunch. What am I?', '["A suitcase", "A basket", "A wallet", "A backpack"]', 3, 'A backpack has two straps that let you carry things on your back.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What five-letter word gets shorter when you add two letters to it?', '["Small", "Tall", "Short", "Brief"]', 2, 'Add ''er'' to ''short'' and you get ''shorter''.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m yellow and shiny, and I keep you dry when you stand out in the pouring rain. What am I?', '["A raincoat", "A sweater", "A scarf", "A swimsuit"]', 0, 'A raincoat is waterproof, so rain slides right off.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have 206 bones, I''m hidden beneath your skin, and I hold your body up. What am I?', '["Your muscles", "Your skin", "Your blood", "Your skeleton"]', 3, 'An adult skeleton has 206 bones that give the body its shape and support.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a reptile that carries a hard shell everywhere, and I bury my eggs on the beach. What am I?', '["A sea turtle", "A snail", "A crab", "A seal"]', 0, 'A sea turtle is a shelled reptile that comes ashore to lay eggs in the sand.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What day is always one day away, but you never quite get there?', '["Yesterday", "Tomorrow", "Sunday", "Today"]', 1, 'When tomorrow arrives it becomes today, so it''s always a day ahead.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What word has a whole mile between its first and last letters?', '["Simple", "Smile", "Smiles", "Miles"]', 2, 'In ''smiles'', the word ''mile'' sits between the first S and the last S.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Sand dunes, blazing sun, hardly any rain, and camels crossing me. What am I?', '["A rainforest", "A glacier", "A meadow", "A desert"]', 3, 'A desert is a very dry place, often hot and sandy, where little rain falls.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I rise in the oven thanks to tiny yeast, and I''m sliced up for sandwiches. What am I?', '["A pancake", "An omelet", "A loaf of bread", "A salad"]', 2, 'Yeast makes bread dough puff up, and a baked loaf is sliced for sandwiches.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'A basket hangs below me, and a burning flame heats the air inside my colorful bag to lift us off the ground. What am I?', '["A parachute", "A hot-air balloon", "An airplane", "A helicopter"]', 1, 'Hot air is lighter than cooler air, so it lifts the balloon and its basket.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a book that shows the whole world on my pages, full of maps of every country. What am I?', '["An atlas", "A diary", "A novel", "A cookbook"]', 0, 'An atlas is a book of maps.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a huge bright flash in a storm, hotter than the surface of the sun, and I always come before the thunder you hear. What am I?', '["A rainbow", "A meteor", "Lightning", "A sunbeam"]', 2, 'Lightning is a giant electric spark in a storm; light travels faster than sound, so you see it first.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m shiny, shaped like a cup, and given to the winner. What am I?', '["A trophy", "A medal", "A ribbon", "A ticket"]', 0, 'A trophy is a cup-like prize for the winner.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a white stick that squeaks on a board and leaves dust on your fingers. What am I?', '["A crayon", "Chalk", "A pen", "An eraser"]', 1, 'Chalk is a soft white stick that leaves dust on the board.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the shortest month of the year, usually with just 28 days. What am I?', '["January", "March", "April", "February"]', 3, 'February has 28 days, or 29 in a leap year.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a pink bird who often stands on one leg in shallow water. What am I?', '["A flamingo", "A heron", "A pelican", "A parrot"]', 0, 'Flamingos are pink from the food they eat, and they often rest standing on one leg.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Players bounce a ball and shoot it up through a hoop with a net. What am I?', '["Golf", "Basketball", "Swimming", "Bowling"]', 1, 'Basketball is a team game where you score by shooting the ball through the hoop.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a big hollow inside a hillside where bats sleep, and if you shout, your voice bounces back at you. What am I?', '["A nest", "A pond", "A cave", "A cliff"]', 2, 'A cave is a large hollow space in rock or a hill, and bats often roost inside.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I beat all day and all night, right in the middle of your chest, and I never take a break. What am I?', '["Your lungs", "Your brain", "Your stomach", "Your heart"]', 3, 'Your heart pumps blood around your body without stopping.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have six strings and a hollow wooden body, and you strum me around the campfire. What am I?', '["A drum", "A flute", "A guitar", "A trumpet"]', 2, 'A guitar has six strings that you strum or pluck.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I travel through the air in waves, I''m slower than light, and I make your eardrums wiggle so that you hear. What am I?', '["Light", "Sound", "Heat", "Color"]', 1, 'Sound is made of vibrations moving through air that make your eardrums wiggle.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What time of day is spelled the same way forwards and backwards?', '["Night", "Dusk", "Dawn", "Noon"]', 3, 'Noon reads the same both ways.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'There are seven of us, and Asia is the biggest of the bunch. What are we?', '["Continents", "Oceans", "Islands", "Countries"]', 0, 'The seven continents are giant land masses; Asia is the largest.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I gurgle and rumble when you''re hungry, and I mash up the dinner you swallow. What am I?', '["Your knee", "Your elbow", "Your stomach", "Your ear"]', 2, 'Your stomach churns food and can growl when it''s empty.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a wide, open field of soft grass and wildflowers, with no trees, where cows might graze. What am I?', '["A meadow", "A jungle", "A swamp", "A desert"]', 0, 'A meadow is an open grassy field, often full of flowers.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have huge back wheels and I pull a plow across the farmer''s field. What am I?', '["A taxi", "A tractor", "A train", "A bus"]', 1, 'A tractor is a strong farm machine with big wheels that pulls tools like plows.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I run all day over pebbles and rocks, singing a bubbly song, but I have no legs. I''m small and shallow. What am I?', '["A pond", "A well", "A puddle", "A stream"]', 3, 'A stream is a small flowing body of water that babbles over stones as it runs.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I store water in my thick green body, and I''m covered in prickly spines. What am I?', '["A fern", "A cactus", "A daisy", "A pine tree"]', 1, 'A cactus stores water in its stem, which helps it live in a dry desert.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I sit in the kitchen with a hot ring on top, and pots and pans sit on me while dinner cooks. What am I?', '["A stove", "A sink", "A fridge", "A table"]', 0, 'A stove has burners on top that heat pots and pans.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a bendy joint in the middle of your leg, and I get scraped when you fall off your bike. What am I?', '["Your elbow", "Your shoulder", "Your knee", "Your wrist"]', 2, 'The knee is the joint halfway down your leg that bends when you walk.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I streak across the night sky for just a second, a space rock burning up as it rushes through the air. What am I?', '["A planet", "A firefly", "A rainbow", "A meteor"]', 3, 'A meteor is a space rock that glows as it burns up in the air; many people call it a shooting star.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a stick with a tuft of hair at one end, and you dip me into paint. What am I?', '["A paintbrush", "A pencil", "A marker", "A ruler"]', 0, 'A paintbrush has bristles that hold paint.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Though it never rained, tiny drops of water are sitting on the grass early this morning. What are they?', '["Hail", "Snow", "Fog", "Dew"]', 3, 'Dew forms when water vapor in the cool night air turns into little drops on grass and leaves.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Scientists peek into me to see tiny living things that are far too small for your eyes. What am I?', '["A telescope", "A microscope", "A ruler", "A camera"]', 1, 'A microscope makes very tiny things look big enough to see.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Red trucks wait inside me with their hoses, ready to zoom off when the alarm rings. What am I?', '["A bus station", "A bakery", "A fire station", "A school"]', 2, 'A fire station is where firefighters and their trucks wait for emergency calls.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a plant that lives in the ocean, waving with the waves. What am I?', '["A cactus", "Seaweed", "A daisy", "A fern"]', 1, 'Seaweed grows in the sea.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a tall wooden box with doors, and inside me your clothes hang in rows. What am I?', '["A wardrobe", "A suitcase", "A drawer", "A fridge"]', 0, 'A wardrobe is a tall cupboard with doors for hanging up clothes.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m made up of one hundred years, and I''m longer than a decade. What am I?', '["A month", "A season", "A decade", "A century"]', 3, 'A century lasts 100 years, and a decade only lasts ten.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a yellow flower that turns into a fluffy white ball you can blow away. What am I?', '["A sunflower", "A daisy", "A dandelion", "A rose"]', 2, 'A dandelion''s seeds are little parachutes that blow away in the wind.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m curved like your shoulders, and I hold up your shirts and dresses inside the closet. What am I?', '["A hook", "A shelf", "A drawer", "A coat hanger"]', 3, 'A coat hanger is shaped like shoulders so clothes keep their shape.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the line that separates one country from another. What am I?', '["A coastline", "A capital", "A border", "A harbor"]', 2, 'A border marks where one country ends and another begins.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Astronomers look through me to see faraway planets and stars. What am I?', '["A telescope", "A microscope", "A stethoscope", "A ruler"]', 0, 'A telescope gathers light from far away so distant objects look closer.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I cost nothing, yet I''m worth a lot, and I warm up both the person who gives me and the one who gets me. What am I?', '["A ticket", "Kindness", "A prize", "A coin"]', 1, 'Kindness is being nice to others, and it costs no money.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'For a minute the ground under your feet shakes and rumbles, and nobody is doing it. What is it?', '["A tornado", "A blizzard", "An earthquake", "A rainstorm"]', 2, 'An earthquake happens when big pieces of the Earth''s crust move and make the ground shake.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have exactly sixty seconds, no more, no less. What am I?', '["A minute", "An hour", "A day", "A week"]', 0, 'One minute is made of 60 seconds.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have a long arm and a hook at the end, and I lift heavy beams on a building site. What am I?', '["A bulldozer", "A crane", "A dump truck", "A tractor"]', 1, 'A crane lifts and moves heavy loads high in the air with its arm and hook.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a mammal with wings, I hang upside down to sleep, and I go out at night. What am I?', '["A sparrow", "A butterfly", "An owl", "A bat"]', 3, 'A bat is a furry mammal that can fly, and it sleeps hanging upside down.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m catching, but I''m not a sickness. I bubble out when something is funny. What am I?', '["A cough", "A sneeze", "Laughter", "A hiccup"]', 2, 'Laughter is a happy sound that often spreads from person to person.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What kind of key can open a banana?', '["A piano key", "A monkey", "A door key", "A turkey"]', 1, 'A monkey is a funny answer, because monkeys peel bananas.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a rope that you jump over as it swings under your feet. What am I?', '["A hula hoop", "A leash", "A ladder", "A jump rope"]', 3, 'A jump rope is swung over your head and under your feet while you skip over it.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I stretch over a river so that people can cross without getting their feet wet. What am I?', '["A bridge", "A tunnel", "A dam", "A harbor"]', 0, 'A bridge is built above water or a road so you can cross over it.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'We''re tiny bumps that pop up on your arms when you''re cold or get a fright. What are we?', '["Goosebumps", "Freckles", "Wrinkles", "Dimples"]', 0, 'Goosebumps appear when little muscles at the base of your hairs tighten.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a soft, colorful part of a flower, and I drop off when the flower fades. What am I?', '["A root", "A thorn", "A petal", "A trunk"]', 2, 'Petals are the bright parts around the middle of a flower.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I roar as I gobble up crumbs and dirt from the carpet, and I have a hose and a plug. What am I?', '["A hair dryer", "A vacuum cleaner", "A fan", "A blender"]', 1, 'A vacuum cleaner sucks up dust and dirt from floors.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Nobody in the whole world has one just like mine, and I leave a swirly mark on a glass. What am I?', '["Your height", "Your hair color", "Your shoe size", "Your fingerprint"]', 3, 'Everyone''s fingerprint has a different swirl pattern.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Which letter of the alphabet sounds just like a hot drink you might sip with a biscuit?', '["The letter T", "The letter B", "The letter C", "The letter P"]', 0, 'The letter T sounds like ''tea'', while B sounds like ''bee'', C like ''sea'' and P like ''pea''.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a building full of old things and art for everyone to look at, but the rule is ''do not touch''. What am I?', '["A zoo", "A museum", "A stadium", "A bank"]', 1, 'A museum keeps and shows art and historical items so people can learn from them.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'A river carved me over millions of years, and I''m a deep valley with steep rocky walls. What am I?', '["A hill", "A dune", "A canyon", "An island"]', 2, 'A canyon is a deep, narrow valley with steep sides, often cut by a river.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have a handle and a spout, and I pour out a warm drink for the whole family. What am I?', '["A frying pan", "A spoon", "A bucket", "A teapot"]', 3, 'A teapot has a handle to hold it and a spout to pour hot tea.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I sit on your nose and make blurry things sharp and clear. What am I?', '["Glasses", "A necklace", "A headband", "A bracelet"]', 0, 'Glasses have lenses that help people see clearly.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I click when you press my button, and I catch a moment so you can keep it forever. What am I?', '["A television", "A telescope", "A camera", "A mirror"]', 2, 'A camera records a picture of a moment when you press its button.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m soft and squishy, a sculptor shapes me into pots, and then I''m baked hard. What am I?', '["Sand", "Clay", "Glass", "Cotton"]', 1, 'Clay can be molded when wet and turns hard when it''s baked.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the underground part of a plant that drinks up water and holds the plant in the ground. What am I?', '["A leaf", "A petal", "A flower", "A root"]', 3, 'Roots grow under the soil, drawing in water and anchoring the plant.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What has one head, one foot, and four legs?', '["A chair", "A bed", "A dog", "A table"]', 1, 'A bed has a head at the top, a foot at the bottom and four legs.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'You can''t see me or touch me, but I pull every dropped ball back down to the ground. What am I?', '["Wind", "Sound", "Friction", "Gravity"]', 3, 'Gravity is the invisible pull of the Earth that makes things fall down.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m both a country and a continent, and kangaroos and koalas call me home. What am I?', '["Africa", "Canada", "Australia", "India"]', 2, 'Australia is the only place that is a country and a continent at once.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m telling the truth even when it''s hard, and I''m the best policy. What am I?', '["Honesty", "Bragging", "Cheating", "Silliness"]', 0, 'Honesty is telling the truth.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I shine at night and change from a thin curve to a big circle and back again over a month. What am I?', '["The moon", "The sun", "A comet", "A firefly"]', 0, 'The moon looks like it changes shape because we see different amounts of its sunlit side.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a small container where your sandwich and snack stay until noon. What am I?', '["A backpack", "A toolbox", "A jewelry box", "A lunchbox"]', 3, 'A lunchbox holds your lunch.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m waterproof and I go on both feet so I can stomp in puddles. What am I?', '["Sandals", "Slippers", "Rain boots", "Socks"]', 2, 'Rain boots keep your feet dry in water.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m awake all night, I have huge eyes, and I can turn my head almost all the way around while I hoot. What am I?', '["A parrot", "A duck", "A crow", "An owl"]', 3, 'An owl hoots at night and can turn its head very far.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have no doors or windows, yet a golden treasure hides inside my white shell until someone cracks me open for breakfast. What am I?', '["An egg", "A coconut", "A peach", "A pebble"]', 0, 'An egg has a shell with a yellow yolk inside, and people often eat it at breakfast.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I lay eggs, but I have fur and a flat bill like a duck. What am I?', '["A duck", "A platypus", "A beaver", "A hen"]', 1, 'A platypus is an unusual mammal from Australia that lays eggs.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have swings, slides and seesaws, and I''m outdoors, where children run and play. What am I?', '["A garage", "A parking lot", "A playground", "A kitchen"]', 2, 'A playground is an outdoor area with equipment made for children to play on.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Rub a balloon on your hair and I make your hair stand up and stick to the wall. What am I?', '["Gravity", "Static", "Steam", "Rust"]', 1, 'Static electricity builds up when things rub together and makes light objects cling.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the biggest animal that lives on land, and I use my long trunk like a hand. What am I?', '["A rhinoceros", "A hippopotamus", "A giraffe", "An elephant"]', 3, 'An elephant is the largest land animal and uses its trunk to grab and drink.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I sail under the waves and peek out at the surface through a periscope. What am I?', '["A submarine", "A sailboat", "A ferry", "A raft"]', 0, 'A submarine is a boat that can travel underwater.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a curve that can turn a frown upside down, and I cost nothing. What am I?', '["A frown", "A wink", "A smile", "A yawn"]', 2, 'A smile is a curve of the mouth that shows happiness.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a small nut with a little cap, squirrels bury me, and I can grow into an oak. What am I?', '["An acorn", "A pinecone", "A peanut", "A walnut"]', 0, 'An acorn is the nut of an oak tree and has a cap on top.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have two rows of tiny teeth that lock together when you pull my little tab upward. What am I?', '["A button", "A buckle", "A shoelace", "A zipper"]', 3, 'A zipper''s little teeth interlock as the slider moves, closing a coat or bag.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the feeling that makes you ask ''why?'' about everything you see. What am I?', '["Boredom", "Curiosity", "Sleepiness", "Anger"]', 1, 'Curiosity is the desire to learn and know more.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'An artist puts blobs of paint on me and mixes colors with a brush. What am I?', '["A palette", "A ruler", "An easel", "A frame"]', 0, 'A palette is a board on which an artist mixes paint.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the stone copy of a creature that lived millions of years ago, and diggers find me in rocks. What am I?', '["A seashell", "A crystal", "A fossil", "A brick"]', 2, 'A fossil is the preserved trace of an ancient plant or animal turned to stone.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the season with the shortest days and the longest nights, when you wear coats and scarves. What season am I?', '["Summer", "Winter", "Autumn", "Spring"]', 1, 'Winter has the shortest days and is usually the coldest season.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I sit in the middle of your face, I sniff flowers, and I can run without any legs. What am I?', '["Your chin", "Your knee", "Your eyebrow", "Your nose"]', 3, 'Your nose smells things, and it can ''run'' when you have a cold.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m fifty-two pieces of stiff paper in four suits, and I can be shuffled and dealt. What am I?', '["A deck of cards", "A chess set", "A set of dominoes", "A jigsaw puzzle"]', 0, 'A standard deck has 52 cards in four suits, and you shuffle them before dealing.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I slide out like a tray and hold your socks, but I''m always part of a bigger piece of furniture. What am I?', '["A suitcase", "A drawer", "A basket", "A bucket"]', 1, 'A drawer slides out of a cabinet or dresser so you can store things.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m made of tiny floating water drops. I''m white and puffy on a sunny day, and gray and heavy before it rains. What am I?', '["A snowman", "A pillow", "A cloud", "A feather"]', 2, 'A cloud is made of tiny water droplets, and it looks gray when it''s thick with them.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'We''re hard and white, we grow twice in a lifetime, and we''re great at chewing. What are we?', '["Your fingernails", "Your hair", "Your bones", "Your teeth"]', 3, 'People grow baby teeth first and then adult teeth, and teeth are for biting and chewing.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I bite paper with a tiny metal wire to keep the pages together, then snap shut. What am I?', '["A paper clip", "A pencil", "A stapler", "A glue stick"]', 2, 'A stapler pushes a small metal staple through pages to hold them together.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'My siren wails as I rush sick or hurt people to the hospital. What am I?', '["A fire truck", "A taxi", "A school bus", "An ambulance"]', 3, 'An ambulance carries patients to the hospital, unlike a fire truck, which fights fires.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the moment in the dark when one day ends and the next one begins. What am I?', '["Midnight", "Noon", "Sunrise", "Sunset"]', 0, 'Midnight is twelve o''clock at night, when the date changes.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Thousands of fans sit inside me to cheer on their teams in a big game. What am I?', '["A library", "A stadium", "A cinema", "A hospital"]', 1, 'A stadium is a large sports arena with rows of seats around the field.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the coldest continent, buried in ice, with penguins but no countries of my own. What am I?', '["Australia", "Africa", "Antarctica", "Asia"]', 2, 'Antarctica is icy and freezing, and no country owns it.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I run through wires to light up bulbs and power TVs, and I can give you a zap if you touch a bare wire. What am I?', '["Water", "Electricity", "Wind", "Sound"]', 1, 'Electricity is a flow of energy through wires, and it powers many things around the house.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I buzz from flower to flower, I make sweet golden honey, and I can sting only once. What am I?', '["A wasp", "A fly", "A ladybug", "A honeybee"]', 3, 'Honeybees make honey from nectar, and a bee can sting just once.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I pop into your head like a lightbulb, but I weigh nothing at all. What am I?', '["An idea", "A pebble", "A hat", "A pillow"]', 0, 'An idea is a thought that appears in your mind, with no weight.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What has a tongue but cannot talk?', '["A shoe", "A cup", "A pencil", "A hat"]', 0, 'The flap under a shoe''s laces is called its tongue.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m folded in a pack, and when someone jumps out of a plane and pulls my cord, I open to slow their fall. What am I?', '["A kite", "A rocket", "A trampoline", "A parachute"]', 3, 'A parachute catches air so a skydiver floats gently to the ground.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have one wheel in front and two handles at the back, and I carry heavy dirt around the garden. What am I?', '["A wagon", "A bicycle", "A wheelbarrow", "A scooter"]', 2, 'A wheelbarrow has a single wheel and handles so one person can push loads.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a kitchen machine with slots, and two slices of bread go in and come out golden and crunchy. What am I?', '["A microwave", "A toaster", "A blender", "A kettle"]', 1, 'A toaster heats slices of bread until they turn crisp and brown.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What comes down but never goes up?', '["Smoke", "A balloon", "A bird", "Rain"]', 3, 'Rain always falls down from the clouds; it never rises back up.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'A river rolled me over and over for years until I became small, round and smooth. What am I?', '["A diamond", "A brick", "A pebble", "A marble"]', 2, 'Flowing water tumbles a small stone against other stones until its edges wear smooth, making a pebble.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m land with water on three sides, and one side joined to the mainland. What am I?', '["A peninsula", "An island", "A lake", "A glacier"]', 0, 'A peninsula sticks out into the water but stays attached to the mainland.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Rub your hands together and I warm them up, and I''m also why a sled slows down on flat snow. What am I?', '["Gravity", "Friction", "Magnetism", "Sunlight"]', 1, 'Friction is the rubbing force between two surfaces, and it makes heat and slows things down.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I happen when lots of people work together toward one goal, like ants building a hill. What am I?', '["Teamwork", "A quarrel", "A contest", "A solo"]', 0, 'Teamwork is people helping each other to achieve something together.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the season when leaves turn red and gold and then float down from the trees. What season am I?', '["Spring", "Summer", "Winter", "Autumn"]', 3, 'In autumn the leaves change color and fall, which is why it''s also called fall.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Put me in a balloon and it floats up to the ceiling, and if you breathe me in, your voice gets squeaky. What am I?', '["Oxygen", "Helium", "Water", "Sand"]', 1, 'Helium is a gas lighter than air, so balloons filled with it float and voices sound squeaky.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m made in your throat, no one else has one exactly like mine, and you use me to speak and sing. What am I?', '["Your shadow", "Your footprint", "Your voice", "Your fingernail"]', 2, 'Your voice comes from your throat and sounds different for everyone.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I blast off with fire and smoke and carry astronauts beyond the sky. What am I?', '["An airplane", "A rocket", "A helicopter", "A kite"]', 1, 'A rocket burns fuel to push itself fast enough to reach space.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a large pool of calm water with land all around me, a good place for rowing a boat. What am I?', '["An island", "A river", "A lake", "A peninsula"]', 2, 'A lake is a large body of water surrounded by land.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'In the middle of the day the moon slides in front of the sun and the sky goes dim for a few minutes. What is this?', '["A sunset", "A rainstorm", "A rainbow", "An eclipse"]', 3, 'A solar eclipse happens when the moon blocks the sun''s light for a little while.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I begin as a crawling caterpillar, sleep inside a chrysalis, and come out with colorful wings. What am I?', '["A butterfly", "A ladybug", "A bee", "A dragonfly"]', 0, 'A butterfly changes from caterpillar to chrysalis to winged adult.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a flower with thorns on my stem and a lovely smell. What am I?', '["A tulip", "A rose", "A daisy", "A sunflower"]', 1, 'A rose has thorns on its stem and a sweet scent.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I sound like hundreds of hands meeting, and I tell a performer they did a great job. What am I?', '["A whisper", "A roar", "Applause", "A lullaby"]', 2, 'Applause is the sound of clapping that shows people enjoyed a performance.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I stretch your mouth open wide when you''re sleepy, and somebody else''s can start mine. What am I?', '["A sneeze", "A hiccup", "A burp", "A yawn"]', 3, 'People yawn when they feel tired, and yawning is famously catching.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'You can''t see me, but you can see me push the trees and blow a sailboat across the water. What am I?', '["Wind", "Fog", "A wave", "Smoke"]', 0, 'Wind is moving air, which you cannot see, but you see what it pushes.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a glass house that keeps plants warm even on cold winter days. What am I?', '["A barn", "A tent", "A garage", "A greenhouse"]', 3, 'A greenhouse traps the sun''s heat so plants stay warm.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a huge body of salty water with waves and tides, and I touch every continent. What am I?', '["An ocean", "A lake", "A pond", "A fountain"]', 0, 'An ocean is enormous and salty, with waves and tides, and it stretches between the continents.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I grow where nobody planted me, and gardeners keep pulling me out. What am I?', '["A tulip", "A carrot", "A weed", "A sunflower"]', 2, 'A weed is a plant that grows where it isn''t wanted.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I am a long, bendy tube that carries water to your garden, and I can spray it on the flowers. What am I?', '["A ladder", "A garden hose", "A rope", "A scarf"]', 1, 'A garden hose is a long bendy tube that carries water and sprays it onto plants.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the very top of the world, where every direction you look is south. What am I?', '["The South Pole", "The equator", "Mount Everest", "The North Pole"]', 3, 'At the North Pole the only direction you can go is south.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the world''s biggest rainforest, in South America, and jaguars and toucans live in me. What am I?', '["The Amazon rainforest", "The Sahara", "Mount Everest", "The Arctic"]', 0, 'The Amazon rainforest covers a huge part of South America and is full of wildlife.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I live inside your mouth, I help you taste and speak, and I''m always wet. What am I?', '["Your teeth", "Your lips", "Your tongue", "Your nose"]', 2, 'Your tongue has taste buds and helps you talk and swallow.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I rise in the east and set in the west, and my warmth on your skin tells you it''s daytime. What am I?', '["The moon", "The sun", "A star", "A cloud"]', 1, 'The sun gives us both light and heat during the day.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I hold your past inside your head, and I can grow faint as time goes by. What am I?', '["A wish", "A memory", "A plan", "A guess"]', 1, 'A memory is something you remember about the past, and older memories can fade.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m made of hope, and people say me before blowing out their birthday candles. What am I?', '["A wish", "A memory", "A rule", "A fact"]', 0, 'A wish is something you hope for, often said before blowing out candles.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'We''re tiny living things too small to see, and washing your hands with soap sweeps many of us away. What are we?', '["Dust", "Ants", "Crumbs", "Germs"]', 3, 'Germs are microscopic living things, and soap and water wash lots of them off your hands.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What has a thumb and four fingers but isn''t alive?', '["A sock", "A hat", "A glove", "A shoe"]', 2, 'A glove has a thumb and four finger holes.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m wrinkly, I live inside your skull, and I control everything you think and do. What am I?', '["Your heart", "Your brain", "Your stomach", "Your knee"]', 1, 'The brain sits in the skull and is the control center of your body.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m an imaginary line around the middle of the Earth, halfway between the North and South Poles. What am I?', '["The North Pole", "The horizon", "The equator", "A time zone"]', 2, 'The equator circles the Earth at its widest point, halfway between the poles.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m what you show when you wait quietly for your turn without grumbling. What am I?', '["Courage", "Curiosity", "Excitement", "Patience"]', 3, 'Patience is staying calm while you wait.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I loop around your waist and keep your trousers up. What am I?', '["A belt", "A scarf", "A tie", "A hat"]', 0, 'A belt goes around the waist.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I stand at the crossing and shine red, yellow and green so drivers know when to stop and go. What am I?', '["A traffic light", "A rainbow", "A lighthouse", "A street lamp"]', 0, 'A traffic light uses red, yellow and green signals to control traffic.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Billions of tiny grains make me up, and you can build castles from me at the beach. What am I?', '["Salt", "Sand", "Sugar", "Flour"]', 1, 'Sand is made of tiny pieces of rock and shell, and damp sand is great for building castles.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I run on rails, an engine pulls me, and my cars are linked in a long line. What am I?', '["A bus", "A ship", "A truck", "A train"]', 3, 'A train runs along railway tracks with its cars coupled together.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m an invisible gas in the air, and every person and animal needs to breathe me in to stay alive. What am I?', '["Helium", "Steam", "Oxygen", "Smoke"]', 2, 'Oxygen is the part of air that our bodies use to make energy.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I stand in the corner of a room and shine as soon as you flip my switch. What am I?', '["A clock", "A table", "A lamp", "A vase"]', 2, 'A lamp has a bulb that lights up when you turn it on.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have a spout and a handle, and I whistle when the water inside me boils. What am I?', '["A teacup", "A bucket", "A frying pan", "A kettle"]', 3, 'A kettle heats water, and many of them whistle when the steam escapes.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a brown lump with eyes but I can''t see, and I can be turned into fries or chips. What am I?', '["A carrot", "A potato", "A tomato", "A mushroom"]', 1, 'A potato has small dents called eyes, and it can be cooked as fries or chips.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have bristles, and I stand in the corner until someone uses me to sweep dust off the floor. What am I?', '["A mop", "A shovel", "A broom", "A spoon"]', 2, 'A broom has stiff bristles for sweeping; a mop is soft and wet, so it has no bristles.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a box with a door and a light inside, and I warm up leftovers in a minute or two. What am I?', '["A microwave", "A bookcase", "A washing machine", "A fridge"]', 0, 'A microwave heats food very quickly with microwaves.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m flat and green, and I use sunshine to make food for the tree. What am I?', '["A root", "A branch", "A seed", "A leaf"]', 3, 'Leaves use sunlight to make food for the plant.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I rise in a white cloud from the spout of a kettle when the water boils. What am I?', '["Ice", "Frost", "Steam", "Dew"]', 2, 'Steam is water heated so much that it turns into a gas and floats up.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have a huge pouch under my beak that I use to scoop up fish. What am I?', '["A pelican", "A flamingo", "An owl", "A swan"]', 0, 'A pelican''s stretchy beak pouch works like a fishing net.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a river that tumbles over the edge of a cliff and crashes into a pool below, with a thundering splash. What am I?', '["A fountain", "A lake", "A well", "A waterfall"]', 3, 'A waterfall is water falling from a high place over a cliff or ledge.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m baked in the oven, covered in frosting, and I wear candles on my head while everybody sings. What am I?', '["A pie", "A birthday cake", "A pizza", "A salad"]', 1, 'A birthday cake gets candles on top for the birthday song.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What starts with P, ends with E, and holds thousands of letters?', '["A pencil", "A postcard", "A parcel", "A post office"]', 3, 'A post office starts with P, ends with E, and handles thousands of letters.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m tiny white grains that grow in flooded fields, and I turn soft and fluffy when cooked in water. What am I?', '["Salt", "Sugar", "Rice", "Flour"]', 2, 'Rice grows in wet paddies and is boiled until it is soft.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I can walk across a hot desert for days, carrying one or two humps on my back. What am I?', '["A camel", "A horse", "An elephant", "A kangaroo"]', 0, 'A camel''s humps store fat, which gives it energy on long desert walks.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'You roll a heavy ball down a lane to knock down ten pins. What sport is it?', '["Golf", "Bowling", "Archery", "Skiing"]', 1, 'In bowling you roll a ball toward ten pins and try to knock them down.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a hollow giant grass that grows super fast, and pandas munch on me. What am I?', '["An oak", "A pine", "Bamboo", "A fern"]', 2, 'Bamboo grows very fast and is a favorite panda food.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m long and thin, I get slurped up with red sauce, and I swirl around your fork. What am I?', '["Rice", "Spaghetti", "A sandwich", "Soup"]', 1, 'Spaghetti is a long noodle that you twirl on a fork.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I start life as a tadpole with a tail and end up as a green jumper who croaks. What am I?', '["A frog", "A lizard", "A snake", "A goldfish"]', 0, 'A tadpole grows legs, loses its tail, and turns into a frog.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the biggest hot desert in the world, and I stretch across northern Africa. What am I?', '["The Amazon", "The Nile", "Mount Everest", "The Sahara"]', 3, 'The Sahara is a huge, hot desert in Africa.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I fall from winter clouds, and no two of me look exactly alike. Catch me on your tongue and I melt away. What am I?', '["A raindrop", "A snowflake", "A dewdrop", "A sunbeam"]', 1, 'Every snowflake has its own pattern, and it melts into water on your warm tongue.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I hum in the kitchen and keep your milk cold, and you should shut my door quickly. What am I?', '["A refrigerator", "An oven", "A toaster", "A bookshelf"]', 0, 'A refrigerator keeps food cold, and closing the door keeps the cold inside.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m an odd number. Take away one letter and I become even. What number am I?', '["Five", "Nine", "Seven", "Three"]', 2, 'Take away the S from ''seven'' and you get ''even''.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a small round disc that slips through a hole to keep your shirt closed. What am I?', '["A zipper", "A pin", "A coin", "A button"]', 3, 'A button pushes through a buttonhole to hold clothes together.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the season with the longest days, when you swim, and school is out for the holidays. What season am I?', '["Winter", "Autumn", "Summer", "Spring"]', 2, 'Summer has the longest days and the warmest weather.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Boats tie up in me, safe from the big ocean waves. What am I?', '["A garage", "A harbor", "An airport", "A stadium"]', 1, 'A harbor is a sheltered place by the coast where boats and ships stay.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a long silver tube, and you blow across a hole and press little keys to change the notes. What am I?', '["A drum", "A piano", "A violin", "A flute"]', 3, 'A flute makes music when you blow across its mouthpiece and cover holes with keys.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I jump out of your throat with a funny sound, and I might go away if you hold your breath. What am I?', '["A hiccup", "A sneeze", "A yawn", "A cough"]', 0, 'A hiccup is a sudden little squeak that comes from a jump in your breathing muscle.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the biggest and deepest ocean on Earth, and my name means ''peaceful''. What am I?', '["The Pacific Ocean", "The Atlantic Ocean", "The Indian Ocean", "The Arctic Ocean"]', 0, 'The Pacific is the largest and deepest of the world''s oceans.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Two people share me when they trust each other, laugh together, and help each other in tough times. What am I?', '["A rivalry", "A quarrel", "Friendship", "A contest"]', 2, 'Friendship is the bond between people who care about each other.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I come in pairs, I cover your feet, and one of me always goes missing in the wash. What am I?', '["A glove", "A sock", "A hat", "A belt"]', 1, 'Socks cover your feet, and one of a pair often gets lost.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a bird that cannot fly, but I zoom through freezing seas like a fish in my black-and-white suit. What am I?', '["An ostrich", "A seagull", "A duck", "A penguin"]', 3, 'A penguin uses its wings like flippers to swim fast, and it cannot fly.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'My big blades turn in the breeze, grinding grain inside my tall tower. What am I?', '["A helicopter", "A ceiling fan", "A tractor", "A windmill"]', 3, 'A windmill uses wind to turn its blades, and the turning powers a mill that grinds grain.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have springs beneath a stretchy mat, and I make you bounce sky-high. What am I?', '["A hammock", "A swing", "A trampoline", "A sandbox"]', 2, 'A trampoline''s springs push the mat and bouncer upward.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'You sit in me and paddle, since I have no engine and no sails. I''m a long, narrow boat. What am I?', '["A canoe", "A ferry", "A sailboat", "A submarine"]', 0, 'A canoe is a light, narrow boat moved with a paddle.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have a flat blade on a handle, and I dig holes in the garden. What am I?', '["A rake", "A shovel", "A hose", "A ladder"]', 1, 'A shovel is used to dig.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have two wheels and pedals, and I only stay upright while you keep moving. What am I?', '["A tricycle", "A wagon", "A skateboard", "A bicycle"]', 3, 'A bicycle has two wheels and pedals; a tricycle has three wheels, so it stays up by itself.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What can you give away and still keep?', '["Your word", "Your lunch", "Your pencil", "Your sweater"]', 0, 'When you give your word, you make a promise, but you still have it.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I glow when electricity passes through my thin wire, and I hang from the ceiling in a lamp. What am I?', '["A candle", "A light bulb", "A match", "A mirror"]', 1, 'A light bulb lights up when electricity heats its tiny wire, or filament.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Two children sit at either end, and when one goes up, the other goes down. What am I?', '["A swing", "A slide", "A seesaw", "A merry-go-round"]', 2, 'A seesaw balances on the middle, so one side goes up as the other side goes down.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I count seconds while you race, and you press my button to start and stop me. What am I?', '["A stopwatch", "A thermometer", "A compass", "A ruler"]', 0, 'A stopwatch measures how much time passes between when you start and stop it.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Twice a day I pull the sea up the beach, and then I pull it back down again. What am I?', '["A wave", "A whale", "The tide", "A raft"]', 2, 'The tide is the slow rise and fall of the sea, and it happens about twice a day.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m on neither team, I carry a whistle, and I make sure everyone follows the rules. What am I?', '["A goalkeeper", "A fan", "A captain", "A referee"]', 3, 'A referee is a neutral official who enforces the rules of a game.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m shiny brass with three valves, and you buzz your lips into my mouthpiece. What am I?', '["A flute", "A trumpet", "A guitar", "A harp"]', 1, 'A trumpet is a brass instrument played by buzzing your lips and pressing valves.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have an extra day in February, and I come around once every four years. What am I?', '["A weekend", "A new year", "A century", "A leap year"]', 3, 'A leap year has 366 days, with February 29th added.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Knights lived behind my thick stone walls, and I often had a moat and a drawbridge. What am I?', '["A barn", "A hospital", "A castle", "A garage"]', 2, 'A castle is a large fortified building with strong walls, towers and often a moat.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I am a bed made of cloth or rope, hung between two trees so I can swing gently. What am I?', '["A hammock", "A tent", "A sled", "A sofa"]', 0, 'A hammock is a hanging bed tied between two trees or posts that sways gently.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I turn a shiny iron nail orange-brown when it stays wet for a long time. What am I?', '["Rust", "Frost", "Dust", "Soap"]', 0, 'Rust forms when iron reacts with water and air.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'We''re a big group of people who stand together and sing, with no instruments needed. What are we?', '["An orchestra", "A choir", "A circus", "A class"]', 1, 'A choir is a group of singers.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I sprinkle drops through a spout with tiny holes to water the plants. What am I?', '["A watering can", "A teapot", "A bucket", "A spade"]', 0, 'A watering can lets water fall gently over plants.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'The wind fills my big cloth sheets, and I glide across the water with no engine. What am I?', '["A canoe", "A submarine", "A sailboat", "A tractor"]', 2, 'A sailboat catches the wind with its sails to move.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I hang in front of a window, and when you slide me shut the room turns dark and private. What am I?', '["A door", "A rug", "A picture", "A curtain"]', 3, 'A curtain is a piece of cloth that can cover a window to block light and views.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have a red barn, tractors, and rows of crops, and I make the food that ends up in shops. What am I?', '["A factory", "A zoo", "A farm", "A castle"]', 2, 'A farm is land where crops and animals are raised for food.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a machine made of metal and wires that can be programmed to do jobs, sometimes moving like a person. What am I?', '["A statue", "A puppet", "A calculator", "A robot"]', 3, 'A robot is a machine controlled by a computer that can do tasks.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I change my skin color to match leaves, and my long tongue shoots out to catch flies. What am I?', '["A chameleon", "A frog", "A turtle", "A snake"]', 0, 'A chameleon can change color and has a very fast, sticky tongue.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I smell of warm bread and cakes, and my workers get up before sunrise. What am I?', '["A pharmacy", "A bakery", "A bank", "A gas station"]', 1, 'A bakery is a shop where bread, rolls and cakes are baked and sold.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What can you make that no one can see or touch?', '["Noise", "A sandcastle", "A sandwich", "A paper plane"]', 0, 'Noise can be heard, but you can''t see it or hold it.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a slow river of ice that creeps down a mountain so gradually that you can''t see me move. What am I?', '["A waterfall", "An icicle", "A glacier", "A geyser"]', 2, 'A glacier is a huge sheet of ice that flows very slowly downhill.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m red and I travel through tubes all around your body, carrying oxygen to every part. What am I?', '["Your sweat", "Your tears", "Your saliva", "Your blood"]', 3, 'Blood is pumped by the heart and carries oxygen everywhere.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What is black when it''s clean and white when it''s dirty?', '["A pencil", "A blackboard", "A shoe", "A pillow"]', 1, 'A clean blackboard is black and gets covered in white chalk dust.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m made of tiny white crystals, I''m found in seawater, and you shake me onto your chips. What am I?', '["Salt", "Sugar", "Flour", "Pepper"]', 0, 'Salt is found in seawater and is sprinkled on food to add flavor.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What is at the end of every day?', '["The letter D", "The letter A", "The letter Y", "The letter N"]', 2, 'The word ''day'' ends with Y.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a running race over forty-two kilometers, so long that it takes hours. What am I?', '["A sprint", "A hurdle race", "A relay", "A marathon"]', 3, 'A marathon is 42 kilometers long, much longer than a sprint.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I grow on a tall stalk, wearing a green husk that wraps rows of yellow kernels. What am I?', '["Wheat", "Corn", "A pea pod", "A pineapple"]', 1, 'Corn is a plant whose kernels grow in rows on a cob wrapped in green leaves called husks.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I fill up with warm water and bubbles, and you climb in to get clean and play with toy boats. What am I?', '["A sink", "A bucket", "A bathtub", "A teapot"]', 2, 'A bathtub is a big tub in the bathroom that you sit or lie in to wash.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a house made of cloth stretched over poles, and campers sleep inside me. What am I?', '["A tent", "A garage", "A barn", "A lighthouse"]', 0, 'A tent is a portable cloth shelter that campers set up outdoors.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m two slices of bread with a filling in the middle, and I get packed for lunch. What am I?', '["A pancake", "A sandwich", "A salad", "A soup"]', 1, 'A sandwich has a filling between two slices of bread.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have lined pages, and you write your lessons down in me. What am I?', '["A comic book", "A newspaper", "A poster", "A notebook"]', 3, 'A notebook has blank lined pages for writing.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a row of colorful bars, and you hit me with two little mallets. What am I?', '["A xylophone", "A piano", "A harp", "A trumpet"]', 0, 'A xylophone''s bars ring out when you strike them with mallets.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a spinning funnel of wind that dangles from a storm cloud and can twirl across a field. What am I?', '["A rainbow", "A drizzle", "A sunrise", "A tornado"]', 3, 'A tornado is a fast-spinning column of air that reaches down from a storm cloud.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a staircase that moves all by myself, carrying you up to the next floor while you stand still. What am I?', '["An elevator", "A ladder", "An escalator", "A slide"]', 2, 'An escalator''s steps move on a belt, so you ride up without climbing.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Planes take off and land at me, and travelers wait inside with their suitcases. What am I?', '["A train station", "An airport", "A harbor", "A bus stop"]', 1, 'An airport has runways for planes and terminals for passengers.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a piece of cloth in a country''s colors, and I wave from a tall pole. What am I?', '["A flag", "A tablecloth", "A sail", "A bedsheet"]', 0, 'A flag stands for a country and flies from a flagpole.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'A doctor puts me on your chest to listen to your heartbeat and your breathing. What am I?', '["A thermometer", "A stethoscope", "A bandage", "A stopwatch"]', 1, 'A stethoscope lets a doctor listen to the sounds of your heart and lungs.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I am a big red vehicle with a ladder and a hose, and I rush to put out fires. What am I?', '["A school bus", "A fire truck", "A tractor", "A taxi"]', 1, 'A fire truck carries ladders and hoses so firefighters can put out fires.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the tallest mountain on Earth, and climbers dream of reaching my top. What am I?', '["Mount Fuji", "Kilimanjaro", "Mount Everest", "The Alps"]', 2, 'Mount Everest, in the Himalayas, is the highest mountain in the world.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have many teeth but I never bite, and I help you look neat in the morning. What am I?', '["A saw", "A comb", "A spoon", "A shoe"]', 1, 'A comb has a row of teeth for smoothing hair, and it never bites.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m made from milk, and I can be yellow with holes in me. In stories, mice love me. What am I?', '["Cheese", "Butter", "Yogurt", "Pudding"]', 0, 'Cheese is made from milk, and some kinds, like Swiss, have holes.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have one eye but cannot see, and a long thin body, and I pull thread through cloth. What am I?', '["A pin", "A nail", "A needle", "A pencil"]', 2, 'A sewing needle has a small hole, called an eye, that the thread goes through.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a giant yellow flower whose face follows the sun, and my seeds are a snack. What am I?', '["A sunflower", "A daisy", "A rose", "A tulip"]', 0, 'A sunflower turns to follow the sun and its seeds are edible.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'After a flash lights up the sky, I roar and rumble across it, though I have no mouth. What am I?', '["A rainbow", "A breeze", "A snowflake", "Thunder"]', 3, 'Thunder is the loud rumble that follows a lightning flash.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a small room that goes up and down between floors when you press a button. What am I?', '["An escalator", "An elevator", "A balcony", "A ramp"]', 1, 'An elevator is a little box, or car, that carries people between floors of a building.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Hold me over an ant and it looks huge, because I''m a curved piece of glass. What am I?', '["A mirror", "A magnifying glass", "A window", "A pair of scissors"]', 1, 'A magnifying glass bends light so small things look bigger.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I keep your secrets, I sometimes have a tiny lock, and I never tell anyone what I know. What am I?', '["A dictionary", "A magazine", "A diary", "A newspaper"]', 2, 'A diary is a private book where you write your daily thoughts.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'In winter I hang from the edge of a roof, clear and pointy, and I drip when the sun shines on me. What am I?', '["An icicle", "A snowman", "A raindrop", "A candle"]', 0, 'An icicle forms when dripping water freezes, and it drips again when it warms up.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I grow underground, orange and crunchy, and rabbits love to chew me. What am I?', '["A potato", "A pumpkin", "A tomato", "A carrot"]', 3, 'A carrot is an orange root that grows in the soil.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a soft, slow song that a parent sings to help a baby fall asleep. What am I?', '["A march", "A lullaby", "A cheer", "A shout"]', 1, 'A lullaby is a gentle bedtime song.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I wrap around your neck in winter, and I can be very long. What am I?', '["A belt", "A sock", "A hat", "A scarf"]', 3, 'A scarf keeps your neck warm.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m woody and scaly, and I drop from an evergreen tree, holding its seeds. What am I?', '["An acorn", "A seashell", "A pinecone", "A pebble"]', 2, 'Pinecones are the scaly, woody cones of pine trees.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a mammal of the sea, I breathe air through a hole on top of my head, and I sing songs. What am I?', '["A whale", "A shark", "A tuna", "A jellyfish"]', 0, 'A whale breathes air through its blowhole and some kinds sing long songs.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I spin your wet, muddy clothes round and round with soap until they''re clean. What am I?', '["A dishwasher", "A washing machine", "A blender", "A toaster"]', 1, 'A washing machine tumbles clothes in soapy water to clean them.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I come once a year, I bring cake and candles, and I make you one year older. What am I?', '["A Monday", "A rainstorm", "A haircut", "A birthday"]', 3, 'Your birthday marks the day you were born and happens once a year.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m green outside, red and juicy inside, full of black seeds, and big enough to share on a picnic. What am I?', '["A pumpkin", "A cabbage", "A watermelon", "A tomato"]', 2, 'A watermelon has green skin, red juicy flesh and lots of seeds.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m two days in a row, Saturday and Sunday, when many children don''t go to school. What am I?', '["The weekend", "A month", "A week", "A year"]', 0, 'The weekend is the two days at the end of the week.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a piece of land with water all the way around me. What am I?', '["A valley", "A mountain", "An island", "A canyon"]', 2, 'An island is land completely surrounded by water.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'My blades spin on top of me, and I can hover in the air without moving forward. What am I?', '["An airplane", "A helicopter", "A hot-air balloon", "A kite"]', 1, 'A helicopter''s spinning rotor blades let it hover and even fly backwards.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I can pull a nail across a table without touching it, but a wooden spoon ignores me. What am I?', '["A magnet", "A balloon", "A spring", "A fan"]', 0, 'A magnet attracts iron things like nails, but wood is not attracted at all.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m the start of the day, when the sun first peeks over the horizon. What am I?', '["Sunset", "Midnight", "Noon", "Sunrise"]', 3, 'Sunrise is when the sun appears over the horizon in the morning.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m hollow inside, I make a beat when you hit me with sticks, and a band''s rhythm depends on me. What am I?', '["A violin", "A trumpet", "A flute", "A drum"]', 3, 'A drum makes sound when you strike its stretched skin.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a place where wild animals live and visitors pay to see them. What am I?', '["A farm", "A museum", "A zoo", "A pet shop"]', 2, 'A zoo houses wild animals like lions and monkeys for visitors to watch.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have a long neck to nibble treetop leaves and a coat covered in patches. What am I?', '["A giraffe", "An elephant", "A zebra", "A camel"]', 0, 'A giraffe is the tallest animal and reaches high leaves with its long neck.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I hang from chains, and you sit on me to go back and forth. What am I?', '["A slide", "A swing", "A seesaw", "A ladder"]', 1, 'A swing hangs from a frame and moves you back and forth.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a painting that shows a person''s face. What am I?', '["A landscape", "A statue", "A poster", "A portrait"]', 3, 'A portrait is a picture of a person, while a landscape shows scenery.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I grow in bunches, I''m purple or green, and if you dry me in the sun I become a raisin. What am I?', '["A cherry", "A banana", "A grape", "A plum"]', 2, 'Raisins are simply dried grapes.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I lie outside the front door, and you wipe your muddy feet on me. What am I?', '["A curtain", "A doormat", "A doorknob", "A window"]', 1, 'A doormat is a small rough mat placed at the door so people can wipe their shoes.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m played on a board of 64 squares, and I have a king and a queen. What am I?', '["Chess", "Checkers", "Bingo", "Tag"]', 0, 'Chess has kings, queens and other pieces; checkers has no queens.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I slide down over your eye and up again, all day long, to keep it moist and clean. What am I?', '["Your eyelid", "Your eyebrow", "Your nostril", "Your earlobe"]', 0, 'Your eyelid blinks over the eye to wash it and keep it from drying out.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What is easy to lift, but very hard to throw far?', '["A rock", "A ball", "A brick", "A feather"]', 3, 'A feather weighs so little that air slows it down right away.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Doctors and nurses work inside me, helping sick people get better. What am I?', '["A bakery", "A bank", "A hospital", "A museum"]', 2, 'A hospital is where doctors and nurses care for patients.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m cold and sweet, I come in scoops, and if you leave me in the sun I turn into a puddle. What am I?', '["A cookie", "Ice cream", "A pizza", "A sandwich"]', 1, 'Ice cream is a frozen treat that melts quickly when it gets warm.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I wear black-and-white stripes, and no two of my coats look the same. What am I?', '["A zebra", "A tiger", "A panda", "A cow"]', 0, 'A zebra has a unique stripe pattern, like a fingerprint.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Earth is one of eight of us that circle around the sun. What are we?', '["Stars", "Planets", "Comets", "Moons"]', 1, 'Planets like Earth, Mars and Jupiter orbit the sun; there are eight main ones.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I sit on a roof and catch sunshine to turn into electricity. What am I?', '["A chimney", "A weather vane", "A satellite dish", "A solar panel"]', 3, 'A solar panel changes sunlight into electricity.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Violins, trumpets, drums and flutes all play together under one conductor. What am I?', '["A choir", "A circus", "An orchestra", "A parade"]', 2, 'An orchestra is a large group of musicians led by a conductor.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'We''re a pair of pink balloons in your chest that fill with air every time you breathe. What are we?', '["Your stomach", "Your heart", "Your kidneys", "Your lungs"]', 3, 'Your lungs take in air when you breathe in and let it out again.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m hairy and brown outside with a hard shell, and inside I hold sweet white flesh and watery milk. What am I?', '["A coconut", "A walnut", "A potato", "A kiwi"]', 0, 'A coconut has a hard, hairy shell with white flesh and coconut water inside.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I ring to tell the whole school that class is starting or ending. What am I?', '["A doorbell", "A siren", "A school bell", "A whistle"]', 2, 'A school bell rings at the start and end of lessons.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What can you serve but never eat?', '["A pizza", "A tennis ball", "A soup", "A sandwich"]', 1, 'In tennis you serve the ball to start a point, and you can''t eat it.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m round and flat, with melted cheese and tomato sauce on top, and I''m cut into triangle slices. What am I?', '["A pancake", "A pizza", "A muffin", "A sandwich"]', 1, 'A pizza has a crust topped with tomato sauce and cheese and is usually cut into slices.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have eight arms, no bones, and I squirt inky clouds to escape. What am I?', '["A starfish", "A jellyfish", "A crab", "An octopus"]', 3, 'An octopus has eight arms and squirts ink to hide from danger.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m orange and round, I grow on a vine, and I can be carved into a glowing face or baked into a pie. What am I?', '["A pumpkin", "An orange", "A carrot", "A tomato"]', 0, 'A pumpkin grows on a vine, and people bake it or carve it.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'One player closes their eyes and counts while the others race off to find a secret spot. What game is this?', '["Hopscotch", "Simon says", "Hide-and-seek", "Musical chairs"]', 2, 'In hide-and-seek, one person counts, then tries to find the hiders.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a tall tower by the sea, and my bright light warns ships to stay away from the rocks. What am I?', '["A castle", "A windmill", "A barn", "A lighthouse"]', 3, 'A lighthouse shines a beam out to sea so ships can find their way safely.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a glass triangle that splits a beam of white light into all the colors of the rainbow. What am I?', '["A mirror", "A prism", "A candle", "A flashlight"]', 1, 'A prism bends different colors of light by different amounts, spreading them out.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'You spend about a third of your life in me, and you need me every night to grow and feel rested. What am I?', '["Homework", "Breakfast", "Sleep", "Playtime"]', 2, 'People sleep for about a third of their lives, and it lets the body rest and grow.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m gone, and nobody can visit me, but I''m the day just before today. What am I?', '["Yesterday", "Tomorrow", "Monday", "Next week"]', 0, 'Yesterday is the day before today.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a carved figure made of stone or metal, and I stand in the park without ever moving. What am I?', '["A doll", "A statue", "A puppet", "A mirror"]', 1, 'A statue is a sculpture of a person or animal, usually made from stone or metal.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I turn in a keyhole to lock or unlock a door, and I jingle on a ring with my friends. What am I?', '["A key", "A coin", "A nail", "A button"]', 0, 'A key fits a lock and turns it; people keep keys together on a keyring.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m flat and wide with a long handle, and you cook eggs and flip pancakes in me. What am I?', '["A bucket", "A bowl", "A frying pan", "A teapot"]', 2, 'A frying pan is a flat pan with a handle used for frying food on the stove.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have wings that never flap, and I carry hundreds of people through the clouds. What am I?', '["A bird", "A helicopter", "A rocket", "An airplane"]', 3, 'An airplane has fixed wings that hold it up while engines push it forward.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m soft, I''m stuffed with feathers or foam, and you rest your head on me at night. What am I?', '["A drum", "A rug", "A doorknob", "A pillow"]', 3, 'A pillow is a soft cushion that supports your head when you sleep.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have three legs and hold up a painter''s canvas while the artist works. What am I?', '["An easel", "A music stand", "A ladder", "A coat rack"]', 0, 'An easel is a tall stand that holds a painting up.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m yellow and sour, and one lick of my juice makes you scrunch up your face. What am I?', '["A banana", "A lemon", "A grape", "A mango"]', 1, 'Lemons are yellow and very sour.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have four strings, and you draw a bow across them to make a singing sound. What am I?', '["A drum", "A trumpet", "A violin", "A xylophone"]', 2, 'A violin is played by drawing a bow across its strings.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m what you have when you feel scared but still go ahead and do the right thing. What am I?', '["Laziness", "Courage", "Luck", "Boredom"]', 1, 'Courage means doing something even when you''re afraid.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a little cube with dots on every side, from one to six, and you roll me in board games. What am I?', '["A domino", "A marble", "A die", "A card"]', 2, 'One of a pair of dice is called a die; it has one to six dots.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'What two things can you never eat before breakfast?', '["Lunch and dinner", "Eggs and toast", "Cereal and milk", "Juice and jam"]', 0, 'Lunch and dinner come later in the day, after breakfast.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have two blades joined in the middle, and I snip paper and string. What am I?', '["A knife", "A stapler", "A ruler", "Scissors"]', 3, 'Scissors have two blades that cross and cut things when you squeeze the handles.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'You swing a club and hit a tiny white ball across the grass, trying to drop it into a faraway hole. What am I?', '["Tennis", "Baseball", "Golf", "Hockey"]', 2, 'Golf players use clubs to hit a ball into holes on a course.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I''m a game of chalk squares, where you toss a stone and hop on one foot. What am I?', '["Hopscotch", "Tag", "Leapfrog", "Chess"]', 0, 'Hopscotch is played by hopping through numbered squares drawn on the ground.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I have long teeth on a stick, and I gather fallen leaves into a pile. What am I?', '["A comb", "A shovel", "A hose", "A rake"]', 3, 'A rake pulls leaves together with its tines.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'Every country has one of me, and its leaders work there. What am I?', '["A village", "A capital city", "A border", "A harbor"]', 1, 'A capital is a country''s main city, where its government usually meets.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'I walk sideways along the beach and pinch with two big claws. What am I?', '["A crab", "A starfish", "A shrimp", "A seahorse"]', 0, 'A crab walks sideways and has two pincer claws.'),
(2, 'riddle', 'In me you can''t touch the ball with your hands, unless you''re the goalkeeper. What am I?', '["Basketball", "Baseball", "Soccer", "Volleyball"]', 2, 'In soccer, players kick the ball, and only goalkeepers may use their hands.');
